SPDADD({"b:Osamodas:Incendiary Crow": ["{AP} 3", "{Element Fire} Damage: 3-83\n\nIf the target isn't in line of sight of caster:\n{Element Fire} Damage: 4-111 instead", "This spell can strike through obstacles. It inflicts high damage if the target isn't in the caster's line of sight.", "Fire"], "b:Osamodas:Flaming Whip": ["{AP} 2", "{Element Fire} Damage: 2-65\n{Enemy} Scalded (Lvl 3)", "Scalds the target. The target will suffer more indirect damage. \"Indirect\" damage is any damage caused by anything other than the effects of a spell or weapon. For example: glyphs, poisons, auras, etc.", "Fire"], "b:Osamodas:Flame Tornado": ["{AP} 4\n{WP} 1", "{Enemy} {Element Fire} Damage: 4-111\n{Enemy} Flame Tornado\n{Icon Arrow} 30% damage inflicted by {Icon Summon} Summons\n\n{Ally} Flame Tornado\n{Icon Arrow} 30% heals performed by {Icon Summon} Summons", "Cast on an enemy, the enemy suffers more damage from the Osamodas's summons. If it is an ally, they receive more healing from the summons.", "Fire"], "b:Osamodas:Fanning": ["{AP} 3\n{WP} 1", "{Enemy} {Element Fire} Damage: 4-97\n{Icon Arrow} Heals {Icon Summon} Summons by 200% of damage inflicted\n\n{Ally} Fanning (2 turns)", "Heals the Osamodas's summons based on the damage it inflicts. Cast on an ally, the ally is healed at the start of the turn for several turns.", "Fire"], "b:Osamodas:Dragon's Breath": ["{AP} 5", "{Element Fire} Damage: 5-164 {Area Cross}\n{Icon DragonForm} Dragon Form cast on {Caster} or {Icon Summon}:\n{Icon Arrow} {Element Fire} Damage: 8-244 {Area Circlering}\n{Icon Arrow} The original target loses 10% of their current HP", "Inflicts high damage in an area of effect. In dragon form, the spell's target is injured but the damage inflicted around the target are higher.", "Fire"], "b:Osamodas:Sandstorm": ["{AP} 4\n{WP} 1", "{Enemy} {Element Earth} Damage: 5-152\n\nIf {Icon Summon} Summons is adjacent to the target:\n{Icon Arrow} {Icon Summon} 100 Elemental Resistance\n{Icon Arrow} {Icon Summon} 2 Lock\n{Icon Arrow} {Icon Summon} 30% Block", "The Osamodas's summons becomes more resistant if it is adjacent to the target.", "Earth"], "b:Osamodas:Gravity": ["{AP} 2", "{Element Earth} Damage: 2-58\n{Enemy} -1 Lock and Dodge", "Reduces the target's Lock and Dodge.", "Earth"], "b:Osamodas:Impalement": ["{AP} 5", "{Element Earth} Damage: 5-194", "Inflicts high damage in close combat.", "Earth"], "b:Osamodas:Gambol": ["{AP} 3", "{Element Earth} Damage: 3-91\n{Caster} {MP} 1 MP", "Inflicts damage and gives the caster a mobility bonus.", "Earth"], "b:Osamodas:Crackler Punch": ["{AP} 4", "{Element Earth} Damage: 4-121 {Area Circle}\n\n{Icon DragonForm} Dragon Form cast on {Caster} or {Icon Summon}:\n{Icon Arrow} Attracts aligned entities by 2 cells {Area Cross} (5)\n{Icon Arrow} {Element Earth} Damage: 4-121 {Area Circlering}", "Inflicts damage in an area of effect. In dragon form, attracts fighters in line with the target toward the target.", "Earth"], "b:Osamodas:Whip": ["{AP} 4", "{Element Air} Damage: 4-136\n\nIf the target is a summons:\n{Icon Arrow} {Element Air} Damage: 9-272 instead", "Inflicts double damage on summons.", "Air"], "b:Osamodas:Plucking": ["{AP} 3", "Turns the target to face away\n{Enemy} {Element Air} Damage: 3-91", "Changes where the target is looking in order to turn its back.", "Air"], "b:Osamodas:Transfer": ["{AP} 3\n{WP} 1", "Cast on a fighter, they switch places with {Icon Summon} Summons (7 cells maximum)\n{Enemy} {Element Air} Damage: 4-121\n\n{Icon DragonForm} Dragon Form:\n{Icon Arrow} {Caster} switches places with their {Icon Summon} Summons (7 cells maximum)\n{Icon Arrow} {Enemy} {Element Air} Damage: 4-121 {Area Circlering}", "The target switches places with the summons. In dragon form, the Osamodas and their summons switch places then the Osamodas inflicts damage.", "Air"], "b:Osamodas:Repulsive Breath": ["{AP} 2", "{Enemy} {Element Air} Damage: 2-65\nPushes back 1 cell", "Pushes the target 1 cell.", "Air"], "b:Osamodas:Feather Tornado": ["{AP} 3", "Cast on an empty cell:\n{Icon Arrow} The summons is teleported to the cell (up to 2 cells)\n\n{Element Air} Damage: 3-83 {Area Square} (except on {Icon Summon})\n\n{Icon DragonForm} Dragon Form cast on {Caster} or {Icon Summon}:\n{Icon Arrow} {Element Air} Damage: 3-91 {Area Circlering}", "Inflicts damage in an area of effect. Teleports the summons if the spell is cast on a nearby empty cell.", "Air"], "b:Osamodas:Last Breath": ["{AP} 3", "Cast on {Icon Summon} Summons:\n{Icon Arrow} {Icon Summon} 4 MP\n{Icon Arrow} {Icon Summon} 4 Range\n{Icon Arrow} {Icon Summon} Dies at the end of the turn\n\nPer turn spent on the field:\n{Icon Arrow} {Icon Summon} 10% Damage inflicted\n{Icon Arrow} {Icon Summon} 10% Heals performed\n{Icon Arrow} {Caster} 1 WP", "The Osamodas's summons gains large bonuses but dies at the end of its turn.", "Neutral"], "b:Osamodas:Motivating Shot": ["{WP} 3", "{Ally} Motivating Shot\n\nCast on {Icon Summon}Summons:\n{Icon Arrow} {Caster} regains 2 AP\n\nThe target cannot be targeted again by High-Energy Shot for 3 turns", "The target gains an AP bonus and damage inflicted. If the Osamodas targets their summons, they regain 2 AP.", "Neutral"], "b:Osamodas:Animal Link": ["{AP} 4", "Transfers up to 30% of max HP as armor to the target\n\n{Caster} {WP} 2 WP", "The Osamodas sacrifices health points to give them as armor to an ally. The Osamodas regains 2 WP.", "Neutral"], "b:Osamodas:Velocity": ["{AP} 2\n{WP} 1", "{Ally} 15% damage inflicted in melee\nTransfers remaining MP from caster to the target:\n{Icon Arrow} 2 for 1 on an ally (max 4)\n{Icon Arrow} 1 for 1 on their {Icon Summon} Summons (max 8)", "The Osamodas transfers all their remaining MP to the target. The ally will also inflict more damage in melee.", "Neutral"], "b:Osamodas:Weakening Cry": ["{AP} 3", "{Enemy} Weakening Cry\nOn every blow received by {Icon Summon} Summons:\n{Icon Arrow} Halves damage\n{Icon Arrow} -50 Elemental Resistance", "The target reduces the damage suffered by the Osamodas's summons, but in exchange loses resistance when the target inflicts damage on it.", "Neutral"], "b:Osamodas:Relay": ["{AP} 3", "{Ally} Relay\n\n{Icon Summon} Summons or Gobgob:\n{Icon Arrow} Switches positions instantly", "At the start of the turn, the ally changes places with the Osamodas's summons. If the summons is not in play, the ally changes places with the Osamodas.\nCast on their summons or the Gobgob, the Osamodas instantly changes places with them.", "Neutral"], "b:Osamodas:Boowolf Fury": ["", "{Icon Summon} Summons:\n{Icon Arrow} {Icon Summon} -75 Elemental Resistance\n\nAt start of turn (3 times maximum):\n{Icon Arrow} {Icon Summon} 15% Damage inflicted\n{Icon Arrow} {Icon Summon} 15% Heals performed\n{Icon Arrow} {Icon Summon} 1 MP", "The summons is harder to keep alive but gains bonuses for turns passed on the field."], "b:Osamodas:Animal Gift": ["", "At start of turn, if {Icon Summon} Summons is alive:\n{Icon Arrow} {Caster} 1 WP\n\nThe cooldown period for a summons is increased by 2 turns", "The Osamodas regains 1 WP at the start of the turn if their summons is on the field. On the other hand, summoning the same entity again is more difficult."], "b:Osamodas:Taur Strength": ["", "30% single-target damage (transferred to {Icon Summon} Summons)\n\nReduces Dodge to 0", "The Osamodas and their summons inflict more single-target damage at the expense of their Dodge."], "b:Osamodas:Animal Synergy": ["", "{Caster} -20% Damage inflicted\nDamage from {Icon Summon} Summons is increases by 20%\n\nWhen {Icon Summon} Summons kills an enemy:\n{Icon Arrow} {Caster} 2 WP (4 maximum)", "The Osamodas sacrifices some of their power and transfers it to their summons. When a summons kills an enemy, the Osamodas regenerates WP."], "b:Osamodas:Symbiosa": ["", "When {Icon Summon} Summons dies (no matter how):\n{Icon Arrow} {Caster} 30% damage inflicted in melee (1 turn)\n{Icon Arrow} {Caster} -100 Elemental Resistance (1 turn)\n\nThe state is not stackable", "The Osamodas gains a melee-combat damage bonus in exchange for some of their resistances when their summons returns to the Gobgob."], "b:Osamodas:Crobak Vision": ["", "{Icon Summon} Summons:\n{Icon Arrow} No longer blocks line of sight\n\n{Caster} 2 Range", "Summons no longer hinder line of sight. The Osamodas gains range to better take advantage of this."], "b:Osamodas:Summoning Warrior": ["", "{Caster} 20% Damage inflicted\n\nThe Damage and Heals of {Icon Summon} Summons are reduced by 20%", "The Osamodas sacrifices some of their summons's power to become stronger."], "b:Osamodas:Solitary Summoner": ["", "At end of turn, if no {Icon Summon} Summons alive:\n{Icon Arrow} {Caster} 3 AP for the next turn", "At the end of the turn, the Osamodas gains AP for the next turn if their summons isn't on the field."], "b:Osamodas:Dragonic Power": ["", "{Icon DragonForm} Dragon Form\n{Icon Arrow} 25% Damage inflicted\n{Icon Arrow} -1 WP at end of turn\n\nThe Osamodas loses {Icon DragonForm} Dragon Form if they have no more WP", "The Osamodas becomes more powerful in dragon form but has more difficulty regenerating WP."], "b:Osamodas:Phoenix Spirit": ["", "The cooldown periods for a summons is reduced by 2 turns\n\n{Icon Summon} Summons have 30% less HP", "The Osamodas can more quickly re-summmon a creature that has come back in their Gobgob. However, their summons have less HP."], "b:Osamodas:Dragonic Transcendence": ["", "{Icon DragonForm} Dragon Form:\n{Icon Arrow} The first elemental spell of the turn is cast in a 2-cell cross {Area Cross} instead of 1", "In dragon form, the first elemental spell cast on the Osamodas or their summons has its area of effect increased."], "b:Osamodas:South Star": ["", "Fighters have additional effects when they are in one of the Gobgob's auras\n\nLunar Aura:\n{Icon Arrow} Inflicts 20% less damage on the aura bearer's allies\n\nSolar Aura:\n{Icon Arrow} 2 Range and 15% Damage inflicted", "The Gobgob's auras apply an effect on\nfighters while they are in the aura."], "b:Osamodas:Animal Sacrifice": ["", "{Caster} {WP} 3 WP\n\nThe Summons spell no longer has modifiable range", "The Osamodas gains max WP but loses flexibility in managing their summons."], "b:Osamodas:Eastern Star": ["", "The Gobgob's auras can be applied on the Osamodas\n\nThe Gobgob's auras now last only 1 turn", "The Gobgob's auras can be applied on the Osamodas but last for less time."], "b:Osamodas:Animal Devotion": ["", "-25% damage inflicted and heals performed\n(transferred to {Icon Summon})\n\nSingle-target spells on allies no longer inflict damage and have extra effects (double on {Icon Summon} Summons)\n\nFire spells {Element Fire} apply Flaming (1/AP)\nEarth spells {Element Earth} give armor (12/AP)\nAir {Element Air} spells heal 3% of the target's missing HP for each AP", "The Osamodas gains support abilities in exchange for some of their damage."], "b:Osamodas:The Art of Taming": ["", "It is possible to summon two creatures simultaneously\n\nDamage suffered by summons is transferred to the Osamodas\n\nSummoned creatures gain Summoning Sickness (1 turn)", "Two creatures from the Gobgob can be summoned on the field at the same time. In exchange, damage they suffer is transferred to the Osamodas. You cannot summon the same creature twice on the field, but two Osamodas can each summon a different creature."], "b:Osamodas:Animal Sharing": ["", "{Caster} {Elemental Resistance} -100 Elemental Resistance\n{Icon Summon} Summons gains 100 Elemental Resistance\n\nIf the Osamodas suffers damage:\n{Icon Arrow} {Icon Summon}10% damage inflicted (not stackable)\n{Icon Arrow} {Icon Summon} 1 MP (not stackable)", "The Osamodas sacrifices some of their resistances and gives them to their summons. When the Osamodas is attacked, their summons gain bonuses."], "b:Foggernaut:Machinery": ["{WP} 2", "Cast on an ally {Ally}:\n{Icon Arrow} Moving on the rail costs 1 MP (2 turns)\n{Icon Arrow} Inactive if the target is carrying a fighter\n\nCast on an enemy {Enemy}:\n{Icon Arrow} Stabilized (1 turn)", "By using this spell, the Foggernaut can stabilize an enemy or improve an ally's mobility if using rails.", "Neutral"], "b:Eniripsa:Production Secret": ["", "Propagator no longer inflicts damage on activation\n{Icon Arrow} Inflicts damage at end of the target's turn\n{Icon Arrow} For 2 turns\n{Icon Arrow} Damage reduced by 20%", "Propagator now applies its effects for a longer time: it lasts two turns."], "b:Iop:Bravery": ["", "At end of turn:\n{Icon Arrow} {Caster} {Armor} 0.4% of max HP as Armor per level of Power\n\nThe Iop cannot gain Power at end of turn if they have no enemies 3 cells away", ""], "b::Mass Charm": ["{AP} 2", "{Target} {Lock} 150 Lock\nAttracts by 2 cells toward the {Target}", "This spell lets you simulate physical attraction towards your target which is then transferred to others, so they become fatally attracted to it. Warning: this spell has strong emotions."], "b::Mastery of Weapons": ["{AP} 2", "Mastery of Weapons (Lvl 100)\nMisses a turn", "By casting this spell, the caster receives ancestral knowledge from all the weapons masters who ever existed, the wave of power floods through their veins and causes euphoria, and they're ready to happily beat up any opponents!"], "b::Carnage": ["", "15% damage inflicted\n10% damage inflicted on {Enemy} that have Armor\n-30% heals performed", "Want to know the secret ingredient in carnage rolls, extra damage!"], "b::Evasion": ["", "100% of level as Dodge\nAfter dodging (with loss):\n{Icon Arrow} 35% of level as Dodge (3 turns)", "This passive is ideal for getting away from it all!"], "b::Interception": ["", "100% of level as Lock\nAfter locking an {Enemy}:\n{Icon Arrow} 35% of level as Lock (3 turns)", "Hey, where do you think you're going? You're staying right there!"], "b::Fluctuation": ["", "When you dodge an {Enemy}:\n{Icon Arrow} With losses: {Enemy} Fluctuation (+10 Lvl.)\n{Icon Arrow} Without loss: {Enemy} Fluctuation (+15 Lvl.)\nWhen you lock an {Enemy}:\n{Icon Arrow} {Enemy} Fluctuation (+15 Lvl.)\nTo {Enemy} ending their turn upon contact with you:\n{Icon Arrow} {Enemy} Fluctuation (+20 Lvl.)", "When two fighters fight, an energy is inevitably transferred from one to the other. The concept of this liability lies in the misuse of this energy, for brutal purposes."], "b::Rock": ["", "60% Health Points\n25% Heals received\n-25% damage inflicted\n-50% heals performed", "Solid as a rock, let me take that damage for you!"], "b::Inhalation": ["", "50% of level as Initiative\n10% damage inflicted on {Enemy} with more Initiative", "A deep breath, a cold drink and... to battle!"], "b::Medicine": ["", "30% heals performed\n25% Armor given\n-15% damage inflicted", "Need a healer in your team? Here I am!"], "b::Motivation": ["", "{AP} 1 AP\n-20% damage inflicted\n10 Force of Will", "It's easy to be one step ahead of your enemies if you are Motivated."], "b:Eniripsa:Alternative Cure": ["{AP} 2", "{Ally} {Element Fire} Healing: 4-33\n{Ally} Here Mark (Lvl 2-490)", "Heals an ally. The target will then get 20% of the heals done by the Eniripsa on fighters other than the target, until the target reaches 100% HP.", "Fire"], "b:Eniripsa:Heal-splosion": ["{AP} 3", "{Enemy} Sadist Mark (Lvl 4-111) {Area Vline}\n{Enemy} {Element Fire} Damage: 3-83 {Area Vline}", "Inflicts Fire damage on enemies in an area of effect. Places a Sadist Mark: The Eniripsa deals Fire damage around the target when the target is KO'd.", "Fire"], "b:Eniripsa:Guardian Fire": ["{AP} 4", "{Ally} {Element Fire} Healing: 8-61\n{Ally} Triad Mark (Lvl 1-245)", "Heals an ally and applies a mark to the ally: If the ally loses HP and falls below 50% of their max HP, they are healed by the Eniripsa a second time.", "Fire"], "b:Eniripsa:Corrosive Heal": ["{AP} 5\n{WP} 1", "{Enemy} {Element Fire} Damage: 5-164\n{Enemy} Hammle Mark (+1 Lvl.)", "The target becomes marked: boosts the next three direct, single-target damage spells suffered by the target. Also, a portion of damage inflicted on the target is redistributed in the form of healing around the target.", "Fire"], "b:Eniripsa:Purifying Flame": ["{AP} 3", "{Ally} {Element Fire} Healing: 6-50\n\n{Enemy} {Element Fire} Damage: 3-91\n\n{Target} Refund Mark (Lvl 6-42)\n\nIf the Eniripsa has >= 80% HP:\n{Icon Arrow} The spell's area of effect becomes {Area Cross}", "This spell inflicts damage on enemies and heals allies. It also applies a mark, no matter what team the target is on: The target gains 1 MP and triggers the mark if the target ends their turn next to an ally of the Eniripsa. When triggered, the mark heals the Eniripsa's allies near the mark bearer.", "Fire"], "b:Eniripsa:Invigoration": ["{AP} 2", "{Ally} {Element Water} Healing: 4-35\n{Ally} {Dodge} 1-49 Dodge\n\n{Enemy} {Element Water} Damage: 2-65", "Heals the targeted ally and gives a small Dodge gain. This spell has a Iong range.", "Water"], "b:Eniripsa:Healing Word": ["{AP} 3", "{Ally} {Element Water} Healing: 6-50\n{Ally} {Range} 1 Range (max. 3)\n\n{Enemy} {Element Water} Damage: 3-91", "Heals the targeted ally and gives the a Range bonus for one turn. Each Range point increases the max range of Range-modifiable spells.", "Water"], "b:Eniripsa:Infusion": ["{AP} 4", "{Ally} {Element Water} Healing: 4-33\n{Ally} At start of turn:\n{Icon Arrow} {Element Water} Healing: 4-33 (3 turns) (stackable)\n\n{Enemy} {Element Water} Damage: 4-121", "Cast on an ally, the targeted ally is healed several turns in a row.", "Water"], "b:Eniripsa:Revitalization": ["{AP} 3", "{Ally} {Element Water} Healing: 6-42 {Area Cross}\n{Ally} {Damage Inflicted} 10% damage inflicted (max 20%) {Area Circle}\n\n{Enemy} {Element Water} Damage: 3-76 {Area Cross}\n\nIf the Eniripsa has >= 80% HP:\n{Icon Arrow} the spell's area of effect becomes {Area Circle}", "Heals allies in an area of effect and gives them a bonus to damage inflicted.", "Water"], "b:Eniripsa:Regeneration": ["{AP} 5\n{WP} 1", "{Ally} {Element Water} Healing: 12-100\n{Icon Arrow} {Caster} {Element Water} Healing: 12-100\n{Icon Arrow} {Caster} {Heart percent} 20% heals performed (1 turn)\n\n{Enemy} {Element Water} Damage: 6-182", "This spell can reach targets through obstacles. It heals the targeted ally and increases healing done by the Eniripsa for the rest of their turn.", "Water"], "b:Eniripsa:Anatomy": ["{AP} 3", "If the target has more than 80% of max HP:\n{Icon Arrow} {Element Air} Damage: 5-152 (penetrates Armor)\n\nOtherwise:\n{Icon Arrow} {Element Air} Damage: 3-91 (penetrates Armor)", "Inflicts Air damage that penetrates Armor. This damage is greater if the target has high HP.", "Air"], "b:Eniripsa:Psychosis": ["{AP} 3\n{WP} 1", "{Element Air} Damage: 3-83 {Area Cross}\n{Damage Inflicted} -20% damage inflicted {Area Cross}\n{Critical Hit} -20% Critical Hit {Area Cross}", "This area-of-effect spell weakens all fighters in an area for one turn, in addition to dealing damage.", "Air"], "b:Eniripsa:Cross-Airs": ["{AP} 2", "{Element Air} Damage: 2-60\n\nPainful Collisions (Lvl 1-30)\nWhen suffering a collision:\n{Icon Arrow} {Element Air} Damage: 1-30", "Inflicts Air damage on the target and makes the target vulnerable to collisions. To cause a collision, you must push one obstacle against another one.", "Air"], "b:Eniripsa:Infected Flask": ["{AP} 4\n{WP} 2", "{Element Air} Damage: 4-102\n{Icon Arrow} 100% health stolen\n\nGangrene (Lvl 4-102)\nAt end of turn:\n{Icon Arrow} {Element Air} Damage: 4-102\n{Icon Arrow} 100% health stolen", "This spell steals health from the target: one time when it is cast, and a second time at the end of the target's turn.", "Air"], "b:Eniripsa:Lethargy": ["{AP} 5", "{Element Air} Damage: 5-164\n\nIf the Eniripsa has >= 80% HP:\n{Icon Arrow} {Element Air} Damage: 2-65 extra\n{Icon Arrow} {Caster} {Element Air} Damage: 2-65", "If the Eniripsa has very high HP, this spell deals more damage, but it also hurts the Eniripsa casting it.", "Air"], "b:Eniripsa:Eniraser": ["{AP} 2\n{WP} 1", "Cast on KO'd {Ally}:\n{Icon Arrow} Revives the {Ally} with 30% max HP\n{Icon Arrow} {Ally} In Recovery (Lvl 1)", "The Eniripsa can revive a KO'ed ally. Be careful, a character can only be revived once per combat, and he will also die if his reanimator is KO'ed.", "Neutral"], "b:Eniripsa:Fountain of Youth": ["{AP} 2", "Fountain of Youth\n-20% Health Points\n{MP} 2 MP\n{Heart percent} 15% heals performed\n{Dodge} 3 Dodge", "For two turns, the Eniripsa loses some of their max HP, but they become more mobile and have enhanced healing abilities.", "Neutral"], "b:Eniripsa:Bond of Friendship": ["{AP} 2\n{WP} 1", "Bond of Friendship\nWhen the state bearer suffers damage (>= 3% of their max HP):\n{Icon Arrow} Regenerator (+3 Lvl.)\n{Icon Arrow} The Eniripsa gains Generator (+3 Lvl.)\"", "Applies the Bond of Friendship state: The targeted ally gets a boost to damage inflicted and resistance if they suffer damage. The Eniripsa can only place one Regeneration per team.", "Neutral"], "b:Eniripsa:Transcendence": ["{AP} 1\n{WP} 2", "{Target} Transcendent\n{Icon Arrow} Can only be Transcendent once per combat", "The target loses all AP but becomes immune to damage for one turn.", "Neutral"], "b:Eniripsa:Ban": ["{AP} 2", "Removes 10% of {Caster} max HP as Armor from the target and converts it to healing on the Eniripsa\n\nWith Against Nature:\n{Icon Arrow} Incurable (Lvl 5)\n\nOtherwise:\n{Icon Arrow} Crumbly (Lvl 5)", "Applies a penalty to armor or healing received by the target for one turn. This spell also steals Armor from the target and gets it back as HP.", "Neutral"], "b:Eniripsa:Life-Saving Fountain": ["{WP} 2", "Place a Life-Saving Fountain glyph in a {Area Circle}:\n{Icon Arrow} {Target} {Element Light} heals: 1-25", "Places a large healing glyph that affects both allies and enemies.", "Neutral"], "b:Eniripsa:Serial Marker": ["", "For each mark placed:\n{Icon Arrow} {Element Light} heal: 2 in a 2-cell {Area Cross} around the target\n\nFire spells' Range is modified:\n{Icon Arrow} +1 to min Range\n{Icon Arrow} Non-modifiable Range", "Each mark placed on a target heals the fighters around that target. In exchange, Fire spells become harder to cast."], "b:Eniripsa:Vital Climax": ["", "30% Heals received\n\nHP conditions on the Eniripsa become:\n{Icon Arrow} HP must be at 100%", "This passive increases the Eniripsa's heals received, but changes the ability activation threshold to require a certain amount of HP."], "b:Eniripsa:Puncture": ["", "If the Eniripsa has >= 80% HP:\n{Icon Arrow} 30% Heals performed\n{Icon Arrow} The Eniripsa suffers 10% of the heals performed as damage", "When the Eniripsa has 80% or more of their maximum HP, their heals performed are increased. However, they also take damage equivalent to 10% of the healing they perform."], "b:Eniripsa:Precision Marking": ["", "A single mark of each type can be active at the same time\n\nWhen a mark is triggered:\n{Icon Arrow} Propagator +10% of level", "Only one mark of a given type can be active at a time. When this mark is consumed or triggered, the Eniripsa gains 10% of their level in Propagator points."], "b:Eniripsa:Vampiripsa": ["", "Propagator:\n{Icon Arrow} -25% damage inflicted\n{Icon Arrow} {Caster} steals 50% of Propagator damage", "This passive changes how Propagator works. Damage inflicted is lower, but the Eniripsa absorbs half of the damage inflicted via Propagator."], "b:Eniripsa:Radiance": ["", "At end of turn, per 2 levels of Propagator:\n{Icon Arrow} {Element Light} heal: 1 {Area Circle} around the Eniripsa\n{Icon Arrow} Propagator is removed", "When the Eniripsa ends their turn, they consume their Propagator to heal themself and their nearby allies."], "b:Eniripsa:Presence": ["", "At end of turn, if the Eniripsa is isolated\n(no ally or enemy 3 or fewer cells away):\n{Icon Arrow} 2 map MP (1 turn)\n{Icon Arrow} Propagator is removed\n\nIf they are not isolated:\n{Icon Arrow} 20% of level as Propagator", "At end of turn, if the Eniripsa is isolated, they gain mobility for the next turn, but lose their Propagator. Conversely, if there are one or more fighters near the Eniripsa, the Eniripsa gains Propagator, but loses Range on the next turn."], "b:Eniripsa:Doctor Without Barriers": ["", "Propagator\n{Icon Arrow} No longer increases after a heal\n{Icon Arrow} Increases after damage inflicted\n\nOn the next single-target heal:\n{Icon Arrow} {Element Light} healing based on the level of Propagator", "Changes how Propagator works: Performing heals no longer increases it, but inflicting damage does. Propagator is consumed on a single-target heal, and improves the healing performed."], "b:Eniripsa:Single Heal": ["", "Each turn, on the first single-target healing spell:\n{Icon Arrow} {Element Light} healing: 11\n\nAfter performing a single-target heal:\n{Icon Arrow} Healing reduced by 30% (1 turn)", "Each turn, the first single-target healing spell cast by the Eniripsa is more powerful. In exchange, after the improved healing spell, any additional healing spells cast by the Eniripsa during their turn have reduced effects."], "b:Eniripsa:Super Coney II": ["", "Coney\n{Icon Arrow} Has a 2 turn cooldown\n{Icon Arrow} Instantly summons a Super Coney\n{Icon Arrow} The Super Coney dies at end of turn", "The Eniripsa now immediately summons the Super Coney, instead of waiting a turn. In exchange, the Coney spell now has a two-turn cooldown, and the Super Coney dies at the end of its turn."], "b:Eniripsa:Transgression": ["", "When Against Nature is active:\n{Icon Arrow} 75 Elemental Resistance\n{Icon Arrow} -2 max Range with elemental spells", "This passive increases the Eniripsa's resistance potential when under the effects of Unnatural Remedies. In exchange, their range decreases while in this mode."], "b:Eniripsa:Delay": ["", "Direct healing performed is halved\n\nEach heal performed applies Delay\n{Icon Arrow} Healing at start of turn", "This passive delays half of the healing that the Eniripsa performs on their targets."], "b:Eniripsa:Wind Elixir": ["", "For each level of Propagator:\n{Icon Arrow} {Caster} 3 Dodge\n\nWhen consuming Propagator, per level:\n{Icon Arrow} {Target} -3 Lock (1 turn) on the target\n\nThe Eniripsa's Lock goes to 0 at start of fight", "This passive increases the Eniripsa's Dodge when they accumulate Propagator. In addition, consuming Propagator on a target removes Lock from it. However, the Eniripsa's Lock drops to 0."], "b:Eniripsa:Apprentice Alchemist": ["", "Each time Propagator is triggered:\n{Icon Arrow} Steals -1 MP from the target\n\nGeneration of Propagator is divided by 2", "When Propagator is triggered, the Eniripsa steals 1 MP from the target. In exchange, the Eniripsa's generation of Propagator is cut in half."], "b:Eniripsa:Anbarul Mark": ["", "Repulsion\n{Icon Arrow} Triggers marks\n{Icon Arrow} No longer pushes marked targets", "Repulsion immediately triggers marks, but does not push the marked targets."], "b:Eniripsa:All for Me": ["", "HP bonus for the Eniripsa:\n{Icon Arrow} 800% of their level\n\nConey now has a max Range of 1 (non-modifiable)", "The Eniripsa's HP increase significantly. In exchance, the Coney spell can only be cast on adjacent targets"], "b:Eniripsa:Unnatural Paradox": ["", "Propagator\n{Icon Arrow} Generation doubled in normal mdoe\n{Icon Arrow} Generation doubled with Propagator", "Heals performed in normal mode increase the Propagator level twice as much, but in exchange, heals performed with Unnatural Remedies no longer increase the Propagator level."], "b:Eniripsa:Ambivalence": ["", "The Against Nature spell has 1 to 3 Range\n\nCast on an {Ally}:\n{Icon Arrow} {Ally} -30% healing resistance (1 turn)\n{Icon Arrow} {Caster} 30% heals performed (1 turn)\n\nCast on an {Enemy}:\n{Icon Arrow} {Enemy} suffer 20% of single-target healing performed by {Caster}", "Unnatural Remedies can now be cast on a target other than the Eniripsa, triggering different effects."], "b:Eniripsa:Still Life": ["", "Coney\n{Icon Arrow} Costs 3 AP\n\nWhen the Coney dies:\n{Icon Arrow} Summons a glyph Still Life\n{Icon Arrow} Range bonus to fighers", "When the Coney dies, a glyph appears on its position. In exchange, the Coney is more expensive."], "b:Pandawa:Flaming Burp": ["{AP} 2", "{Enemy} {Element Fire} Damage: 2 -60 {Size: 3 x 0}\n{Ally} {Element Fire} Healing: 4-33 {Size: 3 x 0}\n\nIf the target is Dizzy:\n{Icon Arrow} {Enemy} {Elemental Resistance} -100 Elemental Resistance (1 turn)\n{Icon Arrow} {Ally} {Damage Inflicted} 20% damage inflicted (1 turn)\n{Icon Arrow} Consumes Dizzy", "The Pandawa blows on his opponents and deals them Fire damage! What's more, he removes their resistances it they are Dizzy!", "Fire"], "b:Pandawa:Light My Fire": ["{AP} 4\n{WP} 1", "{Enemy} {Element Fire} Damage: 3-83\n{Ally} {Element Fire} Healing: 6-46\n\nIf the target is Dizzy:\n{Icon Arrow} Spreads the effects {Size: 1}\n{Icon Arrow} 3 triggers max per target", "Inflicts Fire damage on enemies and heals allies. If the target is Dizzy, the effects apply in a 1-cell cross. Dizzy targets in the area of effect spread the effects in turn.", "Fire"], "b:Pandawa:Dairy Springer": ["{AP} 2", "{Enemy} {Element Fire} Damage: 2-65 {Size: 1}\nIf cast on an empty cell:\n{Icon Arrow} {Caster} Teleports to the cell\n\n{Caster} Merry: spell gains +1 Range", "Inflicts damage on their enemies in an area of effect before teleporting to the targeted cell. It the Pandawa is Merry, the spell's range is increased.", "Fire"], "b:Pandawa:Explosive Flask": ["{AP} 4", "{Element Fire} Damage: 4-121 {Size: 1}\nCast on {Icon Barrel}, the area of effect is increased {Size: 3}\n\nIf the Pandawa is carrying, becomes:\n{Icon Arrow} The spell costs {AP} 1 AP less\n{Icon Arrow} Throws the target on the cell\n{Icon Arrow} {Enemy} {Element Fire} Damage: 4-121 {Size: 3}\n{Icon Arrow} Attracts 2 cells toward the {Icon Barrel} {Size: 3}", "Inflicts Fire damage in an area of effect. The area of effect increased it the spell is cast on the barrel. If the Pandawa is carrying a target, the Pandawa throws the target and then attracts targets around the barrel and inflicts damage on them.", "Fire"], "b:Pandawa:Milking It": ["{AP} 5", "{Element Fire} Damage: 5-139 {Size: 2}\n{Enemy} Scalded (Lvl 3) {Size: 2}\n\nOn Dizzy targets:\n{Icon Arrow} {Element Fire} Damage: 195 instead\n{Icon Arrow} Consumes Dizzy", "Inflicts Fire damage in an area of effect and scalds targets. A Scalded fighter suffers more indirect damage. The Pandawa consumes the targets' Dizzy state to inflict greater damage.", "Fire"], "b:Pandawa:Splash of Milk": ["{AP} 4", "Cast on target:\n{Icon Arrow} {Element Water} Damage: 4-141\nIf target is Dizzy: 100% health stolen\n\nCast on {Icon Barrel}\n{Icon Arrow} {Element Water} Healing: 8-76 {Size: 1-1 x 1-1}\n{Icon Arrow} Places a Milk Cloud lvl. 12-92 {Area Squarering}", "The Pandawa creates a Splash ot Milk which inflicts damage and makes targets Dizzy! Cast on the Barrel, this creates a Milk Cloud that heals all targets present on it at their start ot turn.", "Water"], "b:Pandawa:Milky Breath": ["{AP} 2", "{Enemy} {Element Water} Damage: 2-65 {Size: 2 x 0}\n{Ally} {Element Water} Healing: 4-35 {Size: 2 x 0}\n{Caster} Merry: Pushes back 1 cell {Size: 2 x 0}\n\nIf the Pandawa is carrying, becomes:\n{Icon Arrow} The spell costs {AP} 1 AP less\n{Icon Arrow} Throws the target on the cell\n{Icon Arrow} {Caster} Moves to be adjacent", "Inflicts damage on enemies and heals allies in a straight line. If the Pandawa is Merry, the targets are pushed back 1 cell. If the Pandawa throws a target with this spell, the Pandawa is attracted adjacent to the target directly.", "Water"], "b:Pandawa:Bubble Trouble": ["{AP} 3", "{Enemy} {Element Water} Damage: 3-83\n{Ally} {Element Water} Healing: 6-46\n\nCast on {Icon Barrel}:\n{Icon Arrow} The area of effect becomes {Size: 3}\n\nThe spell is replicated on the previous targets", "Inflicts Water damage on enemies and heals allies. It the spell is cast on the barrel, the effects are applied in an area of effect around the barrel. Each time the spell is cast in the same turn, the effects are replayed on the previous targets.", "Water"], "b:Pandawa:Milk Wave": ["{AP} 6\n{WP} 1", "{Enemy} {Element Water} Damage: 7-247\n{Ally} {Element Water} Healing: 14-134\n\nIf the target is Dizzy:\n{Icon Arrow} {Enemy} {Element Water} Damage: 11-370\n{Icon Arrow} {Enemy} {Damage Inflicted} -15% damage inflicted (1 turn)\n{Icon Arrow} {Ally} {Element Water} Healing: 21-201\n{Icon Arrow} {Ally} {Elemental Resistance} 75 Elemental Resistance (1 turn)\n{Icon Arrow} Consumes Dizzy", "Inflicts Water damage on enemies and heals allies. It the target is Dizzy, the Pandawa consumes the state to apply a bonus on allies or a penalty on enemies. Damage and healing are also increased.", "Water"], "b:Pandawa:Milk Fountain": ["{AP} 4\n{WP} 1", "{Enemy} {Element Water} Damage: 5-152 {Size: 2}\n{Ally} {MP} 1 MP, {MP} 2 MP if Dizzy (1 turn)\n\nIf cast on a {Icon Barrel}:\n{Icon Arrow} The area becomes {Size: 3}\n{Icon Arrow} Attracts 2 cells toward the {Icon Barrel}\n\nPer target hit: {Caster} {MP} 1 MP (1 turn)", "Inflicts Water damage on enemies in an area of effect and grants MP to allies. If the spell is cast on a barrel, the area oi effect is increased, and targets are attracted toward the barrel. For each target hit, the Pandawa gains 1 MP.", "Water"], "b:Pandawa:Triple Whammy": ["{AP} 2", "{Enemy} {Element Earth} Damage: 2-51\nIf the Pandawa is carrying their own {Icon Barrel}:\n{Icon Arrow} The spell costs {AP} 1 AP less\n{Icon Arrow} Increases the spell's max Range by 4\n{Icon Arrow} Attracts by 2 cells if Dizzy, 4 if Dizzy\n\nOtherwise: Pushes back 2 cells", "The Pandawa inflicts damage while pushing his enemy backwards. If he is carrying his Barrel, it will land on his opponent instead of pushing him back!", "Earth"], "b:Pandawa:Six Roses": ["{AP} 4", "{Enemy} {Element Earth} damage: 4-121 (+5% per MP, 30% max)\n{Caster} {Armor} 8-37 {Element Earth} {Armor} Armor (+5% per MP, 30% max)\nIf the target is Dizzy:\n{Icon Arrow} {Caster} {Elemental Resistance} 50 Elemental Resistance (1 turn)\n{Icon Arrow} {Caster} {Lock} 200% of level as Lock (1 turn)", "Inflicts Earth damage and grants Armor to the caster. The Pandawa consumes the target's Dizzy state to gain resistances and Lock. It the Pandawa is carrying their barrel, the spell costs 1 AP less. The more MP the Pandawa has remaining, the more effective the spell's effects are.", "Earth"], "b:Pandawa:Barrel Blow": ["{AP} 3", "Switches places\n{Element Earth} Damage: 3-98 {Size: 1-1 x 1-1}\nIf the target is Dizzy\n{Icon Arrow} {Enemy} {Dodge} -1 Dodge\n\nIf the Pandawa is carrying their own {Icon Barrel}\n{Icon Arrow} The spell costs {AP} 1 AP less\n\nMust target a {Icon Barrel}", "The Pandawa inflicts damage and makes the surrounding targets dizzy. If the Pandawa is carrying their Barrel, they increase their Lock and resistances.", "Earth"], "b:Pandawa:Lactic Acid": ["{AP} 4", "{Element Earth} damage: 4-111 (+5% per MP, 30% max) {Size: 1}\n\nIf the Pandawa is carrying:\n{Icon Arrow} The spell costs {AP} 1 AP less\n{Icon Arrow} Throws the target onto the cell (not {Icon Barrel})\n{Icon Arrow} {Enemy} {Element Earth} damage: 4-111 (+5% per MP, 30% max) {Size: 1}", "Inflicts Earth damage in an area of effect. If the Pandawa is carrying a fighter or their barrel, the spell costs 1 AP less, and the Pandawa throws the target onto the cell before inflicting damage.", "Earth"], "b:Pandawa:Blisskrieg": ["{AP} 6\n{WP} 1", "{Element Earth} Damage: 7-178\nIf the target is Dizzy:\n{Icon Arrow} {Caster} {AP} 1 AP\n{Icon Arrow} Consumes Dizzy\n\nIf the Pandawa is carrying their own {Icon Barrel}:\n{Icon Arrow} The spell costs 2 AP less\n{Icon Arrow} {Caster} Teleports to the cell (3 max)\n{Icon Arrow} Damage is melee", "Inflicts Earth damage in an area of effect and consumes the targets' Dizzy state to regain AP. If the Pandawa is carrying their barrel, they teleport to the targeted cell, and the spell costs 2 AP less.", "Earth"], "b:Pandawa:Bamboo Blow": ["{AP} 2\n{WP} 1", "Bamboo Blow (Lvl 1) (1 turn):\n{Elemental Resistance} -50 Elemental Resistance\n{Critical Hit} -15% Critical Hit\n{Block} -15% Block", "Bamboo Blow removes resistances, critical hits, and blocking from the target for one turn.", "Neutral"], "b:Pandawa:Thirst": ["{AP} 2", "{Caster} Moves closer to the targeted {Icon Barrel}\n\nCan be used while carrying a fighter", "The Pandawa moves closer to the targeted barrel. This spell can be used while the Pandawa is carrying a fighter.", "Neutral"], "b:Pandawa:Bamboozle": ["{AP} 2\n{WP} 1", "If cast on oneself:\n{Icon Arrow} {Caster} Neutral spells cost {AP} 1 AP (1 turn)\n{Icon Arrow} {Caster} Regains 2 AP\n\nIf cast on {Icon Barrel}:\n{Icon Arrow} {Ally} Worn-Out {Size: 2} (1 turn):\n{AP} 1 AP\n{Damage Inflicted} 20% damage inflicted", "Allows the Pandawa to reduce the cost of their neutral spells. Cast on a barrel, the AP and damage of nearby allies increase for I turn.", "Neutral"], "b:Pandawa:Ether": ["{AP} 2\n{WP} 1", "Cast on {Ally}:\n{Icon Arrow} Stabilized (1 turn)\n{Icon Arrow} Cannot be locked (1 turn)\n\nCast on {Enemy}:\n{Icon Arrow} Stabilized (1 turn)\n{Icon Arrow} Cannot lock (1 turn)", "The target of Ether becomes stabilized If the target is an ally, the ally becomes Unlockable. lf the target is an opponent, the opponent can no longer lock", "Neutral"], "b:Pandawa:Worn-Out": ["{AP} 2\n{WP} 1", "If cast on oneself:\n{Icon Arrow} {Caster} Armor: 10% of max HP\n{Icon Arrow} {Caster} {Elemental Resistance} 100 Elemental Resistance (1 turn)\n{Icon Arrow} {Caster} Unbewitches the Merry state\n\nIf cast on {Ally}:\n{Icon Arrow} Worn-Out (3 turns)\n\nIf cast on {Icon Barrel}:\n{Icon Arrow} Pushes back 3 cells around the {Icon Barrel}", "Cast on an ally, the ally will be healed at the start of the turn for several turns. Cast on the barrel, the Pandawa repels all targets around the barrel. Cast on themself, the Pandawa gains Armor and resistances but loses the Merry state.", "Neutral"], "b:Pandawa:Pandiniuras": ["{AP} 2", "{Caster} Merry:\n{Icon Arrow} {MP} 3 MP (1 turn)\n\nOtherwise:\n{Icon Arrow} {Range} 3 Range (1 turn)", "Can be used to grant a bonus to an\nally or self for 1 turn. If the Pandawa is\nMerry, it is an MP bonus. Otherwise, it\n\nis a Range bonus.", "Neutral"], "b:Pandawa:Bottomless Barrel": ["", "At end of turn, if {Caster} is adjacent to a {Icon Barrel}:\n{Icon Arrow} Carries the {Icon Barrel}", "If the Pandawa ends their turn next to one of their barrels, they carry it and drink from it to become automatically Merry. They retain their initial orientation."], "b:Pandawa:Bambottle": ["", "Merry:\n{Icon Arrow} {Caster} {Dodge} 200% of level as Dodge\n{Icon Arrow} {Caster} {Lock} -200% of level as Lock", "The Pandawa gains a Dodge bonus while Merry but also a Lock penalty in return."], "b:Pandawa:Tunslucent": ["", "{Icon Barrel} no longer block line of sight", "The Pandawa's barrels are transparent, so they do not block line of sight."], "b:Pandawa:Pandemic": ["", "Dizzy {Enemy} have a {Damage Inflicted} 20% damage inflicted penalty on the {Caster} Pandawa\n\nThe {Caster} Pandawa no longer gains the {Damage Inflicted} damage inflicted bonus on Dizzy enemies", "Enemies made Dizzy by the Pandawa inflict less damage on the Pandawa. However, the Pandawa no longer gains the damage bonus on Dizzy enemies."], "b:Pandawa:Cocktail": ["", "Merry:\n{Icon Arrow} No longer gives {Damage Inflicted} damage inflicted\n{Icon Arrow} Instead: {Heart percent} 25% heals performed", "The Pandawa no longer gains damage while Merry but gains a heals performed bonus instead."], "b:Pandawa:Master of Merriment": ["", "Modifies the settings on the Exhilaration spell:\n{Icon Arrow} The spell can be used 1 time per turn\n{Icon Arrow} The spell costs 1 extra WP\n{Icon Arrow} The spell has 1 Range, non-modifiable", "The Pandawa can use the Exhilaration spell on every turn. However, the spell costs more to cast and has less Range."], "b:Pandawa:Poisoned Chalice": ["", "At the end of turn, on Dizzy {Enemy}:\n{Icon Arrow} Poisoned Chalice (Lvl 6)", "At end of turn, the Pandawa transforms their enemies' Dizzy state into a poison that inflicts damage on them at start of turn."], "b:Pandawa:Milky Instinct": ["", "When summoned, the {Icon Barrel} is Dizzy\n\nThe {Icon Barrel} is destroyed with it is no longer Dizzy", "The Pandawa makes their barrels Dizzy when they are summoned, which lets the Pandawa trigger additional effects on them. However, the barrel is destroyed when the Pandawa loses the Dizzy state."], "b:Pandawa:Straight Through": ["", "Barrelhop no longer has a line of sight\nBarrelhop can only be cast in a straight line {Area Vline}", "The Pandawa can cast the Barrelhop spell through obstacles but only in a straight line."], "b:Pandawa:One Too Many": ["", "On consuming Dizzy:\n{Icon Arrow} {Caster} {Armor} Armor: 5% of max HP\n{Icon Arrow} {Caster} does not regain {WP} WP", ""], "b:Pandawa:Aggressive Barrel": ["", "The {Icon Barrel} explodes at the end of the Pandawa's turn:\n{Icon Arrow} Applies Dizzy {Area Squarering}\n\nThe {Icon Barrel} does not explode is carried by the Pandawa", "At the end of the Pandawa's turn, the barrel explodes and makes targets around it Dizzy. It does not explode if carried by the Pandawa."], "b:Pandawa:Pandaperitif": ["", "When throwing or summoning {Icon Barrel}:\n{Icon Arrow} Triggers the {Icon Barrel} and applies Dizzy {Area Cross}\n{Icon Arrow} 1 time per turn per barrel\n\nThe area of application of Dizzy around the {Icon Barrel} is reduced to a 1-cell cross {Area Cross}", "When the Pandawa throws their barrel, targets around it become instantly Dizzy. However, the barrels' triggering area is smaller."], "b:Pandawa:Purified Chalice": ["", "At the end of turn, on Dizzy {Ally}:\n{Icon Arrow} Purified Chalice (Lvl 9)", "At end of turn, the Pandawa transforms their allies' Dizzy state into a state that heals them at start of turn."], "b:Pandawa:Tunnel Vision": ["", "Merry:\n{Icon Arrow} {Caster} {Melee Mastery} -20% melee damage received\n{Icon Arrow} {Caster} {Distance Mastery} 20% ranged damage received", "When the Pandawa is Merry, they suffer less melee damage but suffer more ranged damage."], "b:Pandawa:Lactic Fermentation": ["", "At end of turn, if the Pandawa is carrying their {Icon Barrel}:\n{Icon Arrow} {Caster} {Armor} Armor: 20% of max HP\n{Icon Arrow} {Caster} loses all their Armor when suffering direct damage from behind", "If it is being carried, the barrel protects the Pandawa at end of turn by granting them Armor. However, the Pandawa loses their Armor if they suiter direct damage from behind while carrying their barrel."], "b:Pandawa:One for the Road": ["", "If the Pandawa ends their turn aligned with their {Icon Barrel}:\n{Icon Arrow} {Caster} is attracted 4 cells toward the {Icon Barrel}", "It the Pandawa ends their turn aligned with their barrel, they are attracted a cells toward the barrel."], "b:Pandawa:Buzzed": ["", "In Merry:\n{Icon Arrow} {Range} 4 Range bonus for all neutral spells (instead of 2)\n{Icon Arrow} Chamrak has 1 max Range (except {Icon Barrel})", "When the Pandawa is Merry, they gain more Range tor their neutral spells, but they can no longer throw targets far away."], "b:Huppermage:Energy Flux": ["{AP} 2", "{Enemy} {Element Fire} Damage: 2-65\n{Tellu'rune}: {Enemy} Negative Energy (Lvl 1): {Block} -20% Block (1 turn, not stackable)\n{Aqua'rune}: {Ally} Positive Energy (Lvl 1): {Critical Hit} 20% Critical Hit (1 turn, not stackable)\n{Aer'rune}: The area of effect becomes {Size: 3}", "It's one of Huppermages' unique spells. It inflicts damage on enemies and can apply a Block penalty on the if the Huppermage has the right rune. Allies can gain Critical Hits.", "Fire"], "b:Huppermage:Luminescent Disc": ["{AP} 2", "{Element Fire} Damage: 2-60\n\nIf {Caster} has exactly 3 runes:\n{Icon Arrow} {Target} Luminescence (Lvl 1): The target suffers 20% extra damage (2 turns, not stackable)\n{Icon Arrow} {Caster} consumes all runes", "It's one of Huppermages' unique spells. The Huppermage sends a disc flying at the target, inflicting damage on it. If the Huppermage has exactly 3 runes at that time, the target will suffer extra damage for 2 turns.", "Fire"], "b:Huppermage:Light of Dawn": ["{AP} 2\n{QB} 50", "{Element Fire} Damage: 2-65\n\nIf {Caster} has {Incan'rune}:\n{Icon Arrow} Applies an elemental weakness in the element of the last rune generated\n{Icon Arrow} The target suffers 20% extra damage in this element (2 turns, not stackable)\n{Icon Arrow} {Caster} consumes {Incan'rune}", "It's one of Huppermages' unique spells. It creates a minor fireball that is launched at the target, which suffers extra damage in the element of the last rune generated.", "Fire"], "b:Huppermage:Downpour": ["{AP} 2", "{Enemy} {Element Water} Damage: 2-55\n{Ally} {Element Water} Healing: 4-30\n\nEach time the spell is cast:\n{Icon Arrow} Repeats its effects on the previous targets", "It's the \"Drip\" spell, borrowed from the Feca class. The Huppermage creates a water bubble, raises it, and launches at the target it to heal it if it is an ally or inflict damage on it if it is an enemy.", "Water"], "b:Huppermage:Walloping": ["{AP} 2", "{Enemy} {Element Water} Damage: 2-70\n{Ally} {Element Water} Healing: 4-38\n\nIf {Caster} has a {Aqua'rune}:\n{Icon Arrow} Transparent (Lvl 1)\n{Icon Arrow} {Caster} consumes {Aqua'rune}", "It's the \"Refinement\" spell, borrowed from the Enutrof class. The Huppermage conjures a shovel that falls on the target and inflicts damage on enemies. If the Huppermage has the water rune, the target becomes transparent for 1 turn, no longer blocking line of sight.", "Water"], "b:Huppermage:Vestige": ["{AP} 2\n{QB} 50", "{Enemy} {Element Water} Damage: 2-70\n{Ally} {Element Water} Healing: 4-38\n{Incan'rune}: {Ally} Vestige (Lvl 1): {Damage Inflicted} 20% damage inflicted (1 turn, not stackable)\n{Tellu'rune}: {Enemy} Haunting (Lvl 1): {Damage Inflicted} -20% damage inflicted (1 turn, not stackable)\n{Aer'rune}: The area of effect switches to {Area Cross} (1)\n\nMust target a fighter or a Will-o-the-Wisp", "It's the \"Clock\" spell, borrowed from the Xelor class. Huppermages summon a clock over the target, which strikes them with lightning. Enemies in the area of effect lose damage inflicted, while allies gain some.", "Water"], "b:Huppermage:Rock Slide": ["{AP} 2", "{Element Earth} Damage: 2-65\n{Incan'rune}: Doubles removal values\n{Aqua'rune}: {AP} -1 AP\n{Aer'rune}: {MP} -1 MP", "It's the \"Rocknoceros\" spell, borrowed from the lop class. In one quick movement, the Huppermage summons stones that fall on the target, inflicting damage on it. The target will also have reduced stats depending on what runes the Huppermage has.", "Earth"], "b:Huppermage:Rift": ["{AP} 2", "{Enemy} {Element Earth} Damage: 2-60\n{Ally} {Armor} 2-799 Armor\n{Caster} {Armor} 2-799 Armor\n\nIf {Caster} has {Tellu'rune}:\n{Icon Arrow} Armor is doubled\n{Icon Arrow} {Caster} consumes {Tellu'rune}", "It's one of Huppermages' unique spells. The spell lets you generate armor for Huppermages while giving armor to an ally or inflicting damage on an enemy.", "Earth"], "b:Huppermage:Backband": ["{AP} 2\n{QB} 50", "{Enemy} {Element Earth} Damage: 2-60\n{Enemy} {MP} -2 MP\n\n{Caster} {Force of Will} +10 Force of Will per rune possess for the duration of the spell", "This is the \"Shovel Shaker\" spell, borrowed from the Enutrof class. The Huppermage inflicts damage on enemies in front of them and removes MP from them. They gain a Force of Will bonus for the duration of the spell, based on the number of runes they have.", "Earth"], "b:Huppermage:Diurnal Butterflies": ["{AP} 2", "{Enemy} {Element Air} Damage: 2-65\n{Incan'rune}: Doubles the values of moves\n{Aqua'rune}: Attracts by 1 cell\n{Tellu'rune}: Pushes back 1 cell", "It's the \"Scaraleaf Wing\" spell, borrowed from the Osamodas class. They spread their arms as if to beat their wings, then they bring their hands together and focus this force on their target to steal Air Mastery from it, inflict damage on it, and move it.", "Air"], "b:Huppermage:Dancing Shadows": ["{AP} 2", "{Enemy} {Element Air} Damage: 2-60\n\nTeleports the target 2 cells farther\n\nIf {Caster} has exactly 2 runes:\n{Icon Arrow} Teleports the target 4 cells farther\n{Icon Arrow} {Caster} consumes all runes", "It's a technique borrowed from Srams. The Huppermage creates a whirlwind that surrounds the target and teleports it farther away.", "Air"], "b:Huppermage:Mirage": ["{AP} 2\n{QB} 50", "Switches places\n{Enemy} {Element Air} Damage: 2-60\n\nIf {Caster} has {Aer'rune}:\n{Icon Arrow} The spell's min and max range increases by 3\n{Icon Arrow} {Caster} consumes {Aer'rune}", "It's the \"Assault\" spell that's been borrowed from the Sacrier class. The Huppermage switches places with the target, inflicting damage on it if it is an enemy. If the Huppermage has an Air rune, this spell's range is modified.", "Air"], "b:Huppermage:Resonance": ["{AP} 4", "{Element Light} Damage: 4-121 {Size: 1 x 1}\n{Incan'rune}: The area of effect becomes {Area Con}\n{Tellu'rune}: Damage penetrates Armor\n{Aer'rune}: The spell no longer has a line of sight", "It's one of Huppermages' unique spells. They extend their hand and a conical shockwave spreads out in front of them. There are additional effects depending on what runes the Huppermage has.", "Light"], "b:Huppermage:Light Arrow": ["{AP} 6\n{QB} 200", "{Element Light} Damage: 10-317\nAdditional effect based on the last rune generated:\n{Incan'rune}: The area of affect becomes {Area Vline} (3)\n{Aqua'rune}: The spell costs 1 AP less\n{Tellu'rune}: {Element Light} Damage: 5-158 (on Armor) \n{Aer'rune}: The target is pushed back 2 cells if they collide: {Element Light} damage: 3-105 (indirect)", "It's the \"Destructive Arrow\" spell, borrowed from the Cra class. The Huppermage brandishes a majestic light arrow, which they loose to strike their target with full force. The spell has additional effects depending on the last rune generated.", "Light"], "b:Huppermage:Moonbeam": ["{AP} 4", "{Element Light} Damage: 4-131 {Area Vline}\nIf a Will-o-the-Wisp is in the area of affect:\n{Icon Arrow} Damage is spread over it in a {Area Hline} (5)\n\nIf {Caster} has {Tellu'rune}:\n{Icon Arrow} {Caster} 20% health stolen and converted to Armor\n{Icon Arrow} {Caster} consumes {Tellu'rune}", "It's one of Huppermages' unique spells. They bring their hands together to project a devastating beam of light. The beam spreads horizontally over Will-o'-the-Wisps.", "Light"], "b:Huppermage:Shiny Orbs": ["{AP} 3\n{QB} 100", "{Enemy} Twice: {Element Light} Damage: 2-63\n{Ally} Twice: {Element Light} Healing: 5-35\n\nIf cast on Will-o-the-Wisp, the area of effect becomes {Area Cross} (1)\n\n{Caster} Abundance (+10 Lvl.) per rune possessed", "It's one of Huppermages' unique spells. They create a Shiny Orb in each hand and then successively launch them at the target, inflicting two lines of damage on enemies and healing allies. The impact zone is extended when the spell is cast on one's own Will-o'-the-Wisp.", "Light"], "b:Huppermage:Twilight Beam": ["{AP} 4", "{Element Light} Damage: 4-131\n\nIf {Caster} has {Incan'rune}:\n{Icon Arrow} 0.5% extra damage per remaining QB%\n{Icon Arrow} {Caster} consumes {Incan'rune}", "It's one of Huppermages' unique spells. The Twilight Beam inflicts Light damage flexibly. If the Huppermage has a Fire rune, the damage will depend on their remaining QB gauge.", "Light"], "b:Huppermage:Glistening Tears": ["{AP} 3", "{Enemy} {Element Light} Damage: 3-98\n{Ally} {Element Light} Healing: 6-53\n\nIf {Caster} has {Aqua'rune}:\n{Icon Arrow} {Caster} {Element Light} Healing: 6-53\n{Icon Arrow} {Caster} consumes {Aqua'rune}", "It's the \"Sadida's Tear\" spell, borrowed from the Sadida class. An enormous tear of light falls onto the target, inflicting damage on it if it is an enemy, and healing it if it is an ally. If the Huppermage has a Water rune, they heal themself at the same time.", "Light"], "b:Huppermage:Light Sword": ["{AP} 2\n{QB} 100", "Twice: {Element Light} Damage: 2-51 {Size: 2 x 1}\n{Icon Arrow} Per Rune: Steals 30% of the damage inflicted", "It's a technique borrowed from lops. The Huppermage gracefully unsheathes their light sword and strikes a blow, inflicting damage in a cone shape in front of them. They steal some of the damage inflicted, depending on the number of runes carried.", "Light"], "b:Huppermage:Glistening Halo": ["{AP} 2\n{QB} 50", "Glistening Halo (Lvl 3-98)\nIf the target dies or is again targeted by Glistening Halo:\n{Icon Arrow} {Enemy} {Element Light} Damage: 3-98 {Size: 3}\n{Icon Arrow} Triggers all other Glistening Halos in the area of effect\n{Icon Arrow} The mark is consumed\n\nIf {Caster} has {Aer'rune}:\n{Icon Arrow} The mark is immediately triggered\n{Icon Arrow} {Caster} consumes {Aer'rune}", "This is the \"Sadist Mark\" spell, borrowed from the Eniripsa class. The Huppermage places a mark on their target. If the Huppermage casts the spell again on a marked target, the mark explodes in an area of effect, causing other marks in the AoE to explode. If the Huppermage has an Air rune, the mark placed is immediately triggered. The mark can't be placed on a summons.", "Light"], "b:Huppermage:Solar Stronghold": ["{AP} 3", "Solar Stronghold (Lvl. 1)\n{Elemental Resistance} 100 Elemental Resistance\n\nWhen the bearer suffers damage and has at least 50 QB:\n{Icon Arrow} The Huppermage generates the rune linked to the damage element\n{Icon Arrow} Consumes 50 QB", "The Huppermage protects an ally with the Solar Stronghold. When the bearer of the Stronghold suffers damage, the Huppermage who initiated the Stronghold generates the rune linked to the damage element in exchange for a bit of QB.", "Neutral"], "b:Huppermage:Runic Overcharge": ["{AP} 2\n{QB} 200", "{Ally} {Element Light} Healing: 12-92\n{Incan'rune}: Doubles bonus values\n{Aqua'rune}: {AP} 1 AP (1 turn)\n{Tellu'rune}: {Elemental Resistance} 40 Elemental Resistance (1 turn)\n{Aer'rune}: {MP} 1 MP (1 turn)\n\nThe runes are consumed", "The Huppermage focuses all the power of their elemental runes to heal an ally, in addition to granting the ally bonuses. The runes are consumed.", "Neutral"], "b:Huppermage:Wall of Energy": ["{QB} 150", "Places Wall of Energy (1 turn)", "To isolate themselves fully, Huppermages can conjure a wall of energy that blocks out spells that require line of sight. Characters can pass through the barrier but lose movement points.", "Neutral"], "b:Huppermage:Visio Imperum": ["{AP} 2", "Casts a spell on the target based on the last rune generated\n{Incan'rune}: Incurable (Lvl. 5) and 50% Armor received\n{Aqua'rune}: Crumbly (Lvl. 5) and 50% Healing received\n{Tellu'rune}: Stabilized (1 turn)\n{Aer'rune}: {Enemy} -3 Range {Ally} 3 Range (1 turn)", "Visio Imperum is a spell that applies different penalties based on the last rune the Huppermage generated.", "Neutral"], "b:Huppermage:Principio Valere": ["{AP} 2", "Casts a spell on the target based on the last rune generated\n{Incan'rune}: Switches places with the {Caster}\n{Aqua'rune}: Teleports to the nearest Will-o-the-Wisp (6 cells max)\n{Tellu'rune}: Teleports across from the {Caster}\n{Aer'rune}: Caster teleports to the targeted cell", "The movement effect of the Principio Valere spell varies depending on the last rune generated by the Huppermage.", "Neutral"], "b:Huppermage:Runification": ["N/A", "{Caster} {Damage Inflicted} 10% damage inflicted per Rune (1 turn)\n{Caster} {Heart percent} 10% heals performed per Rune (1 turn)\n\n{Ally} The bonus is halved\n\nThe spell costs 50 QB per run possessed", "The Huppermage concentrates the power of their elemental runes to give themself or an ally a significant bonus to damage inflicted or heals performed.", "Neutral"], "b:Huppermage:Dynamo": ["", "Runes disappear at end of turn", "The Huppermage's Runes are ephemeral and will disappear at end of turn, allowing them to manage their runes differently."], "b:Huppermage:Antithesis": ["", "Elemental Cycle works differently when the {Caster} has the last rune generated:.\n{Icon Arrow} Consumes it to obtain the other runes\n{Icon Arrow} The spell can no longer be cast for 2 turns", ""], "b:Huppermage:Elemental Distension": ["", "When {Caster} is affected by Heart of Light:\n{Icon Arrow} {Element Fire} {Element Water} {Element Earth} {Element Air} spells linked to the Heart gain 2 Range", "Elemental spells gain 2 Range when the Heart of the same element is active."], "b:Huppermage:Light Link": ["", "When {Caster} summons a Will-o-the-Wisp:\n{Icon Arrow} Switches places with it", "The Huppermage switches places with their Will-o'-the-wisp when they summon it."], "b:Huppermage:Fullness": ["", "When recovering a rune from a Will-o-the-Wisp:\n{Icon Arrow} {Caster} Abundance (+25 levels)\n\nAbundance is only used when it is at max level", "The Huppermage gains a lot ot Abundance by consuming a Will-o'-the-Wisp, but they can only use Abundance when it is at maximum level."], "b:Huppermage:Universality": ["", "Runes possessed at end of turn grant a bonus:\n{Incan'rune}: {Caster} 15% damage inflicted (1 turn)\n{Aqua'rune}: {Caster} 15% heals performed (1 turn)\n{Tellu'rune}: {Caster} 75 Elemental Resistance (1 turn)\n{Aer'rune}: {Caster} 2 Range (1 turn)", "The Huppermage's knowledge allows them to convert their runes into bonuses at the end of the turn, in exchange for some of their Quadramental Breeze."], "b:Huppermage:Sensextension": ["", "Under the effect of Heart of Light, the Huppermage has an active QB regeneration, depending on the element:\n{Icon Arrow} {Incan'rune} Fiery Regeneration\n{Icon Arrow} {Aqua'rune} Aquatic Regeneration\n{Icon Arrow} {Tellu'rune} Earthly Regeneration\n{Icon Arrow} {Aer'rune} Aerial Regeneration\n\nHeart of Light lasts 2 turns and freezes QB regeneration linked to runes", "The Huppermage can regenerate QB under the effects of Heart of Light by meeting certain conditions, but the Heart lasts longer, and QB regeneration linked to runes is disabled."], "b:Huppermage:Runic Profusion": ["", "At end of turn:\n{Icon Arrow} Abundance (+15 Lvl.) per rune possessed\nQB gains are reduced by 20%", "At the end of the turn, the Huppermage increases the abilities of their Light spells for the following turn based on the number of runes they have."], "b:Huppermage:Quadramental Absorption": ["", "{Force of Will} 20 Force of Will\nWhen {Caster} performs a reduction (AP, MP or Range):\n{Icon Arrow} 20 Quadramental Breeze\n\n-10% damage inflicted by {Element Light} spells", "The Huppermage gains Force of Will to obstruct their opponents. They generate QB for each reduction (AP, MP, or Range) performed."], "b:Huppermage:Elemental Refraction": ["", "The rune linked to the Heart of Light element is no longer immutable\n\nWhen casting a {Element Fire} {Element Water} {Element Earth} {Element Air} elemental spell with Heart of Light:\n{Icon Arrow} The Heart of Light element takes on the spell element\n{Icon Arrow} The change takes place before the spell's effects are applied", "The Huppermage can automatically change their Heart of Light element, but the rune linked to the active Heart element is no longer immutable."], "b:Huppermage:Soul Altruism": ["", "With Heart of Light:\n{Icon Arrow} {Caster} 15% extra heals performed\n{Icon Arrow} {Caster} The damage inflicted bonus is lost\n{Icon Arrow} {Caster} When healing an ally: +30 QB", "The Huppermage sacrifices the damage granted by Heart of Light to gain heals performed. This passive also allows them to recover Quadramental Breeze each time they heal an ally."], "b:Huppermage:New Breath": ["", "Increases the Will-o'-the-Wisp spell's range by 3\n\nWhen the spell is cast, if a Will-o-the-Wisp is already on the field:\n{Icon Arrow} Moves the Will-o-the-Wisp\n\n1 Will-o-the-Wisp maximum", "The Huppermage has better control of their Will-o'-the-wisp. However, they can only place one at a time."], "b:Huppermage:Soul Development": ["", "Under Heart of Light:\n{Icon Arrow} {Caster} -100 resistance in the Heart of Light's element\n{Icon Arrow} {Caster} 100 resistance in all other elements\n{Icon Arrow} Elemental mastery is increased by\n10% (instead of 20)", "The Huppermage uses the Heart of Light to gain resistance in other elements."], "b:Huppermage:Pulsation": ["", "When {Caster} summons the Will-o-the-Wisp:\n{Icon Arrow} Attracts aligned targets within 5 cells by 2 cells\n\nWhen the {Caster} recovers the Will-o-the-Wisp\n{Icon Arrow} Repels aligned targets within 5 cells by 2 cells", "The Will-o'-the-Wisp attracts fighters when placed; it repels them when consumed."], "b:Huppermage:Runic Save": ["", "If {Caster} has exactly 1 rune:\n{Icon Arrow} Saves the other 3 runes onto the Will-o'-the-Wisp when it is summoned\n\nWill-o'-the-Wisp changes to 1 use per turn", "The Huppermage can save 3 runes onto their Will-o'-the-Wisp, provided they have exactly I rune. In return, the Will-o'-the-wisp spell can only be used once per turn."], "b:Huppermage:Soul Initiative": ["", "If Heart of Light is the first spell cast\nduring turn: {Caster} {AP} 2 AP\n\nElemental masteries other than that of Heart of Light are set to 0", "The Huppermage gains 2 AP for the current turn if the first spell they cast is Heart of Light."], "b:Huppermage:Elemental Combination": ["", "If {Caster} generates a Nemesis Rune on last rune generated:\n{Icon Arrow} Abundance (+15 Lvl.)\n\nAbundance is limited to 60 levels", "The Huppermage increases the abilities of their Light spells by creating elemental combinations."], "b:Huppermage:Runic Transcendence": ["", "If {Caster} has all 4 runes:\n{Icon Arrow} {Caster} QB gains are doubled\n\nOtherwise:\n{Icon Arrow} {Caster} QB gains are halved", "The Huppermage doubles their QB regeneration when they have all their runes. Otherwise, their regeneration is halved."], "b:Masqueraider:Fracture": ["{AP} 3", "{Element Fire} damage: 3-91 {Area SmallT}\n\nIncurable and Crumbly (Lvl.3) {Area SmallT}", "A simple yet effective spell that causes damage in an area of effect and reduces the protection and heals received by enemies.", "Fire"], "b:Masqueraider:Whipkick": ["{AP} 3", "{Element Fire} Damage: 3-83\n\nTurns the target to face away\n(If the target is already facing away, pushes 1 cell)", "This spell inflicts damage and turns the target around so that its back faces the caster.", "Fire"], "b:Masqueraider:Unhinging": ["{AP} 3", "{Enemy} {Element Fire} Damage: 3-98 {Size: 1-1 x 1-1}\n\n{Ally} Unhinging (+10 Lvl.) {Size: 1-1 x 1-1}", "This spell inflicts damage on enemies in an area of effect. If there are allies in the damage area, they receive a damage bonus.", "Fire"], "b:Masqueraider:Neurosis": ["{AP} 4\n{WP} 1", "Cast on {Ally}:\n{Icon Arrow} {Ally} Flaming (Lvl 5-152)\n{Icon Arrow} Attracts aligned {Target} by 3 cells (max 4 cells)\n\nCast on {Enemy}:\n{Icon Arrow} Damage: 5-176\n{Icon Arrow} Scalded (Lvl 4)", "Depending on the target, this spell can pull enemies in around an ally, or inflict considerable single-target damage on an enemy.", "Fire"], "b:Masqueraider:Capering": ["{AP} 6", "Along the path:\n{Icon Arrow} {Enemy} {Element Fire} Damage: 6-153 (melee)\n{Icon Arrow} {Ally} {Armor} 5-2,398 armor\n\nTeleports to the cell", "The Masqueraider teleports several cells away, dealing damage along the way. If any allies are in their path, those allies gain armor.", "Fire"], "b:Masqueraider:Armature": ["{AP} 4", "{Ally} {Lock} 1 Lock (1 turn)\n\n{Ally} {Armor} 4-2,038 Armor", "This spell gives a good amount of Armor and Lock to an ally to help them appreciate the joys of melee fighting.", "Water"], "b:Masqueraider:Sign": ["{AP} 2", "{Enemy} {Element Water} Damage: 2-70\n\n{Ally} {Element Water} Healing: 4-35", "This flexible spell can heal an ally or inflict damage on an enemy.", "Water"], "b:Masqueraider:Deliverance": ["{AP} 3", "In {Size: 3}:\n{Icon Arrow} {Enemy} {Element Water} Damage: 3-76\n{Icon Arrow} {Ally} {Element Water} Healing: 6-42\n{Icon Arrow} {Ally} {Dodge} 15-88 Dodge", "Deliverance is an area-of-effect spell. It inflicts damage on enemies, and allies in the area of effect are healed and gain Dodge for one turn.", "Water"], "b:Masqueraider:Manhunt": ["{AP} 5", "{Enemy} {Element Water} Damage: 5-139 {Size: 1}\n\n{Ally} {Element Water} Healing: 10-88 {Size: 1}", "This spell has an area of effect: It inflicts damage on enemies and heals allies.", "Water"], "b:Masqueraider:Sarabande": ["{AP} 5\n{WP} 1", "{Enemy} {Element Water} Damage: 6-197\n{Enemy} {WP} -1 WP\n\n{Ally} {Element Water} Healing: 12-119\n{Ally} {Elemental Resistance} 50 Elemental Resistance", "When cast on an enemy, the Masqueraider inflicts damage and may remove one Wakfu Point. On an ally, they heal him.", "Water"], "b:Masqueraider:Fugue": ["{AP} 3", "{Enemy} {Element Air} Damage: 3-98\n\nMoves away and pushes 1 cell", "The Masqueraider inflicts damage on a target, then moves back I cell while pushing it back.", "Air"], "b:Masqueraider:Pursuit": ["{MP} 2", "{Enemy} {Element Air} Damage: 1-30\n\nPushes 2 cell, then follows", "Pursuit is used to push the target back and chase after them so they can't get away.", "Air"], "b:Masqueraider:Somersault": ["{AP} 2", "Attracts by 1 cell", "The Masqueraider pulls the target and slips behind their back.", "Air"], "b:Masqueraider:Cavalcade": ["{AP} 2", "{Enemy} {Element Air} Damage: 2-51\n\n{Target} Cavalcade", "Cavalcade can link the Masqueraider to a target. They can then pull the target with them.", "Air"], "b:Masqueraider:Dislocation": ["{AP} 4\n{WP} 1", "Switches places\n\n{Enemy} {Element Air} Damage: 4-131", "The Masqueraider leaps toward their target and switches places with the target.", "Air"], "b:Masqueraider:Masked Spirit": ["{AP} 4\n{WP} 1", "Summons a Masked Spirit (40% of the Masqueraider's max HP)\n{Icon Arrow} Copies the Masqueraider's characteristics\n{Icon Arrow} Has 6 AP + the Masqueraider's unused AP (max 6)\n{Icon Arrow} Has 6 WP\n{Icon Arrow} The Masqueraider also receives any Damage received by their Spirit\n{Icon Arrow} Cannot lock", "The power of masks can be used to summon a copy of oneself. Be careful, though. The Masqueraider also suffers the damage received by their Masked Spirit (except for damage causing the death of the Masked Spirit).", "Neutral"], "b:Masqueraider:Inspiring Dance": ["{AP} 3", "Inspiring Dance (state lasts 2 turns)\n\nAt start of turn:\n{Icon Arrow} {MP} 2 MP (1 turn)\n{Icon Arrow} 4% of the target's max HP in Armor", "This spell applies a state that boosts an ally's (or the Masqueraider's) mobility and protection for two turns.", "Neutral"], "b:Masqueraider:Dance of Death": ["{AP} 2\n{WP} 1", "Cast on KO'd {Ally}:\n{Icon Arrow} Revives the {Ally} with 30% max HP\n{Icon Arrow} {Ally} In Recovery (Lvl 1), {AP} 2 AP (1 turn)", "A simple dance, or a deadly ritual? Nobody knows for sure. Either way, the Masqueraider's Dance of Death can revive allies.", "Neutral"], "b:Masqueraider:Acrobatics": ["{AP} 3", "Teleports the Masqueraider to a cell next to a fighter\n{Caster} {Elemental Resistance} 50 Elemental Resistance", "The Masqueraider teleports to an empty cell next to an allied or enemy fighter. They also gain resistances until the next turn.", "Neutral"], "b:Masqueraider:Brutality Aura": ["{AP} 2", "Brutality Aura\n{Damage Inflicted} 20% damage inflicted", "The Masqueraider is surrounded by a Brutality Aura. Adjacent allies inflict more damage on their opponents.", "Neutral"], "b:Masqueraider:Solidity": ["{AP} 1\n{WP} 1", "Stabilized (1 turn)\n{Armor} Armor with 10% of the caster's max HP", "The Masqueraider stabilizes their target. The target is immune to all movement effects (teleportation, pushback, etc.) for 1 turn. Also, the Masqueraider gains Armor.", "Neutral"], "b:Masqueraider:Masks Off": ["", "Changing masks regenerates 2 AP\n(1 time per turn)", "The Masqueraider regains 2 AP when they start wearing a mask different from the one they already have."], "b:Masqueraider:Fancy Footwork": ["", "Dodge gain: 200% of level\n\nFor each time the Masqueraider dodges\n{Icon Arrow} {MP} 1 MP (max 3 per turn)\n\n{Elemental Resistance} -50 Elemental Resistance", "The Masqueraider gains mobility but loses resistance."], "b:Masqueraider:Violent Pushes": ["", "Collisions normally reduce AP", "\"Dopu\" was a famous Masqueraider specializing in collisions. He pushed his opponents around so much that they took pushback damage. An ancestral art that was thought to have been lost since the Dofus Era..."], "b:Masqueraider:Artful Locker": ["", "1 Melee Mastery for 2 Lock\n\nMax: 200% of level", "The Masqueraider gains melee damage based on their Lock."], "b:Masqueraider:Health Mask": ["", "When attacking a target from the front:\n{Icon Arrow} Steals 50% of damage inflicted", "This passive gives the Masqueraider a health-stealing ability on targets they attack from the front."], "b:Masqueraider:Carnival": ["", "Masks do not cost WP\n\nMasks take 4 turns to recast", "Masks do not consume WP but they have a shared recast time of 4 turns."], "b:Masqueraider:Unique Armor": ["", "100% Armor given on targets with no Armor\n\nOtherwise, -50% Armor given", "This passive significantly strengthens the Armor given to a target that has none at all. Giving Armor in the right situation is an art."], "b:Masqueraider:Anchor": ["", "At start of fight:\n{Icon Arrow} Lock doubled\n\n{MP} -1 max MP", "The Masqueraider increases their Lock to keep opponents in close combat but loses mobility in exchange."], "b:Masqueraider:Brute": ["", "{Damage Inflicted} 25% damage inflicted\n-40% Armor received, -40% Armor given", "The Masqueraider specializes in dealing damage, and inflicts more damage on their opponents. In exchange, their ability to give and receive Armor is reduced."], "b:Masqueraider:Cautious Protector": ["", "At end of turn, if the Masqueraider has not performed any heals:\n{Icon Arrow} 30% Heals performed and 1 Range (1 turn)\n\nAt end of turn, if the Masqueraider performed a heal:\n{Icon Arrow} -20% heals performed (1 turn)", "With this passive, the amount of healing provided varies depending on the Masqueraider's recent actions. Heals increase if the Masqueraider didn't heal anyone on the previous turn, and decrease if they did heal someone on the previous turn."], "b:Masqueraider:Support Collisions": ["", "If they collide:\n{Icon Arrow} Applies Critical Bonus on an {Ally} ally\n\n{Heart percent} --30% Heals received", "The Masqueraider increases their support potential through collisions. Add a dash of crash and smash!"], "b:Masqueraider:Erosion": ["", "{Damage Inflicted} -25% damage inflicted\n\nModifies the effects of Psychopath Mask II\n{Icon Arrow} When the Masqueraider casts a spell on an enemy:\n{Icon Arrow} -15 Resistance for each spell AP/MP (1 turn)\n{Icon Arrow} -30% Resistance for each spell WP (1 turn)", "Changes the Psychopath Mask so that the Masqueraider's spells remove resistance from opponents, specifically from the direct target of the spell. The resistance is removed before the spell's effects (damage, etc.) are applied. In exchange, the Masqueraider's offensive ability is reduced."], "b:Masqueraider:Pirouette": ["", "25% damage inflicted from the side\n\n-25% damage inflicted from the front", "Increases damage from the side but reduces damage from the front."], "b:Masqueraider:Regenerating Collisions": ["", "Collision healing on {Ally} allies:\n{Icon Arrow} {Element Fire}{Element Water}{Element Air} healing: 1-8 per spell AP\n{Icon Arrow} Healing element depends on the spell\n\n-30 Armor received", "Collisions gain a healing effect. You have to push an obstacle into another one, and if allies are involved, they will receive healing."], "b:Masqueraider:Mirrors": ["", "The Masqueraider switches places with the direct target of a spell cast in melee\n{Icon Arrow} Once per target and per turn", "The Masqueraider switches places with the direct target of a spell cast in melee. The Masqueraider cannot switch places if they are being carried or stabilized."], "b:Masqueraider:Keep in Contact": ["", "At end of turn, if adjacent to at least one fighter:\n{Icon Arrow} 15% damage inflicted (1 turn)\n{Icon Arrow} 75 Elemental Resistance (1 turn)\n\nOtherwise:\n{Icon Arrow} -10% damage inflicted (1 turn)", "The Masqueraider increases their damage and resistance abilities if they stay adjacent to a fighter (allied or enemy). If they move away and finish their turn in an isolated position, they have a penalty instead."], "b:Masqueraider:Artful Dodger": ["", "1 Distance Mastery for 2 Dodge\n\nMax: 200% of level", "The Masqueraider gains ranged damage based on their Dodge."], "b:Masqueraider:Masked Gaze": ["", "{MP} 1 MP\n\n+1 Minimum Range for elemental spells", "The Masqueraider gains mobility, but can no longer cast any spells on adjacent cells."], "b:Masqueraider:Debuff Pushes": ["", "-1 MP on a collision with an {Enemy} enemy\n{Icon Arrow} Can be triggered 3 times per target per turn\n\n{Range} -2 Range", "Any pushback causing a collision will reduce MP. Useful for Masqueraiders who want to reduce their opponents' mobility."], "b:Cra:Fulminating Arrow": ["{AP} 3", "{Element Fire} Damage: 3-98\n\nPrecision Shot: {Element Fire} Damage: 4-131\n{Icon Arrow} Consumes 45 Precision", "Inflicts considerable Fire damage on the target. This spell generates 30 Sharpening and Precision.", "Fire"], "b:Cra:Burning Arrow": ["{AP} 2", "{Element Fire} Damage: 2-60 {Size: 1}\n{Icon Arrow} {Element Fire} Damage: 4-121 on summons {Size: 1}\n\nPrecision Shot: {Element Fire} Damage: 6-182 on summons \n{Icon Arrow} Consumes 30 Precision", "Inflicts Fire damage in a cross-shaped area of effect. The spell inflicts double damage on targeted summons. This spell generates 20 Sharpening and Precision.", "Fire"], "b:Cra:Flaming Arrow": ["{AP} 4", "In a 5-cell vertical line {Area Vline}:\n{Icon Arrow} {Element Fire} Damage: 4-121\n{Icon Arrow} {Enemy} Scalded (Lvl 3)\n\nPrecision Shot: {Enemy} Scalded (Lvl 5)\n{Icon Arrow} Consumes 60 Precision", "Inflicts damage in an area of effect, hitting 5 cells in a vertical line from the cell where the spell is cast. In addition, enemies hit by this spell take greater indirect damage (poisons, traps, etc.) for one turn. This spell generates 40 Sharpening and Precision.", "Fire"], "b:Cra:Blazing Arrow": ["{AP} 2", "Steals 1 MP\n{Element Fire} Damage: 2-60\n\nPrecision Shot: Steals 2 MP\n{Icon Arrow} Consumes 30 Precision", "Steals 1 MP from the target. This spell generates 20 Sharpening and Precision.", "Fire"], "b:Cra:Explosive Arrow": ["{AP} 5\n{WP} 1", "{Element Fire} Damage: 5-139 {Size: 2}\n\nPrecision Shot: {Element Fire} Damage: 7-195 {Size: 2}\n{Icon Arrow} Consumes 80 Precision", "Inflicts heavy Fire damage in a 2-cell circle. This spell generates 60 Sharpening and Precision.", "Fire"], "b:Cra:Lashing Arrow": ["{AP} 3", "{Element Earth} Damage: 3-76\n{MP} -3 MP\n\nPrecision Shot: {MP} -5 MP\n{Icon Arrow} Consumes 45 Precision", "Reduces the target's MP. This spell generates 30 Sharpening and Precision.", "Earth"], "b:Cra:Raining Arrows": ["{AP} 4", "{Element Earth} Damage: 4-141\n\nAt start of next turn:\n{Icon Arrow} The spell is replicated on the last cell it was cast on\n{Icon Arrow} 75% of original spell's damage\n\nPrecision Shot: The spell is replicated 2 times\n{Icon Arrow} Consumes 60 Precision", "Inflicts Earth damage. At the start of the Cra's next turn, the spell is replicated on the targeted cell. This will inflict additional damage if the target has not moved, for example. This spell generates 40 Sharpening and Precision.", "Earth"], "b:Cra:Riddling Arrow": ["{AP} 3\n{WP} 1", "{Element Earth} Damage: 3-105 and applies {Enemy} Riddled (Lvl 1-13)\nWhen the Cra consumes 15 Precision:\n{Icon Arrow} {Element Earth} damage: 1-13 (direct)\n\nPrecision Shot: {Enemy} Riddled (Lvl 1-25)\n{Icon Arrow} Consumes 60 Precision", "In addition to the damage inflicted by this spell, the Cra marks their target and inflicts damage on it each time they consume Precision. This spell generates 40 Sharpening and Precision.", "Earth"], "b:Cra:Piercing Arrow": ["{AP} 5", "{Element Earth} damage: 5-139\n\n2 rebounds in 3-cell {Area Circle}:\n{Icon Arrow} 1st: {Element Earth} damage: 6-167\n{Icon Arrow} 2nd: {Element Earth} damage: 7-195\n\nPrecision Shot: Adds 2 rebounds: {Element Earth} damage: 8-223\n{Icon Arrow} Consumes 75 Precision", "The damage from this spell is inflicted as rebounds. If the spell targets an enemy A, the spell rebounds to an enemy B within 3 cells or less from enemy A. It then rebounds again to an enemy C within 3 cells or less from fighter B. Beacons can be triggered using this spell. This spell generates 50 Sharpening and Precision.", "Earth"], "b:Cra:Destructive Arrow": ["{AP} 6\n{WP} 1", "{Element Earth} Damage: 10-295\n\nPrecision Shot: {Element Earth} Damage: 11-353\n{Icon Arrow} Consumes 105 Precision", "Inflicts heavy Earth damage. This spell generates 70 Sharpening and Precision.", "Earth"], "b:Cra:Homing Arrow": ["{AP} 2", "{Enemy} {Element Air} Damage: 2-55\n\nPrecision Shot: The spell no longer requires line of sight\n{Icon Arrow} Consumes 30 Precision", "This spell has a very long range. It can also pass through obstacles if the Cra is in Precision Shot. This spell generates 20 Sharpening and Precision.", "Air"], "b:Cra:Retreat Arrow": ["{AP} 3\n{WP} 1", "{Element Air} Damage: 4-121\nPushes back 3 cells\n\nPrecision Shot: Pushes back 6 cells\n{Icon Arrow} Consumes 60 Precision", "Repels the target by several cells. This spell generates 40 Sharpening and Precision.", "Air"], "b:Cra:Storm Arrow": ["{AP} 3", "{Element Air} Damage: 3-91 {Area SmallT}\n\nPrecision Shot: {Element Air} Damage: 4-121 {Area SmallT}\n{Icon Arrow} Conumes 45 Precision\n\nArea of Effect is larger as a diagonal", "Inflicts Air damage in a cone-shaped area of effect. This spell generates 30 Sharpening and Precision.", "Air"], "b:Cra:Plaguing Arrow": ["{AP} 4", "{Element Air} Damage: 4-111\nPlaguing Arrow (+50 Lvl.)\n{Icon Arrow} 50% damage inflicted by the next Plaguing Arrow\n{Icon Arrow} Max 100%, is then removed\n\nPrecision Shot: Damage penetrates Armor\n{Icon Arrow} consumes 45 Precision", "This spell does not require line of sight. It can pass through obstacles to inflict damage on hidden targets. This spell generates 40 Sharpening and Precision.", "Air"], "b:Cra:Static Arrow": ["{AP} 5\n{WP} 1", "{Element Air} Damage: 6-182\n\nIf the Cra hasn't used MP to move around on their turn:\n{Icon Arrow} Additional {Element Air} damage: 2-60\n\nPrecision Shot: Additional {Element Air} damage: 4-121\n{Icon Arrow} Consumes 90 Precision", "Repels the target by several cells. This spell generates 40 Sharpening and Precision.", "Air"], "b:Cra:Roly-Poly": ["{WP} 2", "{Caster} Teleports to the cell\n{MP} 1 MP", "Rolls to the targeted cell. The Cra can use this spell to escape from an enemy that was locking them, or move to a more favorable position to inflict damage.", "Neutral"], "b:Cra:Beacon Sneakin'": ["{AP} 2", "{Caster} teleports to the targeted cell", "Teleports to the targeted cell, if the targeted cell is adjacent to one of the Cra's Beacons.", "Neutral"], "b:Cra:Scout": ["{AP} 2", "{Damage Inflicted} 20% damage inflicted (2 turns)\n\nConverts all Precision into Sharpening", "The caster gains damage and converts all their Precision into Sharpening.", "Neutral"], "b:Cra:Bat's Eye": ["{MP} 2\n{WP} 1", "Cast on the Cra:\n{Icon Arrow} {Ally} 4 Range (2 turns) {Size: 1}\n\nOtherwise:\n{Icon Arrow} {Enemy} -4 Range (2 turns) {Size: 1}", "Removes Range from enemies in an area of effect. Their spells can hit less distant targets. However, if the spell is cast on the Cra, they and their adjacent allies gain 4 Range.", "Neutral"], "b:Cra:Biting Blow": ["{AP} 2", "Stabilized (1 turn)\nIncurable (Lvl 4) (1 turn)", "Stabilizes the target, which therefore cannot be pushed, attracted, teleported or carried for 1 turn. In addition, healing received by the target will decrease for 1 turn.", "Neutral"], "b:Cra:Flurry": ["{AP} 1\n{WP} 1", "Unlocks 3 charges of Luminous Arrow (max 5)", "The Cra unlocks 3 luminous arrows to use whenever needed. Light damage draws on the element of the caster's best mastery.", "Neutral"], "b:Cra:Devious Archer": ["", "Sharpened Arrowhead gives Luminous Arrow (+1 lvl.)\n\nLuminous Arrow\n{Icon Arrow} The spell's range becomes non-modifiable\n{Icon Arrow} Does not trigger Sharpened Arrowhead", "Each Sharpened Arrowhead that the Cra gains gives them a Luminous Arrow. In exchange, the Luminous Arrow spell will now have non-modifiable range."], "b:Cra:Scout Specialty": ["", "Evasive heals 25% of missing HP\n\nIncreases the size of the Evasive area of effect by 1\n{Icon Arrow} (Reduced by 1 if Cra's Paradox is equipped)", "The Evasive state heals the Cra's missing HP. However, the area required to be Evasive becomes larger."], "b:Cra:Discreet Beacons": ["", "Beacons become transparent\n\nBeagon:\n{Icon Arrow} Pushes aligned fighters back 2 cells if they are within 5 cells of the Beacon", "Cra Beacons no longer block line of sight. When Beagon is cast, targets aligned with the beacon are pushed back."], "b:Cra:Voracious Precision": ["", "When under Precision Shot:\n{Icon Arrow} 25% health stolen by spells that consume Precision\n\nPrecision Shot now limited to 1 use per turn", "When the Cra is affected by Precision Shot, their spells that consume Precision steal 25% of the damage inflicted. However, Precision Shot can only be cast once per turn."], "b:Cra:Sharp Mind": ["", "On entering Precision Shot:\n{Icon Arrow} {Caster} Sharpening (Lvl. 50)\n\nPrecision's max level becomes 200", "The Cra gains Sharpening when they cast their Precision Shot. However, they can no longer increase their Precision level above 200."], "b:Cra:Hunter's Instinct": ["", "Single-target spells trigger Beacons in a new way (per spell AP)\n\n{Element Fire} -10% Critical Hit in a 2-to-3-cell ring\n{Element Air} Pushes {Target} aligned with the Beacon by 1 cell (3 cells)\n{Element Earth} -5% of the Cra's max HP in Armor removal in a square\n\nThe distance between Beacons is increased by 5 cells instead of 3", "The Cra's single-target spells have different effects on their Beacons. In exchange, their Beacons must be spaced farther apart when placed."], "b:Cra:The Way of the Bow": ["", "For each MP removed on a successful MP removal, applies\n{Icon Arrow} Sharpening and Precision (10 levels)\n\nEvasive no longer applies Sharpening or Precision", "When the Cra removes MP from a target, they generate Precision and Sharpening. They no longer gain any at end of turn when Evasive."], "b:Cra:Massive Beagon": ["", "Beagon now has 0 Range and 2-turn cooldown\n\nThe spell's effect becomes:\n{Icon Arrow} Destroys all the Cra's Beacons\n\nFor each Beacon destroyed:\n{Icon Arrow} Sharpening (Lvl. 30)\n{Icon Arrow} Precision (Lvl. 30)", "The Beagon spell immediately destroys all the Cra's beacons to generate Sharpening and Precision."], "b:Cra:Ballistic Analysis": ["", "-100% to damage redirect by Beacons onto {Ally} allies\n{Icon Arrow} Beacons give 1 Range (1 turn, 1 per turn) to affected allies\n\nThe Cra can only have one beacon per element on the field", "Beacons' redirected damage is no longer applied to allies; in addition, allies hit by a Beacon gain 1 Range. However, the Cra can now only summon one beacon in each element."], "b:Cra:Cra's Paradox": ["", "Evasive\n{Icon Arrow} The area is triggered if an {Enemy} enemy is within 3 cells or less of the {Caster} Cra", "To be able to acquire the Evasive bonus, the Cra must have at least one enemy within 3 cells or less."], "b:Cra:Untouchable Scout": ["", "{Force of Will} 20 Force of Will\n\nAt start of fight:\n{Icon Arrow} The Cra's Dodge is reduced to 0", "The Cra gains Force of Will. In return, their Dodge is reduced to 0 at the start of the fight."], "b:Cra:Lone Shooter": ["", "When Evasive is level 40 or more:\n{Icon Arrow} 1 MP\n{Icon Arrow} 2 Range\n\nThe Cra no longer triggers Evasive when they have an ally around them", "The Cra can gain bonuses when Evasive reaches level 40 or higher. However, the state also requires that there be no allies around the Cra."], "b:Cra:Short-Range Beaconing": ["", "Beagon becomes free\n\nThe range of spells that summon Beacons is no longer modifiable", "The Cra can remove their Beacons for free. However, the summoning range of the Beacons can no longer be modified."], "b:Cra:Firm Stance": ["", "Once per turn, when Sharpened Arrowhead is applied:\nPrecision Shot:\n{Icon Arrow} 2 AP\n{Icon Arrow} -2 MP\nOtherwise:\n{Icon Arrow} -2 AP\n{Icon Arrow} 2 MP", "Each Sharpened Arrowhead that the Cra gains gives them a Luminous Arrow. In exchange, the Luminous Arrow spell will now have non-modifiable range."], "b:Cra:Focal Distance": ["", "+2 min and max Range for elemental spells", "The Cra can naturally cast their elemental spells 2 cells farther. In return, the minimum range of their elemental spells also increases by 2."], "b:Cra:The Art of Beacons": ["", "Beacons now cost 2 AP 1 WP\n{Icon Arrow} 1 WP is Sharpened Beacon\n\nspells to summon Beacons are now without line of sight", "Beacons can be cast without line of sight but cost 1 WP more."], "b:Cra:Protective Point": ["", "At end of turn, if the Cra has Sharpening:{Icon Arrow} {Caster} {Elemental Resistance} 1 Elemental Resistance per level\n{Icon Arrow} Consumes Sharpening", "If the Cra ends their turn with Sharpening that state is consumed to give the Cra elemental resistance for the following turn."], "b:Cra:Cra Perforation": ["", "When Sharpened Arrowhead is consumed:\n{Icon Arrow} If the spell cast is elemental, single-target and straight-line:\n{Icon Arrow} If spell hits a target, the area of effect becomes a 3-cell {Area Vline}\n\nSharpened Arrowhead no longer gives damage inflicted", "When the Cra has the Sharpened Arrowhead, their next single-target spell runs through the target and inflicts damage in a straight line. In return, their Sharpened Arrowhead no longer gives them damage inflicted."], "b:Cra:Diverging Fire": ["", "On consuming Sharpened Arrowhead, once per turn per target:\n{Icon Arrow} {Caster} -2 MP\n{Icon Arrow} {Target} -2 MP", "Each Sharpened Arrowhead that the Cra gains gives them a Luminous Arrow. In exchange, the Luminous Arrow spell will now have non-modifiable range."], "b:Iop:Thunderbolt": ["{AP} 3", "{Element Fire} Damage: 3-93\n{Enemy} Lost (Lvl 2-55)\n{Icon Arrow} When the {Caster} Iop reaches 100 Concentration\n{Icon Arrow} {Element Fire} damage: 2-55\n\n{Caster} Concentration (+15 Lvl.)", "Inflicts damage on the target and applies the Lost state to it. When the lop reaches 100 Concentration, the Lost state inflicts extra damage.", "Fire"], "b:Iop:Celestial Sword": ["{AP} 2", "{Enemy} {Element Fire} Damage: 2-65 {Area Hline}\n{Icon Arrow} 25% extra damage on targets 65% current HP or higher\n\n{Caster} Concentration (+10 Lvl.)", "Inflicts area-of-effect damage; damage is greater on targets at full health.", "Fire"], "b:Iop:Super Iop Punch": ["{AP} 4", "{Element Fire} Damage: 4-141\n\nIf this spell kills a fighter, {Caster} regains 2 {AP} and Concentration (+50 Lvl.)\n\n{Caster} Concentration (+20 Lvl.)", "This spell inflicts damage. When this spell kills a target, the lop recovers action points (AP) and Concentration. Concentration is a state that allows the lop to regenerate Wakfu points (WP) and inflict more damage.", "Fire"], "b:Iop:Judgment": ["{AP} 1", "Cast on an enemy {Enemy}:\n{Icon Arrow} {Element Fire} Damage: 1-30\n{Icon Arrow} Judgment (Lvl 15)\n{Icon Arrow} The next Fire {Element Fire} spell suffered by the state bearer inflicts 15% extra damage\n\nCast on an ally {Ally}:\n{Icon Arrow} Preparation (+10 Lvl.)\n\n{Caster} Concentration (+5 Lvl.)", "Inflicts damage on an enemy and makes them vulnerable to the next Fire damage suffered. If cast on an ally, increases the damage of the ally's next spell.", "Fire"], "b:Iop:Iop's Wrath": ["{AP} 6\n{WP} 1", "{Element Fire} Damage: 6-182 {Area Ring}\n{Enemy} Concentration (Lvl. 3-91) {Area Circle}\n{Icon Arrow} When the {Caster} Iop reaches 100 Concentration:\n{Icon Arrow} {Element Fire} damage: 3-91\n\n{Caster} Concentration (+40 Lvl.)", "Inflicts damage all around the lop, applying the Lost state to affected enemies. When the lop reaches 100 Concentration, the Lost state inflicts extra damage.", "Fire"], "b:Iop:Shaker": ["{AP} 2", "{Enemy} {Element Earth} Damage: 2-70\n{Enemy} Shaken\n{Icon Arrow} Increases damage suffered on {Armor} Armor by 30%\n\n{Caster} Concentration (+10 Lvl.)", "Inflicts damage on the target and applies the Shaken state to it. Armor losses are increased by 30% for 1 turn.", "Earth"], "b:Iop:Rocknoceros": ["{AP} 4", "{Element Earth} Damage: 4-121, penetrates Armor\n{Icon Arrow} Target loses the same amount of {Armor} Armor\n\n{Caster} Concentration (+20 Lvl.)", "Inflicts damage on the target. If the target has Armor, this spell inflicts an extra loss of Armor on it.", "Earth"], "b:Iop:Cleaver": ["{AP} 3", "In a cross {Area Cross} area of effect:\n{Icon Arrow} {Enemy} {Element Earth} Damage: 2-55\n{Icon Arrow} {Ally} {Armor} 1-20 {Element Earth} Armor and {Block} 25% Block (1 turn)\n\nPer target hit:\n{Icon Arrow} {Caster} {Armor} 1-20 {Element Earth} Armor\n\n{Caster} Concentration (+15 Lvl.)", "This area-of-effect spell is versatile; within a cross-shaped area of effect, enemies suffer damage, and allies gain Armor and Block. And for every ally or enemy target hit, the lop gains Armor.", "Earth"], "b:Iop:Charge": ["{AP} 1", "This spell's cost is variable\n\nFor each cell away from the target (min. 1):\n{Icon Arrow} Charge costs {AP} 1 extra AP\n{Icon Arrow} {Enemy} {Element Earth} Damage: 1-30\n{Icon Arrow} {Caster} Comes right up to the target\n{Icon Arrow} {Caster} Concentration (+5 Lvl.)\n\n{Enemy} Current Charge", "The lop comes right up to their target before inflicting damage on it. Charge inflicts more damage if cast on the same target several turns in a row.", "Earth"], "b:Iop:Devastate": ["{AP} 5", "{Caster} Teleports to the cell\n{Element Earth} Damage: 5-164 {Area Square}\n\n{Caster} Concentration (+25 Lvl.)\n{Icon Arrow} +5 levels per target hit", "This spell inflicts damage in an area of effect around the lop. If the spell is cast on a free cell, the lop teleports onto it before inflicting damage. Based on the number of targets hit, the lop gains more Concentration.", "Earth"], "b:Iop:Jabs": ["{AP} 3", "{Element Air} Damage: 3-105\n\n{Caster} Concentration (+25 Lvl.)", "This spell boosts the lop's Concentration even more. Concentration is a state that allows the lop to regenerate Wakfu points (WP) and inflict more damage.", "Air"], "b:Iop:Flurry": ["{AP} 1", "{Enemy} {Element Air} Damage: 1-32\nAttracts by 1 cell\n\n{Caster} Concentration (+5 Lvl.)", "The spell's target is drawn to the lop.", "Air"], "b:Iop:Wallop": ["{AP} 2", "{Enemy} {Element Air} Damage: 2-70\n\n{Caster} Concentration (+15 Lvl.)", "This spell boosts the lop's Concentration even more. Concentration is a state that allows the lop to regenerate Wakfu points (WP) and inflict more damage.", "Air"], "b:Iop:Pounding": ["{AP} 4", "{Element Air} Damage: 6-197\n{Icon Arrow} 50% of damage is converted into {Armor} Armor\n\n{Caster} Concentration (+20 Lvl.)", "Inflicts a great deal of Air damage. The target then gains an amount of Armor equal to half of the damage suffered. This Armor cannot be increased or decreased by the Armor Given or Armor Received characteristics.", "Air"], "b:Iop:Sword of Iop": ["{AP} 3", "In a cross {Area Cross} area of effect:\n{Icon Arrow} {Enemy} {Element Air} Damage: 3-83\n{Icon Arrow} {Ally} {Damage Inflicted} 10% damage inflicted (2 turns)\n\n{Caster} Concentration (+15 Lvl.)", "In an area of effect, this spell inflicts minor damage on enemies and increases allies' damage.", "Air"], "b:Iop:Focus": ["{AP} 2", "Stabilized (1 turn)\n{Elemental Resistance} -50 Elemental Resistance (1 turn)\nIncurable (Lvl 5)\nCrumbly (Lvl 5)", "The lop immobilizes the target and reduces the target's resistances, as well as healing and armor received, for 1 turn.", "Neutral"], "b:Iop:Virtue": ["{AP} 2\n{WP} 1", "In a 2-cell {Area Circle} circle:\n{Icon Arrow} {Caster} {Ally} {Element Physical} heals 20% of the caster's max HP {Fixed: The value is not influenced by the caster's damage.}\n\nEffects are applied around the Standard.", "The lop heals themself and allies around them. The healing is also done around the lop's standard.", "Neutral"], "b:Iop:Increase": ["{MP} 2\n{WP} 2", "In a 2-cell {Area Circle} circle:\n{Icon Arrow} {Caster} {Ally} {Damage Inflicted} 15% damage inflicted (2 turns)\n\nPer {Ally} ally hit:\n{Icon Arrow} {Caster} {MP} 1 MP\n\nThis spell is replicated around the Bravery Standard", "The lop increases their damage and that of allies around them. This spell also increases the lop's movement points (MP). The effects are applied around the standard.", "Neutral"], "b:Iop:Duel": ["{AP} 1", "The {Target} turns to face the {Caster}\n\nOn the target {Target} and the {Caster} caster, for 1 turn:\n{Icon Arrow} {Block} -30% Block", "The target turns to face the lop, and both of them have a reduced chance of blocking.", "Neutral"], "b:Iop:Stance": ["{AP} 2\n{WP} 1", "{Armor} {Element Physical} Armor: 1-25\n{Icon Arrow} Armor is based on the element of the last spell cast\n\nBased on the element of the last spell cast, the Iop applies a Stance (1 turn)\n{Icon Arrow} The Stance is triggered on direct damage received\n\n{Element Fire} Counter Stance\n{Icon Arrow} Triggered: {Element Physical} damage: 3-83\n{Icon Arrow} {Caster} 2 WP\n{Icon Arrow} Damage is based on the element of the last spell cast\n{Icon Arrow} Once triggered: {Caster} loses the Stance\n\n{Element Earth} Defensive Stance\n{Icon Arrow} Triggered: Reduces the direct damage suffered by 25% if the Iop has Armor\n{Icon Arrow} When the Iop is out of Armor: {Caster} loses the Stance\n\n{Element Air} Vivacity Stance\n{Icon Arrow} Tirggered: 1 max MP (1)\n{Icon Arrow} With 5 direct damage received: {Caster} loses the Stance", "Applies a stance to the lop. The type of stance is based on the lop's last spell used and is triggered when the lop suffers direct damage.", "Neutral"], "b:Iop:Hour of Glory": ["{AP} 3", "Hour of Glory\nThe Iop's elemental spells have modifiable range\n+2 {Range} min and max range on elemental spells that can be cast at 1 or more Range\n{Melee Mastery} Melee Mastery is converted into {Distance Mastery} Distance Mastery", "This passive lets you switch to Ranged mode for one turn. Elemental spells increase in Range to reach targets farther away.", "Neutral"], "b:Iop:Compulsion": ["", "At start of turn, {Caster} gains a level of Wrath\n\nAt end of turn, {Caster} loses the Wrath state", "The lop gains a level of Wrath at the tart of each turn. However, they lose Wrath at the end of each turn."], "b:Iop:Virility": ["", "HP boost for the Iop:\n{Icon Arrow} {Caster} 300% of their level\n\nJump can no longer be cast without line of sight", "The lop has more health points, but they can no longer use the Jump spell without line of sight (behind obstacles)."], "b:Iop:Duelist": ["", "If facing an enemy when their turn ends:\n{Icon Arrow} Duelist (Lvl 1) on the Iop {Caster} and the enemy {Enemy} (1 turn)", "If the lop ends their turn facing an enemy, both of them gain a large amount of resistance for 1 turn."], "b:Iop:Authority": ["", "When inflicting frontal and straight-line direct damage:\n{Icon Arrow} Attracts the target {Target} 1 cell\n\nWhen inflicted rear and straight-line direct damage:\n{Icon Arrow} Pushes the target {Target} 1 cell (doesn't cause a collision)", "The lop gains the ability to attract or repel targets by attacking them from the front or from behind."], "b:Iop:Mini-jump": ["", "The Jump spell is modified:\n{Icon Arrow} It costs 2 AP and 1 WP\n{Icon Arrow} It can be cast from 1 to 3 Range (non-modifiable)\n{Icon Arrow} It can be used 3 times per turn", "The Jump spell can be used multiple times in a turn and costs less AP. However, its range is reduced, and it costs 1 WP."], "b:Iop:Impetuous": ["", "When the Jump spell is cast:\n{Icon Arrow} {Caster} The AP cost is reimbursed\n{Icon Arrow} {Caster} The AP cost is lost at the start of the next turn", "When the lop uses the Jump spell, its AP cost is refunded. However, the lop will lose the same amount of AP at the start of their next turn."], "b:Iop:Show Off": ["", "At end of turn, per level of Wrath\n{Icon Arrow} {Caster} {WP} 1 WP and 15 Preparation\n\n{Caster} No longer recovers WP at level 100 Concentration", "The lop recovers WP and Preparation at end of turn based on the level of the Wrath state. However, they no longer recover WP instantly with Concentration."], "b:Iop:King of the Hill": ["", "At end of turn, if the Iop is on their standard:\n{Icon Arrow} {Caster} 200% of level as Lock (1 turn)\n{Icon Arrow} {Caster} 50% of level as Flaming\n\nOtherwise: {Caster} loses 100% of their Lock (1 turn)", "The lop gains a large amount of Lock and Flaming ii they end their turn on their standard. However, they lose all their Lock ii they don't end it on their standard"], "b:Iop:Precipitation": ["", "After moving with a spell:\n{Icon Arrow} {Caster} {MP} 1 MP\n{Icon Arrow} {Caster} -25 Elemental Resistance (1 turn, stackable)", "The lop gains 1 MP every time they use one of their spells to move, but they also lose resistances for 1 turn."], "b:Iop:Conquest": ["", "When the Iop {Caster} kills an enemy {Enemy}, a Conquest glyph is placed on the cell\n\nAt end of turn, the Standard is summoned or moved to the Conquest if the cell is free", "When the lop kills an enemy, they place a conquest glyph on this cell. If the cell is free at end of turn, they summon or move their Standard onto the conquest. It they kill an enemy while a conquest glyph is already present, the new glyph replaces the old one."], "b:Iop:Standard Bearer": ["", "The Bravery Standard spell can be cast on self\n\nIf the spell is cast on the Iop {Caster}:\n{Icon Arrow} At end of turn, {Caster} switches to Standard Bearer mode (1 turn)\n{Icon Arrow} Stabilized (1 turn)\n{Icon Arrow} {Caster} Deploys the Bravery Aura in a 2-cell circle\n\nThe Standard has 50% less HP", "The lop can use the Bravery Standard on themself to deploy the Bravery Aura around them at end of turn. In doing so, they become stabilized, and the aura's area of effect is larger. However, the Bravery Standard is more fragile."], "b:Iop:Dissipation": ["", "The Gutting Gust and Uppercut spells gain 2 max Range\n\nCombos no longer give Concentration", "The Gutting Gust and Uppercut spells can be cast at longer range. However, the lop no longer gains Concentration by performing combos."], "b:Iop:Rallying": ["", "When summoning the Standard:\n{Icon Arrow} Attracts surrounding targets {Target} by 2 cells\n\nThe Bravery Standard spell loses 1 Range", "When the lop summons their standard, nearby targets are drawn to the lop. The Bravery Standard spell loses 1 Range."], "b:Iop:Seismic Rift": ["", "Gutting Gust:\n{Icon Arrow} {Dodge} -50% of the Iop's level as Dodge on the target {Target} and the Iop {Caster} (1 turn)\n{Icon Arrow} {Lock} 50% of the Iop's level as Lock on the target {Target} and the Iop {Caster} (1 turn)", "Gutting Gust removes Dodge and gives\nLock to the target and the lop."], "b:Iop:Outpost": ["", "Bravery Standard no longer has a line of sight\n\nThe Standard is destroyed if the Iop {Caster} jumps on it", "The lop can use the Bravery Standard spell without line of sight (through obstacles). However, the Standard is destroyed if the lop uses it to jump on top oi it."], "b:Iop:Hit and Run": ["", "On consuming Wrath:\n{Icon Arrow} {Caster} {MP} 1 MP per level of Wrath\n\nWrath can only be consumed starting at level 2", "The lop instantly recovers MP after using their Wrath. However, the Wrath is only triggered at a minimum of level 2."], "b:Iop:The Iop of Wazemmes": ["", "The Iop's spells inflict {Melee Mastery} damage at 1 to 3 Range (instead of 1 to 2 Range)\n\n-20% Armor received", "Damage inflicted by the lop up to a range of 3 cells is considered melee damage. However, they receive less Armor."], "b:Iop:Fortification": ["", "At end of turn, if the Iop {Caster} is on their standard:\n{Icon Arrow} 50% of {Critical Hit} critical hits are converted to {Block} Block (1 turn)\n\nWhile on the Standard:\n{Icon Arrow} {Caster} Each Block restores 5% of missing HP", "If the lop is on their Standard, each successful Block restores some of their HP. Also, if they end on their Standard, half of their Critical Hit is converted to Block until the end of the next turn."], "b:Iop:Destiny": ["", "The Bravery Aura becomes a redirection aura:\n{Icon Arrow} Allies {Ally} in the aura transfer 20% of the damage suffered to the Iop {Caster}\n{Icon Arrow} The aura no longer applies Resistance", "The standard's aura no longer gives resistance; it becomes a redirection aura: Allies within the aura will redirect some of the damage they suffer to the lop."], "b:Enutrof:Meteor": ["{AP} 2\n{WP} 1", "Moves the nearest {Mine} to the targeted cell\n{Enemy}{Element Fire} Damage: 3-83 {Area Cross}", "Inflicts Fire damage on enemies in an area of effect. The Enutrof moves the closest Mine to the targeted cell.", "Fire"], "b:Enutrof:Ember": ["{AP} 3", "{Element Fire} Damage: 1-83 {Area Square}", "Inflicts Fire damage in an area of effect.", "Fire"], "b:Enutrof:Fusion": ["{AP} 3\n{WP} 1", "If the Enutrof is on a {Mine}:\n{Icon Arrow} Moves the {Mine} under the target\nIf the enutrof has the Treasures state and the {Mine} is consumed:\n{Icon Arrow} A new {Mine} is summoned under the Enutrof\n{Icon Arrow} consumes 1 Treasures instead of generating one\n\n{Enemy}{Element Fire} Damage: 4-111", "If the Enutrof is on a Mine, the Mine immediately moves underneath the target and inflicts Fire damage on the target. If the Enutrof also has the Treasures state, they consume the state to immediately summon a new Mine at their position (only if the moved Mine was consumed). In this case, the consumed Mine does not give Treasures to the Enutrof.", "Fire"], "b:Enutrof:Firedamp Explosion": ["{AP} 4", "{Element Fire} Damage: 4-111 {Area Cross}\n\nMust target a {Mine}", "The Enutrof inflicts major damage around one of their Mines. This spell can be cast anywhere on the battlefield, but it must target a Mine.", "Fire"], "b:Enutrof:Hot Magma": ["{AP} 5\n{WP} 1", "Drhellzerker form:\n{Icon Arrow} Teleports to the targeted cell before inflicting damage\n\n{Element Fire} Damage: 6-167 {Area Cross}", "Inflicts major Fire damage in an area of effect. If the Enutrof is in Drhellzerker form and the targeted cell is free, the Enutrof teleports.", "Fire"], "b:Enutrof:Rascalry": ["{AP} 2", "{Element Water} Damage: 2-55\nSteals 1 MP\nIf the target has more MP than the Enutrof\n{Icon Arrow} Steals 2 MP instead", "Inflicts Water damage and steals 1 MP from the target, or 2 MP if the target has more MP than the Enutrof.", "Water"], "b:Enutrof:Purge": ["{AP} 3", "{Element Water} Damage: 4-83\nSteals 1 Range (1 turn)\n\nIf a {Mine} is on the targeted cell:\n{Icon Arrow} Effects now apply in {Area Cross} AoE", "Inflicts Water damage at long range and steals Range from the target. If the Enutrof targets a Mine, the spell's area of effect is increased.", "Water"], "b:Enutrof:Cutting": ["{AP} 3\n{WP} 1", "{Element Water} Damage: 3-105\n{Icon Arrow} Damage quadrupled on summons\n\nIf the Enutrof kills a fighter with this spell:\n{Icon Arrow} Treasures (+1 Lvl.)", "Inflicts Water damage on a target, quadrupled if the target is a summons. If the Enutrof kills their target with this spell, the Enutrof gains the Treasures state.", "Water"], "b:Enutrof:Tax": ["{AP} 4", "{Element Water} Damage: 4-121\n\nIf the Enutrof has Treasures:\n{Icon Arrow} {MP} -4 MP\n{Icon Arrow} Consumes 1 Treasures", "Inflicts Water damage. If the Enutrof has the Treasures state, the state is consumed and nflicts an MP loss on the target.", "Water"], "b:Enutrof:Refinement": ["{AP} 5\n{WP} 2", "{Element Water} Damage: 7-212\n\nIf the Enutrof has the Treasures state:\n{Icon Arrow} {Element Water} Damage: 9-266 instead\n{Icon Arrow} Consumes 1 Treasures", "Inflicts heavy Water damage. If the Enutrof has the Treasures state, the state is consumed to inflict more damage.", "Water"], "b:Enutrof:Shovel of Judgment": ["{AP} 2", "{Element Earth} Damage: 2-65\n\nEnutrof form:\n{Icon Arrow} Blinded (+1 Lvl.)\nDrhellzerker form:\n{Icon Arrow} Damage goes through Armor", "Inflicts Earth damage. If the Enutrof is in Drhellzerker form, the damage passes through Armor and ignores Block. Otherwise, the target loses Range.", "Earth"], "b:Enutrof:Killer Spade": ["{AP} 3", "Enutrof form:\n{Icon Arrow} Pushes back 1 cell\nDrhellzerker form:\n{Icon Arrow} Switches places\n\n{Element Earth} Damage: 3-91", "Pushes the target back in normal form and switches places in Drhellzerker form. Then, inflicts Earth damage.", "Earth"], "b:Enutrof:Shovel Kiss": ["{AP} 3\n{WP} 1", "Enutrof form:\n{Icon Arrow} {MP} -2 MP\nDrhellzerker form:\n{Icon Arrow} Moves closer to the target\n\n{Element Earth} Damage: 4-121", "Inflicts Earth damage. In normal form, this spell removes MP from the target. In Drhellzerker form, the Enutrof moves into close-combat range of the target before inflicting damage.", "Earth"], "b:Enutrof:Shady Shovel": ["{AP} 4", "{Element Earth} Damage: 4-121\n\nEnutrof form:\n{Icon Arrow} -2 AP\nDrhellzerker form:\n{Icon Arrow} Steals 100% of the damage inflicted\nIf the Enutrof has the Treasures state:\n{Icon Arrow} The effects are doubled\n{Icon Arrow} Consmes 1 Treasures", "Inflicts Earth damage. Removes AP from the target in normal form, and steals HP in Drhellzerker form. If the Enutrof has the Treasures state, they consume it to double the spell's secondary effects.", "Earth"], "b:Enutrof:Shovel Shaker": ["{AP} 5\n{WP} 1", "{Element Earth} Damage: 6-167 {Area Vline}\nIf the Drheller is at the edge of the area:\n{Icon Arrow} {Element Earth} Damage: 2-55 extra", "Inflicts damage in a straight line in front of the Enutrof. If their Drheller is at the edge of the area, it replicates the damage on its turn.", "Earth"], "b:Enutrof:Acceleration": ["{AP} 2\n{WP} 1", "{MP} 1 MP (2 turns)\n\nIf the Enutrof has the Treasures state:\n{Icon Arrow} {MP} 2 MP instead (2 turns)\n{Icon Arrow} Consumes 1 Treasures", "Gives 1 MP to the Enutrof or to an ally for two turns. It the Enutrof has the Treasures state, they consume the state to double the bonus.", "Neutral"], "b:Enutrof:Clumsiness": ["{AP} 1", "{MP} -3 MP\nSteals 1 Lock\nSteals 1 Dodge", "Removes MP trom the target and steals Lock and Dodge from it, reducing its mobility and increasing the Enutrof's.", "Neutral"], "b:Enutrof:Miserliness": ["{AP} 2", "Consumes the {Mine}\nGains 50% of the bonus from the {Mine} (1 turn)\nIf the Enutrof has Treasures:\n{Icon Arrow} Obtains 100% of the bonus instead\n{Icon Arrow} Consumes 1 Treasures instead of generating one\n\nMust target a {Mine}", "The Enutrof consumes a Mine at range, allowing them to gain the Treasures state and gain part of the Mine's bonus for 1 turn. If the Enutrof has the Treasures state, they consume the state to gain the Mine's full bonus.", "Neutral"], "b:Enutrof:Prime of Life": ["{AP} 2\n{WP} 1", "{MP} 3 MP (1 turn)\n{Dodge} 6-375 Dodge (1 turn)\n\nIf the Enutrof has the Treasures state:\n{Icon Arrow} {AP} 2 AP in addition (1 turn)\n{Icon Arrow} Consumes 1 Treasures", "Gives a significant MP and Dodge bonus to the Enutrof or an ally for the current turn. If the Enutrof has the Treasures state, they consume the state to grant additional AP.", "Neutral"], "b:Enutrof:Seismic Wealth": ["{AP} 3", "Per {Mine} on the field:\n{Icon Arrow} {Caster} Seismic Wealth (+15 lvl.) (2 turns)\n{Icon Arrow} Consumes the {Mine} and transforms them into Purse", "The Enutrof consumes all of their Mines. Each Mine consumed grants a significant damage bonus to the Enutrof for a period of 2 turns.", "Neutral"], "b:Enutrof:Corruption": ["{AP} 3\n{WP} 1", "{Target} Transparent\n{Ally} {Element Light} Healing: 15-133\n{Enemy} Corruption (2 turns)", "The Enutrof turns a target transparent (no longer blocks line of sight) for 2 turns. If it is an ally, they are healed. If it is an enemy, they suffer a penalty on damage inflicted, heals performed, and armor given.", "Neutral"], "b:Enutrof:Advanced Geology": ["", "On moving a Mine (max 3x per turn):\n{Icon Arrow} {Caster} Recovers 1 AP in normal form\n{Icon Arrow} Heals: 5% of max HP as Drhellzerker\n\nThe Excavation spell's range is no longer modifiable", "The Excavation spell's range is no longer modifiable. In exchange, when the Enutrof moves a Mine, they recover 1 AP if they are in normal form and heal themself if they are in Drhellzerker form."], "b:Enutrof:Treasure Tracker": ["", "Excavation costs 1 MP instead of 1 AP", "The Enutrof uses their MP instead of their AP to move their Mines."], "b:Enutrof:Comprehensive Insurance": ["", "At end of turn\n{Icon Arrow} {Caster} Armor: 8% of max HP per Treasures\n{Icon Arrow} Treasures is consumed", "The Enutrof consumes their Treasures at end of turn to gain Armor."], "b:Enutrof:Trade Secrets": ["", "Purse are immediately Fat Pouch\n\n{Enemy} can pick up Fat Pouch", "Purses summoned by the Enutrot instantly appear as Fat Pouches. However, they can be picked up by enemies."], "b:Enutrof:Enutrof's Blessing": ["", "At start of turn\n{Icon Arrow} {Caster} Treasures (+1 Lvl.)\n\nThe Treasures state is limited to level 2 max", "The Enutrof gains 1 Treasures at start of turn, but can only accumulate up to a maximum of 2 instead of 3."], "b:Enutrof:Market Investments": ["", "The effects of Purse are delayed by 1 turn:\nPurse: Market Investments +1 Lvl\nFat Pouch: Market Investments +2 lvl.\nStackable, level 6 max", "The Excavation spell's range is no longer modifiable. In exchange, when the Enutrof moves a Mine, they recover I AP if they are in normal form and heal themself if they are in Drhellzerker form."], "b:Enutrof:Drhellzertank": ["", "Drhellzerker:\n{Icon Arrow} When moving, gains Vital Preparation instead of Preparation\nBeastliness:\n{Icon Arrow} Gives 30 Elemental Resistance per level\n{Icon Arrow} No longer gives damage inflicted", "The Enutrof exchanges the offensive bonuses of their Drhellzerker form for defensive bonuses."], "b:Enutrof:Credit Interest": ["", "Broke:\n{Icon Arrow} Targets give 1 Treasures to the Enutrof at the start of their turn\n{Icon Arrow} The state lasts 4 turns instead of 2", "With this passive, the Enutrof acquires Treasures from the targets they've left broke. In exchange, the Enutrof can't put them in debt as often."], "b:Enutrof:Greed": ["", "Excavation can be used to pick up Purse\n\n{Caster} can no longer pick up Purse by walking on them", "The Enutrof can no longer pick up Purses by walking on them, but collects them directly with the Excavation spell."], "b:Enutrof:Asynchronous Swap": ["", "In Drhellzerker:\n{Icon Arrow} Meelee Mastery is based on Distance Mastery\n{Icon Arrow} -2 max Range with elemental spells", "The Enutrof copies their distance mastery to melee mastery by switching to Drhellzerker mode. Their elemental spells in Drhellzerker mode lose 2 max Range."], "b:Enutrof:Springboard": ["", "In Drhellzerker:\n{Icon Arrow} Fancy Footwork\n{Icon Arrow} The first dodge each turn is 100% guaranteed\n\nAt the start of the fight, Dodge is reduced to 0", "In Drhellzerker mode, the first dodge\nof the turn is always 100% guaranteed. In exchange, the Enutrof's Dodge is reduced to 0 at the start of the tight."], "b:Enutrof:Age Merchant": ["", "In Drhellzerker:\n{Icon Arrow} Neutral spells cost 1 MP less\n{Icon Arrow} Neutral spells are limited to 3 Range max", "In Drhellzerker mode, the Enutrof's neutral spells are also limited in Range, but they cost 1 MP less."], "b:Enutrof:Pince-Nez": ["", "In Drhellzerker:\n{Icon Arrow} +2 max Range with elemental spells\n{Icon Arrow} Treasures no longer gives WP at end of turn", "When the Enutrof is in Drhellzerker mode, Treasures no longer gives them WP at end of turn, but their elemental spells have a Range bonus."], "b:Enutrof:Mineral Protection": ["", "At end of turn, if the Enutrof is on a {Mine}:\n{Icon Arrow} {Caster} {Elemental Resistance} 100 Elemental Resistance (1 turn)\n{Icon Arrow} The {Mine} is destroyed\n{Icon Arrow} The {Mine} cannot be dug up (1 turn)", "If the Enutrof finishes their turn on a Mine, they destroy it to gain elemental resistances tor 1 turn. The destroyed Mine cannot be dug up tor 1 full turn."], "b:Enutrof:Optimal Focus": ["", "Excavation: +2 min and max range", "The Excavation spell has greater maximum range, but also greater minimum range, preventing the Enutrof from manipulating their Mines at very short range."], "b:Enutrof:Tunneler": ["", "The Drheller teleports to the {Mine} it digs up\n\nThe Drheller has a penalty of -3 max MP", "The Drheller has less MP, but when it digs up a Mine, it teleports onto it."], "b:Enutrof:Inheritance": ["", "At the end of turn, per level of Treasures:\n{Icon Arrow} Drheller: gains 1 AP and 1 MP\n\nThe Drheller dies if it ends its turn in melee range of an enemy", "The Drheller gains AP and MP based on the level of Treasures that the Enutrof has at end of turn. In exchange, the Drheller dies if it ends its turn in melee range of an enemy."], "b:Ecaflip:Loaded Dice": ["{AP} 3", "{Element Fire} Damage: 2-65\n\n{Caster} 50% to inflict a 2nd damage line:\n{Icon Arrow} +1% per level of Lucky Day\n\nIf this spell kills a fighter, {Caster} regains {AP} 2 AP", "This spell's damage is variable. If the Ecailip kills an enemy with it, they gain 2 AP on the next turn.", "Fire"], "b:Ecaflip:Craps": ["{AP} 2", "{Element Fire} Damage: 2-60\n{Ally} Preparation: 1 to 30\n{Caster} Preparation: 1 to 60", "Inflicts Fire damage on enemies and applies Preparation on the Ecaflip. On an ally, the target also receives Preparation. Preparation increases the damage of the next spell.", "Fire"], "b:Ecaflip:D-Six": ["{AP} 6\n{WP} 1", "{Element Fire} Damage: 7-247\n\nEach time the spell is used:\n{Icon Arrow} The next D-Six costs 1 AP less\n{Icon Arrow} Effect is stackable\n{Icon Arrow} Effect is removed when the tarot is shuffled", "The next time this spell is cast, its\ncost is lower.", "Fire"], "b:Ecaflip:Dice Roulette": ["{AP} 4", "{Enemy} {Element Fire} Damage: 4-121 {Size: 3}\n\n{Ally} {Element Fire} Healing: 6-66 {Size: 3}\n{Ally} 5% to 30% damage inflicted {Size: 3}", "This area-of-effect spell is cast around the Ecaflip. It inflicts damage on enemies and heals allies.", "Fire"], "b:Ecaflip:Yowling": ["{AP} 6\n{WP} 1", "{Enemy} {Element Fire} Damage: 6-197 {Area Cross}\n\nPer target hit:\n{Icon Arrow} 5% of max HP as health steal\n{Icon Arrow} 5% of max HP as Armor", "With this AOE spell, the Ecatlip can\nregain health and armor based on the\nnumber of opponents in the area of\n\neffect.", "Fire"], "b:Ecaflip:Rough Tongue": ["{AP} 3", "Attracts by 2 cells\n{Enemy} {Element Water} Damage: 3-98\n{Ally} {Element Water} Healing: 6-53", "Draws the target toward the caster.\nHeals allies and inflicts damage on\n\nenemies.", "Water"], "b:Ecaflip:Up to Scratch": ["{AP} 3", "Along the path (3 -cell line):\n{Icon Arrow} {Enemy} {Element Water} Damage: 3-98 (melee)\n{Icon Arrow} {Ally} {Element Water} Healing: 5-50\n\nTeleports to the cell", "The Ecaflip teleports several cells away, dealing damage along the way. If any allies are in their path, those allies are healed.", "Water"], "b:Ecaflip:Fleahopper": ["{AP} 4", "{Enemy} {Element Water} Damage: 4-111\n\n2 rebounds in 3-cell {Area Circle}:\n{Icon Arrow} 1st: {Enemy} {Element Water} damage: 5-139\n{Icon Arrow} 2nd: {Enemy} {Element Water} damage: 6-167\n\n{Ally} {Element Water} healing: 8-61", "The damage from this spell is inflicted as rebounds. If the spell targets an enemy A, the spell rebounds to an enemy B within 3 cells or less from enemy A. It then rebounds again to an enemy C within 3 cells or less from fighter B. It works the same way it the spell is cast on an ally, but then the spell will do a chain heal.", "Water"], "b:Ecaflip:Paws Off": ["{AP} 2", "Per water spell cast during the turn:\n{Icon Arrow} Pushes by 1 cell\n\n{Enemy} {Element Water} Damage: 2-65\n{Ally} {Element Water} Healing: 4-35", "This spell pushes the target one cell per water spell previously cast in the turn.", "Water"], "b:Ecaflip:Fleeflee": ["{AP} 4", "Cast on an ally {Ally}:\n{Icon Arrow} {MP} 1 MP (1 turn)\n{Icon Arrow} {WP} 1 WP\n{Icon Arrow} {Element Water} Healing: 6-50\n\nCast on an enemy: {Enemy}:\n{Icon Arrow} {WP} -1 WP\n{Icon Arrow} {Element Water} Damage: 4-141", "This super-powerful spell has a different effect depending on the target it is cast on: on an ally, it provides healing and increases MP and WP. On an enemy, however, the spell reduces their WP and health.", "Water"], "b:Ecaflip:Heads or Tails": ["{AP} 3", "Cast on an enemy {Enemy}:\n{Icon Arrow} {Element Earth} Damage: 3-91\n{Icon Arrow} 50% health stolen\n\nCast on an ally {Ally}:\n{Icon Arrow} {Ally} and {Caster}: {Element Earth} Healing: 6-50", "Cast on an enemy, this spell deals damage and heals the Ecaflip tor an amount equal to the HP lost by the target. Cast on an ally, the spell heals the ally and the Ecaflip.", "Earth"], "b:Ecaflip:All In": ["{AP} 1", "Per spell AP (max 10):\n{Icon Arrow} {Element Earth} Damage: 1-19\n\n50% chance to regain the spell's AP cost:\n{Icon Arrow} +5 per card in the discard pile", "This spell uses the Ecaflip's remaining AP (up to 10). The more AP used, the more damage it deals. The Ecaflip then has a 50% chance to recover all AP used by this spell.", "Earth"], "b:Ecaflip:Battle": ["{AP} 4\n{WP} 1", "{Element Earth} Damage: 5-164\nThe Ecaflip has a 50% chance of winning:\n{Icon Arrow} 1% per % HP above their target\n{Icon Arrow} -1% per % HP below their target\n\nIn the event of a win:\n{Icon Arrow} {Caster} {AP} 2 AP\n{Icon Arrow} {Caster} {Critical Hit} 20% Critical Hit (2 turns)\nOtherwise:\n{Icon Arrow} {Caster} {AP} -2 AP", "The Ecaflip plays battle with their target. If the Ecaflip wins, they gain AP and Critical Hit. It they lose, the opposite happens: They lose their current AP. The higher the Ecaflip's HP (as a %) is in relation to their target, the greater their chance of winning the battle.", "Earth"], "b:Ecaflip:All or Nothing": ["{AP} 2", "{Element Earth} Damage: 3-98\n{Caster} The Ecaflip has a 50% chance of also inflicting the damage on themself:\n{Icon Arrow} -1% per % HP below their target\n{Icon Arrow} +1% per % HP above their target", "This spell inflicts heavy damage. However, the Ecaflip has a 50% chance of getting hurt themself. The lower the Ecaflip's HP (as a %) is in relation to their target, the lower their chance of suffering damage.", "Earth"], "b:Ecaflip:Three Cards": ["{AP} 5\n{WP} 1", "{Enemy} {Element Earth} Damage: 6-167 {Size: 3 x 0}\n{Ally} {Element Earth} Healing: 12-92 {Size: 3 x 0}\nPer card in hand:\n{Icon Arrow} {Enemy} damage: 1-27 extra\n{Icon Arrow} {Ally} healing: 2-15 extra\n\nDiscards all cards in hand", "Inflicts Earth damage and heals allies in a straight line. The Ecaflip uses the cards in their hand to increase the spell's effects before discarding them.", "Earth"], "b:Ecaflip:Misadventure": ["", "Adds a tarot card:\n{Icon Arrow} Misadventure", "Unlocks an extra tarot card (added to the draw pile). This card reduces the target's mobility and damage but increases their resistance for one turn."], "b:Ecaflip:Misfortune": ["", "Adds a tarot card:\n{Icon Arrow} Misfortune\n\nAt end of turn, if the card is in the hand:\n{Icon Arrow} 300% of level as Lock (1 turn)", "Unlocks an extra tarot card (added to the draw pile). This tarot card converts the target's Critical Hit into Block, at a rate of one to one, for one turn."], "b:Ecaflip:Ecaflip's Fate": ["", "Adds a tarot card:\n{Icon Arrow} Ecaflip's Fate", "Unlocks an extra tarot card (added to the draw pile). This tarot card inflicts serious damage on the target. However, if the target is still alive the next turn, the Ecaflip takes the same damage."], "b:Ecaflip:Universe": ["", "When Lucky Day reaches exactly 42:\n{Icon Arrow} Unlocks Universe\n\nAt end of turn, if Universe is in the hand:\n{Icon Arrow} Converts the Lucky Day to % max HP as armor\n{Icon Arrow} Universe is removed\n\nLucky Day gains are halved", "Cuts Lucky Day gains in half. Unlocks the Universe card when the Ecaflip reaches exactly 42 Lucky Day (the card is not in the draw pile)."], "b:Ecaflip:Double or Quits": ["{AP} 2", "The Ecaflip plays the next three cards in their draw pile on themself", "This spell draws three tarot cards from the draw pile and immediately plays them on the Ecailip.", "Neutral"], "b:Ecaflip:Topkaj": ["{AP} 3", "Cast on a KO'ed ally:\n{Icon Arrow} Revives the {Ally} with 25% max HP\n{Icon Arrow} {Ally} In Recovery and {MP} 2 MP (2 turns)\n\nCast on the Ecaflip:\n{Icon Arrow} {Ally} Topkaj (Lvl 1) {Area Circle} (2 turns)\n{Icon Arrow} {Ally} {MP} 1 MP {Area Circle} (1 turn)", "If cast on a KO'd ally, this spell revives the ally (an ally can only be revived once per fight) and gives them MP. If cast on the Ecaflip, it gives a bonus to critical hit rate and boosts MP for 2 turns, applied to the Ecaflip and their nearby allies.", "Neutral"], "b:Ecaflip:Felintuition": ["{AP} 2", "Places a {Area Cross} Felintuition glyph\nAt start of turn:\n{Icon Arrow} {Ally} {Element Light} healing: 1-38\n{Icon Arrow} {Ally} 2 Dodge (1 turn)\n{Icon Arrow} {Enemy} {Element Light} Damage: 1-74\n{Icon Arrow} {Enemy} -2 Dodge (1 turn)\n\nAt the start of the Ecaflip's next turn:\n{Icon Arrow} Jumps to the center of the glyph if the cell is open", "Places a glyph that stays on the field for 1 turn. The glyph activates when an allied or enemy fighter starts their turn on it.", "Neutral"], "b:Ecaflip:Life Token": ["{AP} 2\n{WP} 1", "{Ally} Applies Life Token (1 turn)\n\nIf a lethal attack:\n{Icon Arrow} The life token carrier survives with 1 HP\n{Icon Arrow} The life token is removed\n\nIf the carrier still has a life token when the Ecaflip's turn starts:\n{Icon Arrow} The Ecaflip's HP is set to the carrier's HP", "This spell's target gains a life token. The target can survive a lethal attack once per turn. The token lasts tor one turn: if not consumed, on the Ecatlip's next turn, the Ecaflip recovers it and sets their HP to be the same as the spell target's HP.", "Neutral"], "b:Ecaflip:Spell Strike": ["{AP} 1\n{WP} 1", "Cast on {Caster}:\n{Icon Arrow} Draws another discarded card\n{Icon Arrow} Discards all other tarot cards help\n{Icon Arrow} 10% damage inflicted (2 turns) per discarded card\n\nCast on {Enemy}:\n{Icon Arrow} Random {Element Light} damage (1-32 to 4-131)\n{Icon Arrow} Additional effects based on cards in\nhand:\n{Icon Arrow} Black card: 50% health steal\n{Icon Arrow} White card: 50% extra damage", "This spell uses the cards in hand.", "Neutral"], "b:Ecaflip:Clubs": ["{AP} 3", "Pushes adjacent targets by 2 cells\nCast on {Ally}:\n{Icon Arrow} Clubs (2 turns, 1 target max)\n\nCast on {Enemy}:\n{Icon Arrow} Cataplasm (2 turns, 1 target max)", "This spell can help an ally by granting various bonuses or weaken an enemy by making them more vulnerable for 2 turns.", "Neutral"], "b:Ecaflip:Fleassive": ["", "When the Ecaflip performs a heal:\n{Icon Arrow} The heal is halved\n{Icon Arrow} The heal applies an equal amount of Fleas\n\nRemoves the Fleas at the start of the Ecaflip's turn", "This passive reduces elemental healing done by the Ecaflip. In exchange, each elemental heal is replicated at the end of the target's turn before being transferred to the nearest ally."], "b:Ecaflip:Winning Streak": ["", "Each % Critical Hit given by the Ecaflip increases Lucky Day by 1\n\n% Ciritcal Hit gains now last only 1 turn", "Each Critical Hit point given by the Ecaflip (to themself or someone else) increases their Lucky Day by 1. However, when Critical Hit is given, it only lasts one turn."], "b:Ecaflip:Lucky Tarot": ["", "Each tarot card played, based on the card's numerical value:\n{Icon Arrow} Bonus to Lucky Day and % Critical Hit (1 turn)\n\nPlaying a card no longer gives 7 Lucky Day", "Tarot cards increase the Ecaflip's Lucky Day and give them a boost to critical hit rate based on the cards' numerical value."], "b:Ecaflip:Prophetic Tarot": ["", "Each tarot card has a color\n\n1 time per turn, playing 2 cards in a row gives:\n{Icon Arrow} 2 white cards in a row: {Caster} {WP} 1 WP\n{Icon Arrow} 2 black cards in a row: {Caster} 25 Lucky Day\n\nRoll Again is now 3 AP", "The Ecaflip earns bonuses by playing cards in pairs of the same color. However, Roll Again costs more."], "b:Ecaflip:Feline Impact": ["", "At end of turn, if an enemy is adjacent:\n{Icon Arrow} The next Feline Leap doesn't cost any AP\n\nFeline Leap maxes out at 2 uses per turn", "If the Ecaflip ends their turn adjacent to an enemy, the Ecaflip will gain a free Feline Leap the next turn. However, the spell can only be used two times per turn instead of three."], "b:Ecaflip:Cheat": ["", "The first card of the turn can be played for free, then the Ecaflip draws another card\n\nThe Ecaflip draws only one card at the start of the turn", "This passive allows the Ecaflip to play the first card of their turn for free. However, unless they use Roll Again, the Ecaflip can only draw a single card."], "b:Ecaflip:Healing Luck": ["", "Per Lucky Day point:\n{Icon Arrow} 1% Heals performed\n\nLucky Day goes up by 5 for each heal performed\nThe Lucky Day is lost at end of turn", "With this passive, Lucky Day increases healing done by the Ecaflip However, Lucky Day only lasts one turn, no matter how it's generated."], "b:Ecaflip:Feline Tarot": ["", "By using a tarot card on another fighter\n{Icon Arrow} Switches places\n{Icon Arrow} {Caster} Stabilized until the turn ends", "When the Ecaflip uses a tarot card on a fighter, they switch places with them. However, the Ecaflip will be stabilized until their turn ends."], "b:Ecaflip:Fortune Favors the Bold": ["", "When the Ecaflip drops below 50% HP:\n{Icon Arrow} 50 Lucky Day and 2 WP\n{Icon Arrow} 100% Incurable (1 turn)", "With this passive activated, the Ecaflip will regenerate Wakfu points when badly injured."], "b:Ecaflip:Heads, I win": ["", "When a card is played with 100 Lucky Day:\n{Icon Arrow} {Caster} {Element Light} Heals: 20% of max HP\n{Icon Arrow} {Caster} 50 Resistance (1 turn)\n{Icon Arrow} {Caster} 100% of level as Lock (1 turn)\n\nSets Dodge to 0 at the start of fight", "This passive boosts the Ecaflip's natural resistance and survival abilities. They regenerate and gain resistance bonuses when they play a card with 100 Lucky Day. In exchange, the Ecaflip loses all their dodge."], "b:Ecaflip:Generous Dice": ["", "Lucky Star now grants:\n{Icon Arrow} 0.5 Heals performed", "This passive transforms Lucky Star, applied when the Ecaflip goes over 100 Critical Hit. Instead of boosting damage, Lucky Star now boosts healing."], "b:Ecaflip:Graceful Feline": ["", "Feline Leap no longer has line of sight\nFeline Leap can be cast from a max Range of 2\n\nFeline Leap costs 1 extra AP", "This passive changes the Feline Leap spell. It can be cast without line of sight, but it costs more."], "b:Ecaflip:Blackjack": ["", "At start of turn, adds the values of the cards in the Ecaflip's hand\n\nIf the sum is between 1 and 20:\n{Icon Arrow} 10% of max HP as Armor\n\nOtherwise:\n{Icon Arrow} 5 levels of Crumbly", "Cards in the Ecaflip's hand are added up at the start of the turn. If their total value is equal to or less than 20, the Ecaflip gains Armor. If their value is over 20, the Ecaflip gets a penalty to final Armor received for 1 turn."], "b:Ecaflip:Trump Cards": ["", "Odd turns:\n{Icon Arrow} Only draws and can only play odd cards\n\nEven turns:\n{Icon Arrow} Only draws and can only play even cards", "This passive allows for some control over cards. On odd turns, the Ecaflip can only draw and play odd-numbered tarot cards, and on even turns, they can only draw and play even-numbered tarot cards."], "b:Ecaflip:Lucky Cards": ["", "At end of turn:\n{Icon Arrow} 15 Lucky Day per white card in hand\n{Icon Arrow} -15 Lucky Day per card black in hand", "This passive grants control over Lucky Day based on the cards still in the Ecaflip's hand at the end of their turn."], "b:Ecaflip:Lucky Seven": ["", "When 6 cards are played, but the Lucky Day was not at 100:\n{Icon Arrow} 100 Lucky Day\n{Icon Arrow} The draw pile is emptied", "Every six tarot cards played with their normal effect (not doubled by Lucky Day), the Ecaflip maximizes their Lucky Day and empties their draw pile."], "b:Sacrier:Blood Rush": ["{AP} 3", "{Caster} Flame Return: Flame Return (+5 Lvl.)\n{Element Fire} Damage: 3-113", "Inflicts higher damage, but the caster suffers a Flame Return.", "Fire"], "b:Sacrier:Burning Blood": ["{AP} 4", "{Caster} Flame Return: Damage: 10% of max HP\n{Element Fire} Damage 4-151 {Size: 1 - 1}", "Burns some of the caster's health to inflict heavy damage on nearby targets.", "Fire"], "b:Sacrier:Cage of Blood": ["{AP} 4", "{Element Fire} Damage: 4-121\n{MP} -3 MP\nCage of Blood (Lvl 15)\n{Damage Inflicted} -15% damage inflicted (1 turn)\n\nCast on an {Ally} ally:\n{Icon Arrow} {Armor} 8-34 {Element Fire} Armor\n{Icon Arrow} Barrier:\n{Icon Arrow} -10-2450 Damage received (1 time)", "Removes MP from the target and applies a penalty on damage inflicted.", "Fire"], "b:Sacrier:Punition": ["{AP} 3", "If the Sacrier doesn't have 100 Fury:\n{Icon Arrow} Sets the Sacrier's HP to 20%\n\n{Element Fire} Damage: 6-197", "The caster instantly achieves their maximum berserker potential while losing all HP above 20%. Then they deal high Fire damage.", "Fire"], "b:Sacrier:Sacrier's Fist": ["{AP} 2", "{Caster} Moves closer 3 cells\n{Enemy} {Element Earth} Damage: 2-75\n{Caster} Flame Return: 5% of max HP", "The Sacrier moves closer to their target and suffers a Flame Return. If the target is an enemy and the Sacrier ends up adjacent to them, the Sacrier inflicts damage on them.", "Earth"], "b:Sacrier:Rocky Foot": ["{AP} 3", "If the Sacrier has no Armor:\n{Icon Arrow} {Element Earth} Damage: 3-91\n{Icon Arrow} {Caster} {Armor} 6-28 {Element Earth} Armor\n\nIf the Sacrier has Armor:\n{Icon Arrow} {Element Earth} Damage: 4-121\n{Icon Arrow} {Caster} {Armor} -5% of max HP as Armor", "If the Sacrier has no Armor, they generate some. Otherwise, the Sacrier inflicts more damage by sacrificing some of their Armor.", "Earth"], "b:Sacrier:Insanity": ["{AP} 2\n{WP} 1", "Attracts targets around the targeted cell\n{Target} {Element Earth} Damage: 3-83 {Size: 3}\n{Caster} {Lock} 0-122 Lock (1 turn)", "The Sacrier rages, increasing their Lock, attracting enemies and inflicting damage.", "Earth"], "b:Sacrier:Colonnades": ["{AP} 4", "{Caster} Teleports to the cell\n\nIn a square {Area Square} area of effect:\n{Icon Arrow} {Enemy}\n{Icon Arrow} {Ally} {Element Earth} Damage: 4-131\n\nPer target hit:\n{Icon Arrow} {Caster} {Element Earth} Damage: 4-131\n{Armor} 1-20 {Element Earth} Armor {Area Squarering}", "This area-of-effect spell is versatile; within a square-shaped area of effect, enemies suffer damage, and allies gain Armor. And for every ally or enemy target hit, the Sacrier gains Armor.", "Earth"], "b:Sacrier:Smashes": ["{AP} 5", "{Element Earth} Damage: 5-176\nIncurable (Lvl 5)\n\nIf the Sacrier has 25% or more of their max HP as Armor:\n{Icon Arrow} {Element Earth} Damage: 8-264 instead\n{Icon Arrow} Consumes 25% of max HP as Armor\nOtherwise: {Caster} {Armor} 10-52 {Element Earth} Armor", "Inflicts major damage and reduces the healing that the target receives. If the Sacrier has enough Armor, they sacrifice it to significantly increase damage inflicted on the target. Otherwise, they generate Armor.", "Earth"], "b:Sacrier:Aversion": ["{AP} 4", "{Element Air} Damage: 3-98\n\nIf the target's % HP is higher than the Sacrier's:\n{Icon Arrow} {Element Air} Damage: 4-131 instead", "Inflicts damage on an enemy. This damage is greater if the target has more % HP than the Sacrier.", "Air"], "b:Sacrier:Assault": ["{AP} 1", "Normal Effects\nSwitches places\n{Caster} {Armor} 4-18 {Element Air} Armor\nTurns the target's gaze to the Sacrier\n\nEffects if {Caster} {Berserk Mastery} Berserk\nCosts {WP} 1 extra WP\nSwitches places\n{Enemy} {Element Air} Damage: 2-60\nTurns the target's gaze to the Sacrier", "The caster switches places with their target and inflicts some damage on it.", "Air"], "b:Sacrier:Spiritual Tempest": ["{AP} 4", "{Element Air} Damage: 4-131\nFor each movement spell used during the turn:\n{Icon Arrow} Spiritual Tempest costs {AP} 1 AP less\n{Icon Arrow} {Caster} Flame Return: 10% of map HP", "Opponents in the area of effect suffer damage, then all fighters around the targeted cell are pushed back.", "Air"], "b:Sacrier:Light Speed": ["{AP} 2", "Normal Effects\nTeleports to the targeted cell\n{Caster} {Armor} 6-28 {Element Air} Armor\n\nEffects if {Caster} {Berserk Mastery} Berserk\nCosts {WP} 1 extra WP\n{Enemy} {Element Air} Damage: 3-91 {Area Circle} around the starting cell\nTeleports to the targeted cell", "The Sacrier jumps onto the targeted cell and generates armor. In the Berserk state, the Sacrier inflicts damage around their starting point instead of generating armor.", "Air"], "b:Sacrier:Burning Armor": ["", "Transforms the Martyr spell into Burning Armor", "Unlocks the Burning Armor spell instead of Martyr. With Burning Armor, all Flame Returns are converted to Armor, but the Sacrier suffers their Armor as Flame Returns at the start of their turn."], "b:Sacrier:Transposition": ["{AP} 1\n{WP} 1", "Switches places\n{Caster} {Element Physical} Healing: 10% of HP lost of the caster {Fixed: The value is not influenced by the caster's damage.}", "The Sacrier switches places with an ally or enemy.", "Neutral"], "b:Sacrier:Sanguine Armor": ["{AP} 2", "{Ally} {Armor} Armor with 20% of the target's max HP\n{Ally} {Lock} 2 Lock (1 turn)\n{Ally} Stabilized (1 turn)", "The Sacrier stabilizes the target, which can no longer be moved for 1 turn. When targeting an ally or themself, the Sacrier generates powerful armor and higer Lock gain.", "Neutral"], "b:Sacrier:Sacrifice": ["{AP} 3", "{Ally} Sacrifice (2 turns) and Scar (5 turns)\nIf the spell is cast on the Sacrier {Caster}:\n{Icon Arrow} {Ally} Sacrifice (2 turns) and Scar (5 turns) {Size: 2}\nSacrifice is removed if the Sacrier has less than of their HP\nIf the Sacrier has a sacrificed allied player:\n{Icon Arrow} 100 Elemental Resistance", "The Sacrier protects targeted allies and gains resistance during the effect. When an ally is about to suffer direct damage, the Sacrier suffers the damage instead and switches places with the ally.", "Neutral"], "b:Sacrier:Blood Transfer": ["{WP} 2", "{Ally} Vitality (2 turns) {Size: 2}\nHealth Points\n-15% Healing Resistance", "The Sacrier increases the max HP of allies in the area ot effect for 2 turns. Targets' healing resistance is also reduced.", "Neutral"], "b:Sacrier:Tattooed Blood": ["", "HP bonus for the Sacrier:\n{Icon Arrow} 800% of their level\n\nHot-Blooded Heart now has 2-turn cooldown", "The Sacrier gains HP but can no longer cast Hot-Blooded Heart every.tgrn."], "b:Sacrier:Mobility": ["", "For each movement spell (up to 3 times):\n{Icon Arrow} 1 max MP (1 turn)\n{Icon Arrow} 100% of level as Dodge (1 turn)\n\nAt start of combat, Lock is reduced to 0", "The Sacrier can move their targets and themself more easily, but it costs their ability to keep opponents next to them."], "b:Sacrier:Wakfu Veins": ["", "When moving with a spell:\n{Icon Arrow} {Caster} Flame Return: 5% of current HP", "lf the Sacrier uses a spell to move\nthemself, they suffer a Flame Return."], "b:Sacrier:Placidity": ["", "For each movement spell, as long as the Sacrier has not used MP to move:\n{Icon Arrow} Heals: of missing HP if the Sacrier moved a target\n\n-2 max WP", "As long as the Sacrier has not used MP to move, they heal themself by using their spells to move targets."], "b:Sacrier:Blood Pact": ["", "After falling below 20% max HP (1 time per turn):\n{Icon Arrow} 15% of max HP as Armor\n\nAfter going above 40% max HP (1 time per turn):\n{Icon Arrow} 15% of max HP as Armor\n\n-30% Health Points", "The Sacrier's max HP is reduced, but they gain Armor if they drop below 20% max HP and then if they go above 40% max HP afterward."], "b:Sacrier:Libation": ["", "Every 4 Flame Returns:\n{Icon Arrow} 2 WP\n\nWP regeneration linked to Fury is disabled", "The Sacrier loses their natural WP regeneration. However, they gain it by inflicting Flame Returns on themself."], "b:Sacrier:Transcendence": ["", "Berserk:\n{Icon Arrow} Adds Melee Mastery to Dodge\n\nOtherwise:\n{Icon Arrow} Adds Melee Mastery to Lock\n\n{Range} -1 Range", "The Sacrier can greatly increase their Dodge or Lock while in the Berserk state."], "b:Sacrier:Blood Trail": ["", "When the Sacrier inflicts a Flame Return on themself:\n{Icon Arrow} 100% of level as Lock (1 turn, stackable)\n{Icon Arrow} 100% of level as Dodge (1 turn, stackable)\n\nFlame Returns are increased by 20%", "The Sacrier boosts their Lock and Dodge each time they inflict a flame return on themself. However, the flame returns are greater."], "b:Sacrier:Smasher": ["", "If the target has more %HP than the Sacrier:\n{Icon Arrow} 25% health stolen as {Armor} Armor\n\nOtherwise:\n{Icon Arrow} {Caster} suffers 15% of damage inflicted\n{Icon Arrow} The effect does not count as a Flame Return\n{Icon Arrow} The effect does not KO the Sacrier if they have more than 1 HP", "The Sacrier converts part of the damage they inflict on targets that have more HP than the Sacrier to Armor. However, if the target has less HP, the Sacrier themself suffers part of the damage they inflict."], "b:Sacrier:Clinging to Life": ["", "After falling below 20% max HP:\n{Icon Arrow} 20% of max HP as Armor\n{Icon Arrow} Impending Death", "When the Sacrier is mortally wounded, they gain resistance and a large amount of Armor. However, they won't be able to go above 20% max HP for a full turn."], "b:Sacrier:Blood Flow": ["", "When the Sacrier heals themself, the impact of Healing Resistance is halved\n-50% Armor received", "The Sacrier's healing is significantly less reduced by resistance to healing but the armor the Sacrier receives is reduced."], "b:Sacrier:Dangerous Game": ["", "If {Caster} current HP < 35%:\n{Icon Arrow} 100% Heals received\n\nIf {Caster} current HP >= 35%:\n{Icon Arrow} -75 Heals received", "This passive makes it much easier for the Sacrier to get out of a sticky situation when their HP is very low. However, they are harder to heal when their current HP are high."], "b:Sacrier:Vision": ["", "If there are no fighters adjacent to the Sacrier:\n{Icon Arrow} {Caster} Armor gains are reduced by 100%\n{Range} 2 Range\n-10% ranged damage received", "This passive increases the range of the sacrier. In exchange, Armor gains are reduced by 100% it the Sacrier is not adjacent to another fighter."], "b:Sacrier:Wakfu Pact": ["", "HP bonus for the Sacrier:\n{Icon Arrow} 400% of their level\n\nPer {WP} WP spent:\n{Icon Arrow} {Caster} Flame Return: 5% of current HP", "The Sacrier gains HP but suffers a flame return each time they use WP."], "b:Sacrier:Executor": ["", "If the Sacrier is adjacent to a fighter\n{Icon Arrow} {Caster} Healing is reduced by 100%\n{Range} 2 Range\n-10% melee damage received", "This passive increases the Sacrier's range. In exchange, heating received is canceled it the Sacrier is adjacent to another tighter."], "b:Sacrier:Motion Sick": ["", "If a fighter is moved by the Sacrier:\n{Icon Arrow} -2 MP (1 turn, not stackable)", "Targets moved by the Sacrier lose MP. If the Sacrier uses a spell to move themself, they also lose MP."], "b:Sacrier:Pillar": ["", "At end of turn, per adjacent enemy:\n{Icon Arrow} {Element Physical}Healing: 10% of HP lost of the caster {Fixed: The value is not influenced by the caster's damage.}\n{Icon Arrow} {Elemental Resistance} 30 Elemental Resistance (1 turn)\n{Icon Arrow} {MP} -1 max MP (1 turn)", "Makes the Sacrier less mobile but grants HP regeneration capabilities and a resistance bonus when the Sacrier is adjacent to their enemies."], "b:Sacrier:Burning": ["", "At end of turn, if an enemy is adjacent to the Sacrier:\n{Icon Arrow} 100% of level as Flaming\n{Icon Arrow} If no enemies are adjacent to the Sacrier at the start of the turn: {Caster} Flame Return: 30% of max HP", "The Sacrier catches fire if they end their turn adjacent to an enemy. If no enemies are adjacent to the Sacrier when they start a turn, the Sacrier suffers a flame return equivalent to Flaming."], "b:Sacrier:Sacrier's Heart": ["", "In Berserk:\n{Icon Arrow} Melee Mastery is added to Distance Mastery\n{Icon Arrow} Distance Mastery is added to Melee Mastery\n{Icon Arrow} -2 Range", "Under the influence of Bold Punishment, the Sacrier's melee mastery and distance mastery are added together to increase their damage and versatility, in exchange for their range."], "b:Foggernaut:Fire Thrower": ["{AP} 4", "{Element Fire} Damage: 4-131 and {Range} -2 Range (1 turn)\n\nCast on a turret:\n{Icon Arrow} The area of effect becomes {Area Con}", "Inflicts damage and reduces the range over which the target can cast its spells.", "Fire"], "b:Foggernaut:Blazing Fire": ["{AP} 2", "{Element Fire} Damage: 2-55 {Size: 1}\n\nCast on a turret:\n{Icon Arrow} The area of effect becomes {Area Cross} (2)", "Inflicts damage in an area of effect. This ranged attack is versatile.", "Fire"], "b:Foggernaut:Charring": ["{AP} 4", "Can only be cast outside line of sight\n\n{Enemy} {Element Fire} Damage: 5-164\n\nCast on a turrent:\n{Icon Arrow} The area of effect becomes {Area Square}", "Inflicts high damage but cannot be cast on targets that are already in the Foggernaut's field of vision. Targets must be hidden behind an obstacle or another fighter.", "Fire"], "b:Foggernaut:Flambé": ["{AP} 3", "{Element Fire} Damage: 3-91\n\nCast on a turret:\n{Icon Arrow} Places a Flambé glyph {Area Circlering} (2-3)\n{Icon Arrow} At start and end of turn:\n{Icon Arrow} {Element Fire} damage: 4-102", "Inflicts damage. If the Foggernaut targets their own turret with this spell, it sets the surrounding cells on fire. These cells inflict Fire damage on targets that start or end their turn on them.", "Fire"], "b:Foggernaut:Scuttle": ["{AP} 5", "{Element Fire} damage: 5-164\n\nIf the Turret is adjacent to the target:\n{Icon Arrow} {Element Fire} damage: additional 1-32 per level of Turret", "Inflicts Fire damage. The damage is greater if the target is adjacent to one of the Foggernaut's turrets.", "Fire"], "b:Foggernaut:Current": ["{AP} 3", "{Enemy} {Element Water} Damage: 2-55 {Area Vline}\nPushes back 1 cell ({Enemy} {Element Water} Collision: 2-55) {Area Vline}\n\n+1 level of High Pressure on the caster\n\nAt level 2 of High Pressure:\n{Icon Arrow} Pushes 4 cells rather than 1 {Size: 3 x 0}", "Inflicts damage and pushes the target. If the target hits another fighter or an obstacle, then the target suffers collision damage. If the Foggernaut has two levels of High Pressure, targets are pushed farther.", "Water"], "b:Foggernaut:Evaporation": ["{AP} 4", "{Enemy} {Element Water} Damage: 4-111 (to the targeted cell)\n{Icon Arrow} Teleports to the cell\n\n+1 level of High Pressure on the caser\n\nAt level 2 of High Pressure:\n{Icon Arrow} The spell gains 4 Range", "The Foggernaut jumps on the targeted cell. Water damage is inflicted on the enemies that they fly over on their way there. If the Foggernaut has two levels of High Pressure, they can move farther.", "Water"], "b:Foggernaut:Froth": ["{AP} 3", "{Element Water} Damage: 3-98 {Size: 1 x 1}\n\n+1 level of High Pressure on the caster\n\nAt level 2 of High Pressure:\n{Icon Arrow} The caster regains 3 AP", "Inflicts damage in an area of effect. If the Foggernaut has two levels of High Pressure, they recover the AP spent on the spell.", "Water"], "b:Foggernaut:Pilfer": ["{AP} 3", "{Element Water} Damage: 3-98\n\n+1 level of High Pressure on the caster\n\nAt level 2 of High Pressure:\n{Icon Arrow} -30% Critical Hit and Block (2 turns)", "Inflicts damage without line of sight. If the Foggernaut has two levels of High Pressure, they can reduce the target's Critical Hits and Block.", "Water"], "b:Foggernaut:Dissolution": ["{AP} 4", "{Element Water} Damage: 4-141\n\n+1 level of High Pressure on the caster\n\nAt level 2 of High Pressure, applies Dissolution (Lvl 4-141) (2 turns):\nAt end of turn:\n{Icon Arrow} {Element Water} Damage: 4-141\n{Icon Arrow} {Caster} High Pressure (+1 Lvl.)", "Inflicts damage in a straight line and with limited range. If the Foggernaut has two levels of High Pressure, they can apply a powerful poison that inflicts damage at the end of the target's turn for two turns. Each time the poison is triggered, the Foggernaut recovers a level of High Pressure.", "Water"], "b:Foggernaut:Pummel": ["{AP} 3", "Cast on {Enemy}: {Element Earth} Damage: 3-98\n\nCast on {Ally}: {Armor} 3-1,438 Armor\n\n{Caster} {Armor} 3-1,438 Armor", "Adds Armor to the Foggernaut; the amount of Armor will absorb subsequent damage suffered. If the spell is cast on an ally, the ally also gains Armor.", "Earth"], "b:Foggernaut:Trampling": ["{AP} 3", "Cast on an ally {Ally}:\n{Icon Arrow} Stabilized\n{Icon Arrow} -2 max MP (1 turn)\n\nCast on an enemy {Enemy}:\n{Icon Arrow} {Element Earth} Damage: 3-83\n{Icon Arrow} {MP} -4 MP", "When cast on an enemy, inflicts damage and removes Movement Points from the target. When cast on an ally, stabilizes them.", "Earth"], "b:Foggernaut:Bombardment": ["{AP} 2", "This spell must be cast on an entity\n\n{Enemy} {Element Earth} Damage: 2-55 {Area Cross}\nAdditional {Enemy} {Element Earth} Damage: 1-27 {Area Cross} each time this spell is cast during the current turn", "Inflicts damage in a cross-shaped area of effect. The power of the spell's damage increases with each use.", "Earth"], "b:Foggernaut:Hammer Claw": ["{AP} 4", "Cast on an ally {Ally}:\n{Icon Arrow} Attracts by 2 cells\n{Icon Arrow} Armor: 6% of caster's max HP\n\nCast on an enemy {Enemy}:\n{Icon Arrow} {Enemy} {Element Earth} Damage: 4-111\n{Icon Arrow} Attracts by 2 cells\n{Icon Arrow} On the cast {Caster}: {Lock} 1 Lock", "When cast on a fighter, the target is attracted close to the Foggernaut. If the target is an enemy, the Foggernaut inflicts damage on them. If the target is an ally, the Foggernaut protects them by giving them a certain amount of Armor.", "Earth"], "b:Foggernaut:Shebang": ["{AP} 6", "{Element Earth} damage: 6-211\n{Icon Arrow} 5% extra damage per caster's current SP (50% max)", "Inflicts greater damage for each Stasis Point that the Foggernaut has at the time when they cast the spell.", "Earth"], "b:Foggernaut:Armor Plating": ["{WP} 2", "Cast on an ally {Ally}:\n{Icon Arrow} 10% of the {Caster}'s max HP as Armor\n{Icon Arrow} +100% on their mechanisms (blocks and turret)\n\nCast on an enemy {Enemy}:\n{Icon Arrow} Steals 10% of the {Caster}'s max HP as Armor", "The Foggernaut applies armor to an ally. The amount of armor given is increased on the Foggernaut's mechanisms (blocks and turret).", "Neutral"], "b:Foggernaut:Hypertension": ["{AP} 3\n{SP} 2", "The turret must be on the field\n\nCast on the turret:\n{Icon Arrow} Destroys the turret\n{Icon Arrow} The caster regenerates 2 WP per level of the turret\n{Icon Arrow} Heals self by the turret's remaining HP\n\nCast on an enemy {Enemy}:\n{Icon Arrow} {Element Light} Damage: 6-153 and Hypertension", "This spell allows the caster to sacrifice a turret to recover HP and WP, or to inflict damage on an enemy. In the latter case, the spell's target takes more damage from the turret for 1 turn.", "Neutral"], "b:Foggernaut:Ambush": ["{AP} 3\n{SP} 1", "If the targeted cell is free:\n{Icon Arrow} The Turret teleports to the cell at the start of the caster's next turn\n{Icon Arrow} The Turret activates instantly after teleporting\n\nOtherwise:\n{Icon Arrow} The Turret switches places with the target (7 cells max)\n{Icon Arrow} {Icon Arrow} The Turret activates instantly after the position switch", "If the Foggernaut targets an empty cell, they place a glyph to which the Turret will teleport at the start of its next turn. If the Foggernaut targets a fighter, the Turret switches places with the target (7 cells max). In either case, the Turret activates immediately after it moves.", "Neutral"], "b:Foggernaut:Transition": ["{AP} 1\n{WP} 1", "The spell's target goes to the closest Microbot (4 cells max)\n\nCast on Microbot:\n{Icon Arrow} The Turret is teleported onto it (8 cells max)", "This mobility spell sends the target to the closest free microbot in a four-cell radius. Cast directly on a microbot, it teleports the Foggernaut Turret onto it.", "Neutral"], "b:Foggernaut:Stasis Flux": ["{AP} 2\n{SP} 3", "Cast on an ally {Ally}:\n{Icon Arrow} 2 Range (2 turns)\n{Icon Arrow} 30% ranged damage inflicted (2 turns)\n\nCast on an enemy {Enemy}:\n{Icon Arrow} -150 Elemental Resistance (2 turns)", "This spell strengthens the team's offensive potential, either by increasing an ally's damage or by weakening an enemy's resistances.", "Neutral"], "b:Foggernaut:Winding Roads": ["", "Microbot is now limited to 4 uses per turn\n\n-2 to rail size", "The Foggernaut can place more microbots each turn. In exchange, the maximum length of rails (between two microbots) decreases."], "b:Foggernaut:Energy Moderator": ["", "If the Foggernaut has all their WP at start of turn:\n1 MP (1 turn)\n{Icon Arrow} 30% Armor given (1 turn)\n{Icon Arrow} +2 min and max Range for all spells (1 turn)", "The Foggernaut gains an MP and Range bonus at start of their turn if they are at full WP."], "b:Foggernaut:Versatility": ["", "At end of turn, if the Foggernaut is within 3 cells or\nless of an enemy:\n{Icon Arrow} 50 Resistance and 18 Lock, -10% damage\ninflicted (1 turn)\n\nOtherwise:\n{Icon Arrow} 1 Range and 18 Dodge, -50 Elemental\nResistance (1 turn)", "The Foggernaut gains an MP and Range bonus at start of their turn if they are at full WP."], "b:Foggernaut:Reinforced Armor Plating": ["", "Turret:\n{Icon Arrow} Has 50% additional HP\n{Icon Arrow} Now has a non-modifiable Range of 3", "The turret is more resistant to damage. In exchange, the Foggernaut can only place it at a range of up to 3 cells max, rather than 6."], "b:Foggernaut:Robotic Strategy": ["", "The Foggernaut is healed for 30% of damage inflicted by the Turret\n-20% indirect damage", "The Foggernaut steals HP when their Turret inflicts damage, in exchange for part of their indirect damage."], "b:Foggernaut:Transportation Technology": ["", "Microbot\n{Icon Arrow} Costs 1 AP less\n{Icon Arrow} Now has an non-modifiable max Range of 3", "Microbot cost decreases. In exchange, the maximum range is reduced to 3."], "b:Foggernaut:Earthy Assistance": ["", "Casting an Earth spell on an empty cell places a block (1 turn)\nThe block has 3% of the Foggernaut's max HP for each AP of the spell used\nThe block intercepts damage to allies in melee range\nmax 3 blocks\n\nBlocks' protection zones cannot overlap\n\n-30% Armor received", "The Foggernaut summons blocks when casting an Earth spell on an empty cell. These blocks protect nearby allies. Blocks ' protection zones cannot overlap."], "b:Foggernaut:Mechanical Substitution": ["", "When the Foggernaut casts a {Element Water} {Element Earth} elemental spell on their Turret:\n{Icon Arrow} {Element Water}: The Foggernaut switches places with the turret\n{Icon Arrow} {Element Earth}: Attracts by 1 cell for each AP of the spell {Area Cross} (7)\n{Icon Arrow} {Caster} {AP} 2 AP (1x per turn)\n\nThe Turret spell costs 1 WP", "The turret applies additional effects when the Foggernaut casts an Earth or Water spell on it. The first time an effect is triggered during the turn, the Foggernaut recovers AP. In exchange, summoning or upgrading the Turret costs I WP."], "b:Foggernaut:Patience": ["", "If the Foggernaut reaches their max SP:\n{Icon Arrow} 2 max SP (cannot be regenerated)\n\nAt start of fightL\n{Icon Arrow} {Caster} {WP} -2 max WP", "The Foggernaut instantly gains 2 non-regenerable Stasis points (SP) on reaching their maximum SP. They can therefore temporarily exceed their maximum SP. In exchange, their max WP decreases at the start of the fight."], "b:Foggernaut:Light Alloy": ["", "+2 max microbots on the field\n\n{MP} -1 max MP", "Reduces the Foggernaut's movement ability while increasing their positioning ability with their rails."], "b:Foggernaut:Energy Inversion": ["", "The Foggernaut's SP and WP recovery are inverted:\n{Icon Arrow} {Caster} Recovers 1 SP at end of turn\n{Icon Arrow} {Caster} Recovers 1 WP each time their turret hits an enemy\n{Icon Arrow} Excess WP are converted into SP", "The Foggernaut inverts their Wakfu Point and Stasis Point regeneration. They now naturally recover I SP at end of turn, and their Turret regenerates WP for them."], "b:Foggernaut:Heavy Duty Covering": ["", "600% of level as max HP\n\nFogginator removes 25% of the Foggernaut's current HP at end of turn", "The Foggernaut gains HP. In exchange, Fogginator inflicts heavy damage on them at end of turn."], "b:Foggernaut:Activation": ["", "The Turret spell has additional effects if cast on a target (other than the Turret):\n{Icon Arrow} {Element Fire}: {Element Fire} damage: 3 (+100% level 2)\n{Icon Arrow} {Element Water}: Switches places with the Turret (up to 7 cells away)\n{Icon Arrow} {Element Earth}: Armor 5% of the {Caster}'s max HP (+100% level 2)\n\nThe Turret maxes out at level 2", "The Foggernaut can use the Turret spell on targets. The effect depends on the Turret's active element. If it is Fire, the Turret deals damage to the target. If it is Water, it switches places with the target. If it is Earth, it applies Armor to the target. The effects are boosted if the spell gets a critical hit."], "b:Foggernaut:Immediate Execution": ["", "The Turret activates when the Foggernaut uses the Turret spell on it\n\nThe Turret no longer automatically activates at end of turn", "The Foggernaut's Turret is no longer automatically triggered at end of turn. Instead, the Foggernaut can trigger it manually."], "b:Foggernaut:Stasified Protection": ["", "The Turret only regenerates 1 SP, regardless of its level\nAdditional SP generated based on the Turret's level are converted to Armor for the Foggernaut:\n{Icon Arrow} {Caster} 5% max HP per level as Armor", "Leftover SP (after the first one) generated by the Turret are converted into Armor."], "b:Foggernaut:Hot Wheels": ["", "{Element Light} damage: 4-121 to all enemies {Enemy} who start or end their turn on rails\n\nThe Microbot spell costs 1 extra SP", "The Foggernaut's rails inflict damage on enemies who start or end their turn on them, but Microbots cost 1 SP."], "b:Foggernaut:Serene Conquest": ["", "At start of fight: -2 max SP\n\n50% Block when the Foggernaut is not in the Gunner state", "The Foggernaut gains an increased Block chance. In exchange, they lose max SP at the start of the fight."], "b:Foggernaut:Tactician": ["", "-50% damage inflicted by the turret\n\nThe Turret has additional effects based on the active element:\n{Icon Arrow} {Element Fire} Applies Incurable (+2 lvl.) (+1 per level of the Turret)\n{Icon Arrow} {Element Water}: Pushes enemies 2 cells (+1 per level of the Turret)\n{Icon Arrow} {Element Earth}: Armor to allies (3% of Foggernaut's max HP +2 per level of the Turret)", "The turret gains additional effects at the expense of its damage."], "b:Foggernaut:Advanced Mechanics": ["", "The Foggernaut can control 2 turrets on the field at once\n\n-30% direct damage inflicted", "The Foggernaut can summon two turrets in exchange for some of their direct damage inflicted."], "b:Foggernaut:Tactical Deployment": ["", "The Turret Turret no longer has a line of sight\nThe Turret spell can only be cast in a straight line", "The Foggernaut can place their Turret without line of sight, but only in a straight line."], "b:Ouginak:Ruckus": ["{AP} 3", "Steals 1 MP\n{Element Water} Damage: 3-98\n\nIf the {Caster} has more than 80% of their max HP:\n{Icon Arrow} Steals 2 MP instead", "The Ouginak steals an MP from their target. The theft is greater if the Ouginak has lots of HP.", "Water"], "b:Ouginak:Flail": ["{AP} 4\n{WP} 1", "{Element Water} Damage: 5-152 {Area Hline}\n{Icon Arrow} 40% health stolen", "The Ouginak creates a geyser under their targets. They recover part of the HP removed from the targets.", "Water"], "b:Ouginak:Rupture": ["{AP} 2", "{Element Water} Damage: 2-70\n{Icon Arrow} 50% health stolen\n\nIf the target is a summons:\n{Icon Arrow} {Element Water} Damage: 4-141\n{Icon Arrow} 50% health stolen", "This spell's damage comes with a health steal. The spell is more powerful on summons.", "Water"], "b:Ouginak:Weigh Down": ["{AP} 3", "{Element Water} Damage: 3-98 {Area Vline}\n\nIf the {Caster} has more than 80% of their max HP:\n{Icon Arrow} {Element Water} Damage: 4-131 instead {Area Vline}", "This spell inflicts powerful damage on opponents in a line. The damage is increased if the Ouginak has high HP.", "Water"], "b:Ouginak:Gash": ["{AP} 5", "{Element Water} Damage: 5-188\nIncurable (Lvl 3)\nCrumbly (Lvl 3)\n\nIf the {Caster} has more than 80% of their max HP:\n{Icon Arrow} Incurable (Lvl 6)\n{Icon Arrow} Crumbly (Lvl 6)", "The Ouginak inflicts heavy damage on the target and applies a penalty on its healing and armor received. The penalty is larger if the Ouginak has high HP.", "Water"], "b:Ouginak:Brawl": ["{AP} 3\n{WP} 1", "{Element Earth} Damage: 3-83\nBrawl\n\nIf the target is Brawled:\n{Icon Arrow} {Element Earth} Damage: 9-251 instead", "Inflicts Earth damage on a target. On the following turn, damage is tripled on targets that have already been hit by the spell.", "Earth"], "b:Ouginak:Fang in the Works": ["{AP} 2", "{Enemy} {Element Earth} Damage: 2-65 and {MP} -2 MP {Area Cross}", "A huge classic among Ouginaks. Their bite paralyzes their target, preventing it from fleeing.", "Earth"], "b:Ouginak:Watchdog": ["{AP} 4", "For each enemy affected:\n{Icon Arrow} {Caster} 1-467 armor\n{Enemy} {Element Earth} Damage: 4-121 {Area Cross}", "The Ouginak does damage in an area of effect and gains Armor depending on the number of enemies they hit.", "Earth"], "b:Ouginak:Crosshatch": ["{AP} 3", "{Element Earth} Damage: 3-83 {Area Hline}\nCrosshatch (Lvl 1) {Area Hline}", "Crosshatch does damage in an area of effect and marks the targets; for one turn, they will suffer additional damage each time the Ouginak attacks them directly.", "Earth"], "b:Ouginak:Fits and Starts": ["{AP} 4", "If the target has Armor:\n{Icon Arrow} {Element Earth} Damage: 2-65 (on armor)\n\n{Element Earth} Damage: 4-131\n\n{Caster} Armor gain: 5% of max HP", "The Ouginak inflicts additional damage n the target's Armor, as well as protecting themself in turn.", "Earth"], "b:Ouginak:Sweeping": ["{AP} 4", "Attracts by 1 cell\n{Element Air} Damage: 4-131\n\nIf the target is or becomes adjacent to the Ouginak:\n{Icon Arrow} {Element Air} Damage: 5-164 instead", "The Ouginak attracts their target and inflicts air damage on it. The damage is greater if the target is adjacent to them.", "Air"], "b:Ouginak:Contusion": ["{AP} 3", "{Enemy} {Element Air} Damage: 3-91 {Area Cross}\nPushes back 1 cell", "The Ouginak pushes back fighters around the target and inflicts damage on enemies.", "Air"], "b:Ouginak:Big Dog": ["{AP} 3\n{WP} 1", "{Element Air} Damage: 4-121\nTeleports behind target", "The Ouginak uses their grapple to injure their enemy! They use it to get behind them.", "Air"], "b:Ouginak:Bone Breaker": ["{AP} 2", "{Element Air} Damage: 1-35\n{Enemy} Fracture (Lvl 2-70)", "The Ouginak applies a poison on their target. The target will suffer damage on every movement during its turn.", "Air"], "b:Ouginak:Pugnacity": ["{AP} 6\n{WP} 1", "{Enemy} {Element Air} Damage: 5-152\n{Enemy} Pugnacity (Lvl 4-121) (2 turns)", "The Ouginak applies their most powerful poison on their enemy... If the target ends its turn in close combat with the Ouginak, it suffers additional damage!", "Air"], "b:Ouginak:Hunter": ["{AP} 2", "{Ally} Attracts by 3 cells\n{Icon Arrow} {Dodge} 1 Dodge\n\n{Enemy} Moves closer 3 cells\n{Icon Arrow} {Dodge} -1 Dodge\n\nIf the target is the Ouginak's Prey:\n{Icon Arrow} {Caster} Regains 2 AP", "The Ouginak can use their Hunter abilities to either get closer to opponents or attract allies. If the target is their Prey, the cost of the spell is reimbursed.", "Neutral"], "b:Ouginak:Surge": ["{AP} 1", "If cast on an empty cell:\n{Icon Arrow} Teleports to the cell\n\nIf cast on Bow Wow or Prey:\n{Icon Arrow} Switches places\n\nCosts {AP} 1 AP per cell moved", "The Ouginak jumps to the targeted cell. If they target their Bow Wow or their Prey, they switch places with it. The spell's cost depends on the number of cells the Ouginak has moved.", "Neutral"], "b:Ouginak:Canine": ["{AP} 3", "Places the Canine\nAt start of turn:\n{Icon Arrow} {MP} -3 MP\n{Icon Arrow} {Element Light} Damage: 3-76\n\nThe {Icon Glyph} lasts 2 turns Glyph", "The Ouginak places a glyph that inflicts damage on and immobilizes any targets that start their turn on it.", "Neutral"], "b:Ouginak:Appeasement": ["{AP} 2\n{WP} 1", "{MP} 2 MP max (1 turn)\n\nIf the Ouginak has 20 or more Fury:\n{Icon Arrow} 1% of the {Caster}'s max HP in Armor per point of Fury\n{Icon Arrow} Consumes all fury", "The Ouginak concentrates to give their MP to their target. If they have enough Fury, they consume it to give their target Armor.", "Neutral"], "b:Ouginak:Pursuit": ["{AP} 3\n{WP} 1", "Pursued (Lvl 1)\nAt start of turn, the state bearer:\n{Icon Arrow} Teleports to the cell opposite the Pursued target\n{Icon Arrow} Ouginak: 10 Fury\n\nHave this spell in your deck\n{Icon Arrow} Unlocks spell Pursuer", "The Ouginak has mastered the art of tracking prey. It prepares to attack and pounces on its opponent.", "Neutral"], "b:Ouginak:Pack": ["{WP} 1", "Per ally in the {Area Circle} area:\n{Icon Arrow} {Caster} {Ally} {Damage Inflicted} +5% damage inflicted (2 turns, max 25)\n{Icon Arrow} {Caster} +4 Fury and +3% of max HP as Armor", "The Ouginak and their allies are strengthened based on the number of allies present in the area of effect when the spell is cast.", "Neutral"], "b:Ouginak:Sidekick": ["", "Bow Wow:\n{Icon Arrow} 2 AP\n{Icon Arrow} 100 Elemental Resistance\n{Icon Arrow} Resuces its Dodge to 0\n\nWhen the Bow Wow dies:\n{Icon Arrow} {WP} 2 WP", "The Bow Wow is more resistant and has more AP. In exchange, it can no longer dodge. When it dies, the Ouginak regains 2 WP."], "b:Ouginak:Haggling": ["", "When the Ouginak enters Were-Ouginak, per Fury point:\n{Icon Arrow} {Elemental Resistance} Elemental Resistance (3 turns)\n\nIn Were-Ouginak, loses 5 Fury at start of turn", "The Ouginak gains resistance based on its Fury when it transforms into a Were-Ouginak. In exchange, it loses Fury at start of turn."], "b:Ouginak:Growlight": ["", "300% of level as Lock\n\nWhen the Ouginak enters Were-Ouginak:\n{Icon Arrow} {Caster} converts their Lock to Dodge", "The Ouginak gains lock. When it transforms into a Were-Ouginak, its lock is converted to dodge."], "b:Ouginak:Relentless": ["", "{Force of Will} 20 Force of Will\n{Damage Inflicted} -10% damange inflicted\n\nWhen the Ouginak removes an MP from an enemy:\n{Icon Arrow} {Caster} +4 Fury", "The Ouginak gains force of will to bind targets more easily. The Ouginak gains Fury each time they remove MP. In exchange, they lose damage inflicted."], "b:Ouginak:Open Season": ["", "-10 max Fury\n\nWhen the Ouginak attacks its Prey:\n{Icon Arrow} Fury and Tracker are obtained instantly", "The Ouginak gains Fury and damage upon attacking its Prey, but its maximum Fury decreases."], "b:Ouginak:Digestion": ["", "-15% indirect damage\n\nWhen the Ouginak inflicts indirect damage:{Icon Arrow} {Caster} +4 Fury\n{Icon Arrow} {Caster} Heals: 4% of max HP\n\nUp to 5x per turn", "The Ouginak gains Fury and heals themself when they do indirect damage; this is damage done outside of their turn, such as poisons. In exchange, they sacrifice some of their damage."], "b:Ouginak:Canine Energy": ["", "3 max WP\n-20% damage inflicted in Were-Ouginak", "The Ouginak has more max WP, but their damage bonus in Were-Ouginak form is reduced."], "b:Ouginak:Ardor": ["", "{MP} -1 max MP\nIf the Ouginak ends their turn adjacent to Prey:\n{Icon Arrow} {Caster} 30% damage inflicted in melee", "The Ouginak's mobility is reduced, but they gain lots of damage-dealing power if they can finish their turn adjacent to their Prey."], "b:Ouginak:Raiding": ["", "{Damage Inflicted} -10% damage inflicted\n{Armor received} 30% Armor received\n400% of level as HP\nAt start of turn, if the Prey is in an adjacent cell:\n{Icon Arrow} Armor: 12% of max HP", "The Ouginak sacrifices damage in order to improve their ability to take a hit. They gain HP and armor received. They also gain armor at the start of their turn if adjacent to prey."], "b:Ouginak:Fury": ["", "+10 max Fury\n{WP} -1 max WP", "The Ouginak has greater maximum Fury. In exchange, their max WP decreases."], "b:Ouginak:Exhaustion": ["", "50% indirect damage inflicted\n{Range} -2 Range", "The Ouginak loses range, but their indirect damage increases. This is damage done outside of their turn, such as poisons."], "b:Ouginak:Tailing": ["", "20% damage inflicted from behind\n{MP} 1 MP\n\nPrey can only be cast from behind", "The Ouginak is more effective when attacking its targets from behind. To get there more easily, it gains mobility."], "b:Ouginak:Sniff": ["", "Apply Prey:\n{Icon Arrow} {Element Light} Damage: 3 (indirect damage)\n\nAt start of turn, the Prey receives:\n{Icon Arrow} {Element Light} Damage: 5\n\nPrey costs 2 WP", "The Ouginak's Prey are poisoned and take damage every turn."], "b:Ouginak:Canine Art": ["", "-15% indirect damage\n\nWhen the Ouginak inflicts indirect damage:{Icon Arrow} {Caster} 30% health stolen and converted to Armor\n{Icon Arrow} The armor obtained is limited to 50% of the max HP per turn", "The Ouginak steals part of the indirect damage they inflict and converts it to armor. This is damage done outside of their turn, such as poisons. In exchange, their damage is reduced. The armor obtained with Canine Art is limited to 50% of the Ouginak's max per turn."], "b:Ouginak:Burrow": ["", "At the end of the Ouginak's turn:\n{Icon Arrow} Switches places with the Bow Wow\n\nAt the end of the Bow Wow's turn:\n{Icon Arrow} Switches places with the Ouginak", "At end of turn, the Ouginak switches places with their Bow Wow. The Bow Wow then switches places with the Ouginak at the end of its turn."], "b:Ouginak:Cunning Fang": ["", "{Block} 20% Block\n\nWhen the Ouginak enters Were-Ouginak:\n{Icon Arrow} {Caster} Converts Block into Critical Hit", "The Ouginak gains Block to become more resistant. When it transforms into a Were-Ouginak, it converts its Block into Critical Hits to go on the attack."], "b:Ouginak:Canine Tracker": ["", "When ending their turn adjacent to their Prey:\n{Icon Arrow} Tracker (+10 Lvl.)\n{Icon Arrow} 2 Elemental Resistance per level of Tracker instead of Damage Inflicted (1 turn)", "The Ouginak converts damage into resistance when it ends its turn in contact with Prey."], "b:Ouginak:Wise Strength": ["", "Transforms MP removals\n{Icon Arrow} No longer removes MP\n{Icon Arrow} {Element Light} Damage: 1 at start of turn", "MP removals are replaced by application of indirect damage on the target."], "b:Ouginak:Dog Handler": ["", "The Bow Wow can no longer cast spells\nThe Bow Wow can be healed\n\nWhen the Ouginak casts a spell on a target and the Bow Wow also meets the casting conditions:\n{Icon Arrow} the Bow Wow replicates the spell on the target", "The Bow Wow copies the Ouginak's actions. However, it can no longer cast spells"], "b:Sacrier:Bloodthirsty Fury": ["{AP} 1\n{WP} 1", "Normal Effects\nAttracts by 6 cells\n{Caster} {Armor} 6-26 {Element Fire} Armor\n\nEffects if {Caster} {Berserk Mastery} Berserk\nCosts {WP} 1 extra WP\nAttracts by 6 cells\n{Enemy} {Element Fire} Damage: 3-83", "Attracts a target towards the Sacrier from far away.", "Fire"], "b:Sacrier:Motion Sickness": ["{AP} 2", "Normal Effects\n{Enemy} {Enemy} Motion Sickness (Lvl 1-25)\nWhen the bearer is moved by one of the Sacrier's spells:\n{Icon Arrow} {Element Air} Damage: 1-25 (indirect damage) {Size: 1}\n{Icon Arrow} When the bearer is moved by one of the Sacrier's spells:\n{Icon Arrow} {Element Air} Damage: 1-25 (indirect damage) {Size: 1}\nPushes back 1 cell {Size: 1 - 1}\n\nEffects if {Caster} {Berserk Mastery} Berserk\nCosts {AP} 1 extra AP\n{Enemy} {Element Air} Damage: 2-60 {Size: 1}\n{Enemy} {Enemy} Motion Sickness (Lvl 1-25)\n{Icon Arrow} When the bearer is moved by one of the Sacrier's spells:\n{Icon Arrow} {Element Air} Damage: 1-25 (indirect damage) {Size: 1}\n{Target} Pushes back 1 cell {Size: 1 - 1}", "T his spell applies a state that triggers on the Sacrier's movement effects: When the Sacrier moves a target other than themself, damage is inflicted on the target. If the Sacrier is bearing the state, the Sacrier gains Armor and HP each time a target other than themself is moved", "Air"], "b:Sacrier:Blood Bath": ["{AP} 2", "At the end of the {Caster} Sacrier's turn,\napplies Blood Bath (1 turn)\n{Elemental Resistance} -150 Elemental Resistance\nThe state bearer gains {Damage Inflicted} 30% damage inflicted on the Sacrier", "The Sacrier removes resistances from the target for I turn, but the target inflicts more damage on them.", "Neutral"], "b:Sacrier:Coagulation": ["{AP} 3", "{Caster} Coagulation (2 turns):\nDoubles the Armor cap\nAt the end of turn, per Armor point:\n{Icon Arrow} {Caster} {Ally} 0.5 {Armor} Armor {Size: 2}", "For 2 turns, the Sacrier increases their Armor cap. At end of turn, the Sacrier applies Armor on themself and nearby allies based on the Sacrier's current Armor.", "Neutral"], "b:Sram:First Blood": ["{AP} 2", "{Enemy} If the target has no Hemorrhage: Hemorrhage (+10 Lvl.) {Size: 1 x 1}\n{Enemy} Otherwise: Hemorrhage (+2 Lvl.) {Size: 1 x 1}\n\n{Element Fire} Damage: 2-65 {Size: 1 x 1}\n\n{Caster} Weak Point (+10 Lvl.)", "First Blood applies a high amount of Hemorrhage to enemies who don't have any. Hemorrhage inflicts additional damage on the target when the Sram inflicts direct damage on it. This spell generates Weak Point.", "Fire"], "b:Sram:Cold Blood": ["{AP} 2", "{Element Fire} Damage: 2-70\n\nConsumes the target's Hemorrhage:\n{Icon Arrow} {Caster} Healing: 1% of max HP per level\n{Icon Arrow} {Caster} +1 Weak Point per level\n\n{Caster} Weak Point (+10 Lvl.)", "In addition to inflicting damage, the Sram consumes Hemorrhage on their target to heal themself and gain Weak Point. This spell generates Weak Point.", "Fire"], "b:Sram:Bled Dry": ["{AP} 3", "{Enemy} Hemorrhage (+6 Lvl.)\n{Enemy} Bled Dry (Lvl 1)\n\n{Element Fire} Damage: 3-91\n{Caster} Health steal: 100% damage inflicted by Hemorrhage\n\n{Caster} Weak Point (+15 Lvl.)", "Inflicts damage on and applies Hemorrhage to the target. Hemorrhage inflicts additional damage on the target when the Sram inflicts direct damage on it. The damage inflicted by the Hemorrhage activated by this spell is converted to health steal on the Sram. At the start of the Sram's next turn, they cast a replica of the spell on the target. This spell generates Weak Point.", "Fire"], "b:Sram:Punishment": ["{AP} 4", "{Element Fire} Damage: 4-131 {Area Cross}\n\nIf the Sram consumed Weak Point during their turn:\n{Icon Arrow} {Element Fire} Damage: 5-164 instead {Area Cross}\n\n{Caster} Weak Point (+20 Lvl.)", "This spell's damage is greater if the Sram consumed Weak Point during their turn. This spell generates Weak Point.", "Fire"], "b:Sram:Execution": ["{AP} 6", "{Element Fire} Damage: 6-211\nEvery 50 Weak Point:\n{Icon Arrow} {Element Fire} Damage: 1-52 extra\n{Icon Arrow} {Enemy} Hemorrhage (+10 Lvl.)\n{Icon Arrow} {Caster} regains {AP} 1 AP, {MP} 1 MP, {WP} 1 WP\n{Icon Arrow} {Caster} consumes the Weak Point used", "Inflicts Fire damage and consumes Weak Point to inflict additional damage. Depending on the amount of Weak Point consumed, the Sram regains AP, MP, and WP, and applies Hemorrhage on the target before inflicting damage. Hemorrhage inflicts additional damage on the target when the Sram inflicts direct damage on it.", "Fire"], "b:Sram:Kleptosram": ["{AP} 2", "{Element Water} Damage: 2-65\n\nIf the target's back is turned: {Caster} Weak Point (+5 Lvl.)\n\n{Caster} Weak Point (+10 Lvl.)", "Inflicts Water damage and generates more Weak Point if the target has its back turned.", "Water"], "b:Sram:Scam": ["{AP} 2", "{Element Water} Damage: 2-65\nEvery 50 Weak Point:\n{Icon Arrow} {Element Water} Damage: 0-16 extra\n{Icon Arrow} {Enemy} Hemorrhage (+10 Lvl.)\n{Icon Arrow} {Caster} Healing: 12.5% of max HP\n{Icon Arrow} {Caster} regains {AP} 1 AP, {MP} 1 MP, {WP} 1 WP\n{Icon Arrow} {Caster} consumes the Weak Point used", "Inflicts Water damage and consumes Weak Point to inflict additional damage and heal themself. Depending on the amount of Weak Point consumed, the Sram regains AP, MP, and WP, and applies Hemorrhage on the target before inflicting damage. Hemorrhage inflicts additional damage on the target when the Sram inflicts direct damage on it.", "Water"], "b:Sram:Perfidious Attack": ["{AP} 4", "{Element Water} Damage: 4-141\n\nIf this spell kills a enemy, {Caster} regains {AP} 2 AP and {MP} 2 MP\n\n{Caster} Weak Point (+20 Lvl.)", "If the spell kills the enemy target, the Sram regains AP and MP. This spell generates Weak Point.", "Water"], "b:Sram:Rascalry": ["{AP} 3", "{Element Water} Damage: 4-121, penetrates Armor\n{Icon Arrow} 40% of damage inflicted is converted into {Armor}\nArmor on the target {Target}\n\n{Caster} Weak Point (+15 Lvl.)", "Inflicts heavy Water damage that penetrates Armor. A portion of damage inflicted is converted into Armor on the target. This spell generates Weak Point.", "Water"], "b:Sram:Swindlesram": ["{AP} 5", "{Element Water} Damage: 5-164\n\nIf the {Target}'s HP is < 50%:\n{Icon Arrow} {Element Water} Damage: 7-229 instead\n\n{Caster} Weak Point (+25 Lvl.)", "Inflicts major damage on the target. The damage is greater if the target has less than half of its HP. This spell generates Weak Point.", "Water"], "b:Sram:Forceful Blow": ["{AP} 4", "{Element Air} Damage: 4-141 {Size: 3 x 0}\nIf the target has Armor:\n{Icon Arrow} {Element Air} Damage: 2-70 (on Armor) {Size: 3 x 0}\nDamage is always melee\n\n{Caster} Weak Point (+20 Lvl.)", "Inflicts damage in a 3 -cell line. A line of additional damage is applied to Armor. This spell's damage is always considered melee damage, even if the target is more than 2 cells away. This spell generates Weak Point.", "Air"], "b:Sram:Wily": ["{AP} 3", "Teleports to behind target\n\n{Enemy} {Element Air} Damage: 3-105\n\n{Caster} Weak Point (+15 Lvl.)", "The Sram uses the Shadows to pass sneakily behind his target. This spell generates Weak Point.", "Air"], "b:Sram:Tricky Blow": ["{AP} 3", "{Enemy} {Element Air} Damage: 3-105\n{Caster} Move away 2 cells\n\nEach time the spell is cast:\n{Icon Arrow} Repeats the damage on the previous enemies (melee damage)\n{Icon Arrow} {Caster} Weak Point (+5 Lvl.) for each additional enemy hit\n\n{Caster} Weak Point (+15 Lvl.)", "Inflicts Air damage on enemies and moves the caster away from the target. Each time the spell is cast, the damage is repeated on the previous targets. This spell generates Weak Point. The Sram gains additional Weak Point for each enemy that suffers damage.", "Air"], "b:Sram:Fear": ["{AP} 3", "{Target} turns the target around\n{Enemy} {Element Air} Damage: 3-91\nIf the Sram consumed Weak Point during their turn:\n{Icon Arrow} {Enemy} {Element Air} Damage: 4-121 instead\n\n{Caster} Weak Point (+15 Lvl.)", "Turns the target around before inflicting damage on it. The damage is greater if the Sram consumed Weak Point during their turn. This spell generates Weak point.", "Air"], "b:Sram:Trauma": ["{AP} 4", "{Element Air} Damage: 4-141\nDamage is always melee\n\nEvery 50 Weak Point:\n{Icon Arrow} {Element Air} Damage: 1-35 extra\n{Icon Arrow} {Enemy} Hemorrhage (+10 Lvl.)\n{Icon Arrow} {Caster} regains {AP} 1 AP, {MP} 1 MP, {WP} 1 WP\n{Icon Arrow} {Caster} consumes the Weak Point used", "Inflicts Air damage that is always melee and consumes Weak Point to inflict additional damage. Depending on the amount of Weak Point consumed, the Sram regains AP, MP, and WP, and applies Hemorrhage on the target before inflicting damage. Hemorrhage inflicts additional damage on the target when the Sram inflicts direct damage on it.", "Air"], "b:Sram:Fear Neutral": ["{AP} 2", "Pushes the target in front of the Sram to the targeted cell.\nIf the pushed target is the Double: {Caster} {AP} 2 AP", "An adjustable pushback spell. The target facing the Sram is pushed onto the targeted cell. The Sram regains 2 AP if the pushed target is their Double.", "Neutral"], "b:Sram:Scram": ["{WP} 1", "{MP} 3 max MP (1 turn)\n{Dodge} 4 Dodge (1 turn)", "Allows the Sram or one of their allies to gain mobility.", "Neutral"], "b:Sram:Dirty Trick": ["{AP} 2\n{WP} 1", "Switches places with the Double\n\nUsing it a 2nd time in the same turn is free.", "Allows the Sram to switch places with their Double. Using it a second time in the same turn is free.", "Neutral"], "b:Sram:Deviousness": ["{AP} 2", "Deviousness (Lvl 1) (1 turn):\nIf the state bearer triggers one of the {Caster} Sram's traps:\n{Icon Arrow} The Sram teleports behind the target\n{Icon Arrow} The Deviousness state is removed", "The Sram marks the target for 1 turn. If the target triggers one of the Sram's traps, the Sram teleports behind it.", "Neutral"], "b:Sram:Assassination": ["{AP} 1\n{WP} 2", "{Enemy} {Elemental Resistance} -100 Elemental Resistance\n\nIf the target is still alive at end of turn:\n{Icon Arrow} {Enemy} {Elemental Resistance} 100 Elemental Resistance\n\nCan only be cast once per round per\nteam", "The Sram reduces the target's resistances in order to kill it. Ii it is still alive at end oi turn, it gains resistances for 1 turn. This spell can only be used once per round per team.", "Neutral"], "b:Sram:Stabber": ["{AP} 2", "At start of next turn:\n{Icon Arrow} {Damage Inflicted} 20% damage inflicted from behind\n{Icon Arrow} {Damage Inflicted} 20% damage inflicted on critical hit\n{Icon Arrow} Stabilized (current turn)", "On the next turn, the Sram gains damage inflicted as a critical hit and from behind, and becomes stabilized for the current turn.", "Neutral"], "b:Sram:Murderer": ["", "Upon killing an {Enemy} enemy:\n{Icon Arrow} {Caster} no longer gains Weak Point\n{Icon Arrow} {Caster} immediately regains {AP} 1 AP {MP} 1 MP {WP} 1 WP\n{Icon Arrow} {Caster} Healing: 20% of max HP", "The Sram no longer gains Weak Point upon killing an enemy but immediately regains 1 AP, 1 MP, 1 WP, and 20% of max HP instead."], "b:Sram:Dupery": ["", "After receiving direct damage:\n{Icon Arrow} {Caster} Switches places with their Double (1 time per fighter's turn)", "The Sram switches places with their Double after receiving direct damage."], "b:Sram:Fraud": ["", "Invisibility can no longer be can on an ally {Ally}\n\nInvisible is removed only on a 4-AP or more spell", "The Sram loses their invisibility when inflicting direct damage only when using a spell costing 4 AP or more. This means they can use smaller spells before revealing themself. In exchange, they can no longer turn an ally invisible."], "b:Sram:Hocus Pocus": ["", "The Double can be summoned from up to 4 Range in a straight line without line of sight\nWhen summoning the Double:\n{Icon Arrow} {Caster} Switches places with it\n{Icon Arrow} {Caster} Switches places again at end of turn", "When summoning the Double, the Sram switches places with it, before switching places with it again at the end of their turn."], "b:Sram:Ambush25": ["", "Traps no longer give AP back to the Sram\n{Caster} regains 1 WP upon triggering a trap\nWhen an enemy triggers one of the Sram's traps:\n{Icon Arrow} {Enemy} {Element Light} damage: 3-91 (melee damage)", "The Sram's traps no longer give the Sram AP back when triggered but inflict damage on enemies. The Sram regains 1 WP when their traps are triggered."], "b:Sram:Attraction Trap II": ["", "The Attraction Trap becomes Attraction Trap II:\n{Icon Arrow} The trap now applies in a 1-cell {Area Cross} cross area of effect\n{Icon Arrow} When triggered, targets are attracted toward the center of the trap", "The attraction trap works differently. The trap becomes a 1-cell cross area of effect and attracts targets toward the center of the trap."], "b:Sram:Sram to the Bone": ["", "The Double's Fear spell works differently:\n{Icon Arrow} The spell pulls the target into close combat with the Double", "The Double's Fear spell works differently. Targets are attracted toward the Double instead of being pushed back."], "b:Sram:Bloody Blade": ["", "At end of turn, converts enemies' Hemorrhage into Hemophilia (1 turn):\n{Icon Arrow} 4% of {Caster}'s level per level of Hemorrhage\n\nHemorrhage no longer adds damage to the Sram", "At the end of their turn, the Sram transforms their enemies' Hemorrhage into start-of-turn poison. This poison still inflicts melee damage."], "b:Sram:Repulsion Trap II": ["", "The Repulsion Trap becomes Repulsion Trap II:\n{Icon Arrow} The trap is no longer in an area of effect\n{Icon Arrow} When triggered, the target is pushed back 3 cells in the direction it is facing", "The repulsion trap works differently. When triggered, the trap becomes single-target and pushes the target in the direction it is facing."], "b:Sram:Crazy Scheme": ["", "At the start of the fight, Rear Mastery is converted into Melee Mastery\n\nThe Sram's damage no longer takes account of the target's orientation", "The Sram converts their rear damage into melee damage. In exchange, they no longer take account of their targets' orientation; targets are always considered to be facing the Sram."], "b:Sram:Ambush": ["", "The Double explodes if they suffer direct damage:\n{Icon Arrow} {Enemy} Hemorrhage (+20 Lvl.) {Size: 2}", "The Double explodes when it suffers direct damage, which applies Hemorrhage to enemies around it."], "b:Sram:Alternate Diversion": ["", "The Double's Diversion spell works differently:\n{Icon Arrow} The targets around the Double get turned around {Area Cross}", "The Double's Diversion spell works differently. Targets are turned around with their backs to the Double instead of facing the Double."], "b:Sram:Trap Master": ["", "The Teleportation Trap becomes Teleportation Trap II\n{Icon Arrow} The trap is not consumed when used\n{Icon Arrow} The trap lasts 1 turn\n{Icon Arrow} Teleportation is limited to 4 cells max\n{Icon Arrow} The trap is only triggered by allies {Ally}", "The teleportation trap works differently. The trap stays for 1 turn and is no longer consumed when used. Teleportation is limited to 4 cells max. Only allies can trigger the trap."], "b:Sram:Shadow Master": ["", "The Double's Lethal Mark works differently:\nIf the {Caster} Sram kills an {Enemy}:\n{Icon Arrow} {Caster} Regains {AP} 2 AP\n{Icon Arrow} {Caster} Teleports behind the {Target} mark bearer\n{Icon Arrow} {Target} The mark bearer recovers the Hemorrhage of the killed enemy", "The Double's lethal mark works differently. Instead of moving the mark bearer when the Sram kills an enemy, the Sram teleports right behind the mark bearer."], "b:Sram:Brutal Assault": ["", "Spells costing 4 AP or more no longer generate Weak Point; instead they inflict 5% additional damage per AP\n\nOnly spells that generate Weak Point in their base form are affected", "The Sram's costly spells do more damage but no longer generate Weak Point. The Execution and Trauma spells are no longer affected by this passive's effects."], "b:Eliotrope:Wakmeha": ["{AP} 4", "{Calm} Calm:\n{Icon Arrow} {Element Water} Damage: 4-131\nIf the spell goes through a Portal:\n{Icon Arrow} {Element Water} Damage: 1-32 extra\n\n{Exalted} Exalted:\n{Icon Arrow} {Element Water} Damage: 4-111, penetrates Armor\n{Icon Arrow} Target loses the same amount of Armor", "In calm mode, this spell deals heavy damage if cast through a portal. In exalted mode, it deals damage both on and under a target's armor at the same time.", "Water"], "b:Eliotrope:Pulsation": ["{AP} 2", "If no portals within 3 cells or less of the target:\n{Icon Arrow} {Enemy} {Element Water} Damage: 3-92\n{Icon Arrow} {Ally} {Element Water} Healing: 6-60\n\nOtherwise:\n{Icon Arrow} {Enemy} {Element Water} Damage: 2-60\n{Icon Arrow} {Ally} Healing: 4-33", "This spell inflicts single-target damage or heals an ally through portals in a flexible way. If no portals are within 3 cells or less of the target, the damage and healing are increased.", "Water"], "b:Eliotrope:Flood": ["{AP} 3", "{Calm} Calm:\n{Icon Arrow} Switches places\n\n{Exalted} Exalted:\n{Icon Arrow} {Caster} Teleports symmetrically to the target\n{Icon Arrow} The spell has 2 Range less\n\n{Enemy} {Element Water} Damage: 3-105\n{Ally} {Element Water} Healing: 6-57\n\nIf the spell goes through a portal, only the damage or healing is applied", "In calm mode, the Eliotrope switches places with their target. In exalted mode, the Eliotrope teleports symmetrically to their target. If this spell is cast through a portal, only the damage or healing is applied.", "Water"], "b:Eliotrope:Whirlwind": ["{AP} 2", "{Enemy} {Element Water} Damage: 2-60 {Size: 2}\n{Ally} {Element Water} Healing: 4-33 {Size: 2}\n\n{Calm} Calm:\n{Icon Arrow} Pushes back 2 cells {Size: 2}\n\n{Exalted} Exalted:\n{Icon Arrow} Attracts by 2 cells\n\nCan target any portal on the field starting from an entrance portal\nCan only be cast on Portal", "This spell can only be cast on an allied portal. Besides dealing damage and healing in an area of effect, it pushes targets in an area of effect around the portal (in calm mode) and attracts targets around the portal (in exalted mode).", "Water"], "b:Eliotrope:Cataclysm": ["{AP} 5", "{Calm} Calm: Places a Cataclysm\n{Icon Arrow} {Caster} cannot go through another Portal until the end of turn\nWhen Exaltation is cast, the Eliotrope:\n{Icon Arrow} Teleports to Cataclysm (trades places if the cell is occupied)\n{Icon Arrow} {Enemy} {Element Water} Damage: 7-195 (direct damage) {Size: 2}\n\n{Exalted} Exalted: {Element Water} Damage: 7-247", "In Calm mode, the Eliotrope deploys a Cataclysm area of effect on the field. The next time Exaltation is cast, they teleport to the area and then deal huge damage around them. In Exalted mode, the Eliotrope inflicts heavy damage on the target.", "Water"], "b:Eliotrope:Ardent Aegis": ["{AP} 3\n{WP} 1", "{Calm} Calm: {Enemy} {Element Earth} Damage: 4-111 {Size: 1}\n{Icon Arrow} Places the most distant Portal on the cell\n{Icon Arrow} Can only target a free cell\n\n{Exalted} Exalted: {Enemy} {Element Earth} Damage: 4-111\n\n{Icon Arrow} Places the most distant Portal on the target\n{Icon Arrow} Must target an occupied cell\n\n{Caster} Regains 1 WP if the Eliotrope has Celestial Gift", "This spells repositions a portal on a target or through another portal. If the Eliotrope has Celestial Gift when they cast the spell, the WP cost is refunded.", "Earth"], "b:Eliotrope:Deafening Targe": ["{AP} 3", "{Element Earth} Damage: 3-91\n{Calm} Calm: {AP} -2 AP\n{Exalted} Exalted: {MP} -2 MP\n\nRemoval effects are doubled if the Eliotrope consumes Celestial Gift", "This spell inflicts Earth damage and debuffs the target based on the Eliotrope's active mode. If the Eliotrope consumes the Celestial Gift on the spell, removal effects are doubled.", "Earth"], "b:Eliotrope:Earthquake": ["{AP} 4", "If {Caster} targets themself:\n{Icon Arrow} {Element Earth} Damage: 4-111 {Area Circlering}\n\n{Enemy}: Earthquake (+4 Lvl.) (4x max)", "If the Eliotrope targets themself, they inflict damage around them. If they target an enemy, they mark the enemy; the next time they cast Exaltation, the marked enemy will take indirect damage.", "Earth"], "b:Eliotrope:Clash": ["{AP} 4", "{Calm} Calm:\n{Icon Arrow} {Element Earth} Damage: 4-121 {Size: 1}\n\n{Exalted} Exalted:\n{Icon Arrow} {Element Earth} Damage: 4-121 {Size: 1}\n\n{Caster} Regains 1 AP per target killed if the Eliotrope consumes Celestial Gift", "Inflicts damage in a cross-shaped area of effect. In exalted mode, the area of effect is a diagonal cross. If the Eliotrope consumes Celestial Gift on this spell, they regain 1 AP for each target killed.", "Earth"], "b:Eliotrope:Hiding": ["{AP} 3", "{Element Earth} Damage: 3-98\n\nIf the target is on a Portal:\n{Icon Arrow} {Calm} Calm: Steals 100% of damage inflicted\n{Icon Arrow} {Exalted} Exalted: {Element Earth} Damage: 4-131 instead", "Inflicts Earth damage. If the target is on a portal, the Eliotrope is healed for the amount of damage they deal if in calm mode; their damage is increased if in exalted mode.", "Earth"], "b:Eliotrope:Torrential Flux": ["{AP} 4", "{Element Air} Damage: 4-102 {Size: 5}\nPlaces Wakfu Trail (lvl. 2-63) {Size: 5}\n\nIf the spell goes through a Portal:\n{Icon Arrow} {Element Air} Damage: 5-164\n{Icon Arrow} The destination portal destroyed", "Inflicts damage in a line. Enemies starting or ending their turn in the area where the spell was cast take extra damage. When cast through a portal, the Eliotrope inflicts major damage on the target, but the destination portal is destroyed.", "Air"], "b:Eliotrope:Siphon": ["{AP} 2", "{Enemy} {Element Air} Damage: 2-75\n{Ally} {Element Air} Healing: 4-40\n\n{Calm} Calm:\n{Icon Arrow} Pushes back 1 cell\n\n{Exalted} Exalted\n{Icon Arrow} Attracts by 1 cell", "This spell inflicts Air damage on enemies and heals allies, in addition to pushing or attracting (based on what mode the Eliotrope is in).", "Air"], "b:Eliotrope:Ethereal Burst": ["{AP} 3", "{Element Air} Damage: 3-105\n\n{Calm} Calm:\n{Icon Arrow} Incurable (Lvl 4)\n\n{Exalted} Exalted:\n{Icon Arrow} Crumbly (Lvl 4)", "Inflicts Air damage and gives the target a healing received penalty (in calm mode) or an armor received penalty (in exalted mode).", "Air"], "b:Eliotrope:Tempest": ["{AP} 5", "{Element Air} Damage: 5-164 {Size: 1}\n\nIf this spell is cast on Portal:\n{Icon Arrow} {Element Air} Damage: 5-164 {Size: 1} replicated around each Portal\n{Icon Arrow} A fighter can only take the damage once\n{Icon Arrow} The Portals are destroyed", "Inflicts damage in an area of effect. If this spell is cast on a portal, the area-of-effect damage is dealt around each portal currently on the field, and the portals are destroyed.", "Air"], "b:Eliotrope:Unleashed Blade": ["{AP} 5", "{Element Air} Damage: 5-176\n\nIf the target is on a Portal:\n{Icon Arrow} {Element Air} Damage: 7-247 instead", "This spell inflicts heavy damage on the target, but can only be cast on an adjacent target. The target will take greater damage if it is on a portal.", "Air"], "b:Eliotrope:Coalition": ["{AP} 2", "Removes all allied Portal from the field\nPlaces a new Portal on the targeted cell\n\n{Caster} Recovers 1 AP per Portal removed", "Enables the Eliotrope to destroy all allied portals on the field and instantly place a new one on the targeted cell, in order to more efficiently change how their portals are set up.", "Neutral"], "b:Eliotrope:Wakfu Imprint": ["{WP} 2", "{Ally} 5% of the {Caster}'s max HP as Armor\n{Enemy} 10% of the {Caster}'s max HP as Armor removal\n\nIf the spell is cast through a Portal:\n{Icon Arrow} The effects are doubled", "On an ally, applies Armor that absorbs the next attacks received. On an enemy, removes Armor. The effects are doubled if the spell goes through a portal.", "Neutral"], "b:Eliotrope:Time Breach": ["{AP} 2\n{WP} 1", "{Calm} Calm: Teleports to the cell\n\n{Exalted} Exalted:\n{Icon Arrow} Teleports to the nearest Portal (6 cells max)\n{Icon Arrow} Destroys the Portal\n\nThis spell cannot pass through a portal {Calm} It can target any {Ally} portal on the field", "The Eliotrope can teleport to the targeted cell if they are in Calm mode. In Exalted mode, the target is teleported to the closest portal.", "Neutral"], "b:Eliotrope:Exodus": ["{AP} 1\n{WP} 1", "Cast on an empty cell:\n{Icon Arrow} Replaces the nearest Portal\n\nCast on a target:\n{Icon Arrow} Switches places with the nearest free portal (up to 4 cells away)", "When cast on an empty cell, this spell moves a nearby portal to the targeted cell. Cast on a target, the target switches places with the nearest free portal.", "Neutral"], "b:Eliotrope:Incandescence": ["{AP} 1", "Per portal in the {Size: 3} area (max 2):\n{Icon Arrow} {Enemy} {Element Light} Damage: 3-91\nStabilized (Lvl 1)", "Stabilizes the target. If the target is an opponent, they suffer damage based on the number of portals near the target.", "Neutral"], "b:Eliotrope:Barrier": ["{AP} 2\n{WP} 1", "Deploys a Barrier (1 turn) {Area Circle} (2)\n{Icon Arrow} {Ally} -20% damage received\n{Icon Arrow} {Enemy} -3 MP (1x per turn)\n\nCan only be cast on a Portal", "When cast on a portal, this spell places a barrier that shields any allies standing on it and debuffs any enemies that pass through it.", "Neutral"], "b:Eliotrope:Trapster": ["", "When {Caster} has Celestial Gift:\n{Icon Arrow} 60% damage inflicted from behind on the next damage spell\n{Icon Arrow} No longer gives the base 40% damage inflicted", "Celestial Gift provides a very high damage bonus, but only if the target has its back to the Eliotrope."], "b:Eliotrope:Resilience": ["", "On gaining Celestial Gift:\n{Icon Arrow} {Caster} Armor gain: 10% of max HP\n{Icon Arrow} {Caster} No longer recovers WP", "The Eliotrope no longer recovers WP upon gaining Celestial Gift. Instead, they gain Armor to absorb incoming attacks."], "b:Eliotrope:Medium": ["", "Celestial Portal no longer costs AP\n\nUpon gaining Celestial Gift:\n{Icon Arrow} {Caster} {MP} 2 max MP (1 turn)", "Celestial Portal no longer costs AP to cast, but Celestial Gift gives an MP bonus instead of an AP bonus."], "b:Eliotrope:Fury": ["", "Upon casting Celestial Portal:\n{Icon Arrow} Directly gains Celestial Gift\n\nAP bonus from Celestial Gift maxes out at 1 time per turn", "The Eliotrope gains Celestial Gift instantly after casting the Celestial Portal spell. However, the AP bonus from Celestial Gift maxes out at 1 time per turn."], "b:Eliotrope:Transitory": ["", "When {Caster} {Ally} uses a Portal (1 time per turn):\n{Icon Arrow} 2 MP (1 turn)\n{Icon Arrow} Can no longer use portals until the turn ends", "If the Eliotrope or an ally goes through a Portal, they gain MP for the current turn. In exchange, they can no longer use portals to move until the following turn. This passive applies to all of the team's portals."], "b:Eliotrope:Effervescence": ["", "After casting the Exaltation spell:\n{Icon Arrow} Connection: 50% damage inflicted for the next spell\n\nThe damage bonus from {Calm} Calm lasts only 1 turn", "This passive allows the Eliotrope to deal much greater damage with their next spell after changing modes. In exchange, the damage bonus from Calm lasts only one turn."], "b:Eliotrope:Celestial Portal": ["", "At start of turn:\n{Icon Arrow} {Caster} teleports to the nearest Portal", "The Eliotrope teleports to the closest portal at the start of the turn."], "b:Eliotrope:Portal Disciple": ["", "After casting the Exaltation spell:\n{Icon Arrow} A portal is created under the Eliotrope\n{Icon Arrow} The portal cannot be moved and disappears at end of turn\n{Icon Arrow} The portal can exceed the limit of 4\n{Icon Arrow} {Caster} can no longer use the Portal spell for the current turn", "This passive allows the Eliotrope to create a temporary portal under them when they cast the Exaltation spell. The portal can exceed the limit of 4, but it cannot be moved and will disappear at the end of the turn. In exchange, the Eliotrope can no longer use the Portal spell until the end of their turn."], "b:Eliotrope:Reminiscence": ["", "Exaltation has 4 Range\n\nAt end of turn:\n{Icon Arrow} If {Calm} Calm, enters {Exalted} Exalted\n{Icon Arrow} If {Exalted} Exalted, enters {Calm} Calm", "The Eliotrope automatically changes modes at end of turn. Also, they can cast Exaltation on another ally from a distance."], "b:Eliotrope:Interstellar": ["", "Using a portal more than 6 cells away no longer applies Long Teleportation:\n{Icon Arrow} The starting portal is destroyed instead\n{Icon Arrow} {Caster} Regains 1 max WP", "Allies that use one of the Eliotrope's portals more than 6 cells away are no longer affected by Long Teleportation, but the starting portal is destroyed. This passive applies to all of the team's portals."], "b:Eliotrope:White Dimension": ["", "At start of turn, on targets adjacent to Portal:\n{Icon Arrow} {Calm} Calm 40% Critical hit (1 turn)\n{Icon Arrow} {Exalted} Exalted -40% Critical hit (1 turn)", "Fighters around portals gain Critical Hits at the start of the Eliotrope's turn if the Eliotrope is in Calm mode, and lose Critical Hits if the Eliotrope is Exalted."], "b:Eliotrope:Quietude": ["", "After casting the Exaltation spell:\n{Icon Arrow} {AP} 3 AP\n\nExaltation no longer gives damage inflicted to the caster", "The Eliotrope regains AP (instead of gaining a damage inflicted bonus) when the Exaltation spell is cast."], "b:Eliotrope:Spacetime": ["", "A Portal disappears after 2 turns", "Instead of lasting indefinitely, portals last for 2 turns. This passive applies to all of the team's portals."], "b:Eliotrope:Porta(i)l": ["", "The Portal spell has 2 Range more\nDamage and heals performed through portals are increased by an additional 15%\nPortal are capped at 2\n\nIf 2 portals are already on the field:\nPortal moves the nearest portal to the cell", "The Eliotrope now has just two portals, but they can move them around more easily and at a greater distance. Also, their damage and heals performed through portals are increased."], "b:Eliotrope:Final Shield": ["", "When {Caster} {Ally} uses a Portal:\n{Icon Arrow} {Element Physical} Healing: 10% of HP max of the target {Fixed: The value is not influenced by the caster's damage.} (1/tour)\n{Icon Arrow} 2 AP\n\nPortals can only be placed adjacent to a fighter", "The Eliotrope must place their portals adjacent to a fighter. In return, allies who use their portals are healed and gain AP. This passive applies to all of the team's portals."], "b:Eliotrope:Novice Sword": ["", "-1 Range on all spells\n\nCasting a spell on an adjacent target increases Celestial Portal - Counter", "The Eliotrope can get Celestial Gift by casting spells on adjacent targets. In exchange, the maximum range of all of their spells is reduced."], "b:Eliotrope:Healing": ["", "If the Eliotrope ends their turn with {Calm} Calm:\n{Icon Arrow} {Caster} 15% of missing HP healed \n(plus 15% more if the {Caster} is on a portal\n{Icon Arrow} {Caster} {WP} -1 WP", "The Eliotrope is healed for part of their missing HP when ending their turn in Calm mode, in exchange for one WP. If they are on a portal, the healing is greater."], "b:Eliotrope:Concentration": ["", "Celestial Portal:\n{Icon Arrow} Now has 4 Range (fixed)\n{Icon Arrow} Costs 1 WP less\n{Icon Arrow} On a free cell, replaces the closest portal\n{Icon Arrow} Now limited to 2 uses per turn", "Celestial Portal is more useful and can be cast multiple times per turn. In exchange, it is harder to cast."], "b:Eliotrope:Meditation": ["", "When starting turn in {Calm} mode with Calm:\n{Icon Arrow} {Caster} 1 map MP and 50 elemental Resistance (2 turns)\n{Icon Arrow} {Caster} No longer gains damage inflicted\n\nCelestial Gift also grants 20% Heals performed", "The Eliotrope no longer gains damage by starting their turn in Calm mode, but gains MP and elemental resistance instead. Celestial Gift is also consumed if heals are performed, which then boosts healing."], "b:Eliotrope:Breath of the Goddess": ["", "When casting the Portal spell on an ally while standing on a portal:\n{Icon Arrow} {Caster} {Ally} Switches places\n{Icon Arrow} Does not place a portal", "If the Eliotrope casts the Portal spell on an ally while standing on a portal, they switch places, but the caster does not place a new portal."], "b:Xelor:Disruption": ["{AP} 3", "{Element Fire} Damage: 3-83 {Area Hline}\n\nIf the current hour is odd:\n{Icon Arrow} {Element Fire} Damage: 3-83 {Area Vline} instead", "Inflicts area-of-effect damage over 5 cells in front of the Xelor.", "Fire"], "b:Xelor:Suspension": ["{AP} 4", "{Caster} Stabilized until the end of the current turn\n{Element Fire} Damage: 4-131\n\nCast on the Dial:\n{Icon Arrow} The current hour stops advancing\n{Icon Arrow} {Caster} Temporal Suspension (+2 Lvl.)\n{Icon Arrow} {Caster} regains 2 AP\n{Icon Arrow} {Caster} For each WP spent Temporal Suspension (+1 Lvl.)\n\nNext time it is cast on the Dial:\n{Icon Arrow} Consumes the Temporal Suspension to move the current hour forward\n{Icon Arrow} {Caster} regains {AP} 2 AP", "This spell stabilizes the Xelor until the end of their turn while inflicting Fire damage. When cast on the dial, the current hour freezes, and all its forward movement is saved in a state. The next time it is cast on the dial, the state is consumed to move the current hour forward in one go.", "Fire"], "b:Xelor:Dark Bolt": ["{AP} 5", "{Element Fire} Damage: 3-97\n\nRebounds on an enemy (1 to 2 cells)\n{Icon Arrow} Rebound: {Element Fire} Damage: 7-181", "Inflicts Fire damage on the spell's target. Then a rebound happens and damage is inflicted on another enemy present near the spell's target.", "Fire"], "b:Xelor:Hand": ["{AP} 4", "{Element Fire} Damage: 4-111\n\nIf this spell kills a fighter, {Caster} the spell cost is reimbursed", "Inflicts Fire damage from a distance. The spell cost varies: It consumes all of the caster's AP, up to 4 AP. If this spell kills a fighter, the spell cost is reimbursed immediately.", "Fire"], "b:Xelor:Dust": ["{AP} 3", "{Element Fire} Damage: 3-105\n\nEach time the spell is cast, mininum range and maximum range increase by 2", "With each use, this spell increases its minimum and maximum casting ranges. This spell does not require a line of sight. It can therefore be cast through any obstacle to inflict great damage.", "Fire"], "b:Xelor:Hammhour": ["{AP} 3", "{Element Water} Damage: 3-83\n{AP} -1 AP\n\nEach time the spell is cast:\n{Icon Arrow} Repeats its effects on the previous targets", "Inflicts damage and reduces the target's AP.", "Water"], "b:Xelor:Slow Down": ["{AP} 1\n{WP} 1", "{Enemy} {Element Water} Damage: 1-35\n{This spell can be casted on oneself} {Force of Will} 15 Force of Will\n{Target} {AP} -2 AP", "This very inexpensive spell boosts the Xelor's Force of Will for one turn (resistance and removal capacity). This spell is even craftier when the Xelor later attempts to remove AP from the target.", "Water"], "b:Xelor:Clock": ["{AP} 5", "{Element Water} Damage: 6-182 at end of the target's turn\n\nEvery 12 WP regained:\n{Icon Arrow} The spell's effects are doubled", "Applies an indirect damage state. When the Xelor regains 12 Wakfu points in combat, the next Clock spell is twice as powerful.", "Water"], "b:Xelor:Sandglass": ["{AP} 3", "{Target} applies Sandglass:\nAt start of the state bearer's turn:\n{Icon Arrow} {Enemy} {Element Water} Damage: 4-121 {Area Cross}\n{Icon Arrow} Triggers the other Sandglass {Area Cross}", "Applies an indirect damage state. At the start of the spell's target's turn, the Xelor inflicts damage in an area of effect on the target and adjacent enemies, and triggers other sandglasses in the area of effect.", "Water"], "b:Xelor:Desynchronization": ["{AP} 4", "{Enemy} {Element Water} Damage: 4-102 {Area Cross}\n{AP} -3 AP {Area Cross}\n\nCast on the Dial (1 time per turn):\n{Icon Arrow} The current hour advances by 6\n{Icon Arrow} {Caster} regains 2 AP", "Reduces AP in an area of effect while inflicting Water damage. Cast on the dial, the current hour advances by 6 hours.", "Water"], "b:Xelor:Tempus Fugit": ["{AP} 3", "{Enemy} {Element Air} Damage: 3-76\nThe target is teleported to the current hour (6 cells max)\n\nCast on the Dial:\n{Icon Arrow} The Dial is moved to the Current Hour\n{Icon Arrow} {Caster} regains {AP} 2 AP", "The spell's target is teleported to the current hour cell on the dial (6 cells maximum). When cast on the dial, the dial is moved to the current hour.", "Air"], "b:Xelor:Underhand": ["{AP} 2", "{Enemy} {Element Air} Damage: 2-60\n\nTeleports the target 2 cells farther\nSwitches places if the cell is occupied\n{Icon Arrow} {Caster} regains 1 AP if the switch is successful", "The target is teleported two cells back.", "Air"], "b:Xelor:Paradox": ["{AP} 4", "Teleports the targets in the area of effect symmetrically in relation to the center\n\n{Enemy} {Element Air} Damage: 4-102 {Area Cross}", "Teleports the targets within the spell's area of effect symmetrically in relation to the targeted cell.\nTargets that are symmetrically opposite to each other switch places.", "Air"], "b:Xelor:Symmetry": ["{AP} 3", "Teleports symmetrically in relation to the target\n\n{Enemy} {Element Air} Damage: 3-76\n\nIf the current hour is odd:\n{Icon Arrow} Teleports symmetrically in relation to the Xelor", "This spell allows the Xelor to teleport symmetrically in relation to its target or vice versa, depending on the current hour. If the destination cell is occupied by an obstacle, the fighter switches places with it.", "Air"], "b:Xelor:Spontaneous Return": ["{AP} 3", "{Enemy} {Element Air} Damage: 3-98\n\nThe last movement not using MP during the Xelor's turn is canceled", "This spell cancels the last movement executed on the Xelor's turn. Whether from a pushback, attraction, teleportation, or position swap, the last target to have moved returns to its previous position.", "Air"], "b:Xelor:Devotion": ["{WP} 4", "At start of turn:\n{Icon Arrow} {AP} 3 max AP (1 turn)", "Increases AP on an ally for one turn.", "Neutral"], "b:Xelor:Against the Clock": ["{AP} 2", "{Target} Applies Against the Clock (Lvl 1)\nAt end of the target's turn:\n{Icon Arrow} Teleports the target to its start-of-turn position\n\nIf the target is the Xelor or one of their summons:\n{Icon Arrow} Teleports to the position when the spell was cast\n\ncan no longer be targeted by the spell for 4 turn", "At the end of this spell's target's turn, the target is teleported to their start-of-turn cell. If the cell is occupied by an obstacle, the target of the spell and the obstacle switch places.", "Neutral"], "b:Xelor:Sinistro": ["{AP} 2", "Summons a Sinistro (max 1 per Xelor)\n\nAt end of the Xelor's turn, {Size: 2} allies receive:\n{Icon Arrow} {Ally} Healing: 2% of missing HP per Sinistro Charge\n{Icon Arrow} {Ally} {AP} 1 AP for 5 Sinistro Charge", "Summons a Sinistro. This summons does not play a turn. Fighters near the Sinistro gain one AP.", "Neutral"], "b:Xelor:Cog": ["{AP} 2", "Summons a Cog (max 1 per Xelor)\n\nAt end of the Xelor's turn, per level of Cog Charge:\n{Icon Arrow} {Element Light} Damage: 1-20 around the Cog", "Summons a Cog. This summons does not play a turn. By moving fighters, the Xelor generates charges; based on the charges, the Cog deals damage around its position when the Xelor ends their turn.", "Neutral"], "b:Xelor:Premonition": ["{AP} 3", "Saves the target's HP and freezes them at that value on the Xelor's next turn\n\nIf the target gains or loses 50% of their HP:\n{Icon Arrow} The state is removed\n\nCast on an empty cell:\n{Icon Arrow} The Xelor teleports onto it on next turn", "This spell saves the target's HP. On the Xelor's next turn, the HP are set back to this value, thereby canceling any HP gains or losses that have happened in the meantime.", "Neutral"], "b:Xelor:Regulator": ["{WP} 3", "Summons a Regulator (max 1 per Xelor)\n\nCatches direct damage suffered by the other summons of the Xelor (Dial, Sinistro, or Cog)", "Summons a Regulator. The Regulator redirects the damage taken by the Xelor's other summons (Dial, Sinistro, and Cog) toward itself.", "Neutral"], "b:Xelor:Timeliness": ["", "When the current hour is even:\n{Icon Arrow} Spells are cast without line of sight\n{Icon Arrow} Spells are only cast in a straight line", "Depending on the current hour's position when the dial is summoned, the Xelor's elemental spells are cast without line of sight, meaning they can target through obstacles. However, these spells can only be cast in a straight line."], "b:Xelor:Dial Master": ["", "When the current hour goes around the Dial:\n{Icon Arrow} Delayed effects are instantly applied", "Delayed effects (those with Sinistro, Sandglass, Against the Clock, etc.) are also triggered when the current hour goes around the dial."], "b:Xelor:Portent": ["", "{Caster} 1 WP per AP reduction (1 time per {Target})\n\nThe Xelor does not regenerate WP based on\nAP at end of turn", "The Xelor regains WP when they reduce an enemy's AP. However, the Xelor no longer regains WP based on their remaining AP at the end of the turn."], "b:Xelor:Tick, Tock": ["", "Odd turns: 20 Force of Will\n\nEven turns: -20 Force of Will", "Reduces Force of Will on even turns and increases it on odd turns. In order to make full use of this passive's potential, the Xelor can keep resources from one turn to the next to use them at the right time."], "b:Xelor:Tock, Tick": ["", "Odd turns: -20% Damage inflicted\n\nEven turns: 20% Damage inflicted", "Increases the damage inflicted during even turns, and reduces it during odd turns. In order to make full use of this passive's potential, the Xelor can keep resources from one turn to the next to use them at the right time."], "b:Xelor:Clockmaking": ["", "At start of turn, the Xelor teleports to the current hour\n\nDial changes to 2 turns to recast", "The Xelor is teleported to the current hour on their Dial at the start of each turn. If the current hour cell is occupied by an obstacle, the Xelor switches places with the obstacle."], "b:Xelor:Memory": ["", "{WP} 6 WP\n\nAt start of fight:\n{Icon Arrow} -2 max MP", "Gains a large amount of WP while losing mobility through an MP restriction."], "b:Xelor:Course of Time": ["", "For each transposition caused by the Xelor:\n{Icon Arrow} {Caster} regains 1 AP if Distortion is active\n{Icon Arrow} Otherwise, {Caster} regenerates 1 WP\n\nDistortion takes 3 turns to recast", "Transpositions caused by the Xelor's spells or passives make the Xelor regain 1 AP or 1 WP."], "b:Xelor:Counterclockwise": ["", "Even turn: Reverses the rotation of the current hour", "Every other turn, the current hour goes the other way."], "b:Xelor:Déjà Vu": ["", "When the current hour is odd:\n{Icon Arrow} -25% Damage inflicted\n{Icon Arrow} 25% health steal", "Depending on the current hour's position when the dial is summoned, the Xelor's damage is reduced but regenerates the Xelor's health."], "b:Xelor:Knowledge of the Past": ["", "The Dial has 50% additional HP\n\nThe Dial costs 2 extra WP", "The dial is more resistant but costs more to summon."], "b:Xelor:Violent Omens": ["", "30% indirect damage inflicted\n\nAt start of turn, on the current hour:\n{Icon Arrow} {Element Light} damage: 7", "The current hour inflicts high damage on any fighter starting their turn on it."], "b:Xelor:Dark Dimension": ["", "The current hour gives a bonus of 30 Force of Wil\n\nAP removals can only be inflicted from the current hour or with\nPunctuality", "The current hour gives a Force of Will bonus, improving the Xelor's ability to remove AP. However, the Xelor's AP removals can now only happen from the current hour or if they have Punctuality."], "b:Xelor:Slowdown of Time": ["", "Increases the size of the Dial\n\nElemental spells can only be cast from an hour cell when a Dial is play", "The Dial spreads its hour cells over a 6-cell ring rathe than a 3-cell ring. Each hour cell is 4 cells from the next, unlike the Dial's standard layout (2 cells)."], "b:Xelor:Remanence": ["", "Summons no longer block line of sight\n\n+1 Sinistro and +1 Cog max", "The Xelor's summons (Dial, Sinistro, Cog Regulator) can no longer block line of sight; enemy and ally spells can go through them."], "b:Xelor:Specialized Mechanisms": ["", "On summoning a Cog, Sinistro, Dial, or Regulator:\n{Icon Arrow} Immediately switches places with it (6 cells max)", "The Xelor's summons (Dial, Sinistro, Cog and Regulator) gain an ability: When one is summoned, the Xelor immediately switches places with it (within a maximum Range of 6 cells)."], "b:Xelor:Momentary Permutation": ["", "At end of the Xelor's turn:\n{Icon Arrow} Switches places with the dial\n\nThe Dial gains 100 Elemental Resistance", "The Dial, which is Stabilized, can be repositioned anywhere on the field with this passive. The Xelor switches places with their Dial at the end of every turn."], "b:Xelor:Combat Mage": ["", "Transforms AP removals in melee\n{Icon Arrow} No longer removes AP\n{Icon Arrow} -3% damage inflicted (1 turn) (max 30)", "AP removals in melee combat (within 2 cells or less of the Xelor) are replaced with a damage penalty on the target."], "b:Xelor:Shriveling": ["", "Transforms ranged AP removals\n{Icon Arrow} No longer removes AP\n{Icon Arrow} {Element Light} damage: 1 at start of turn", "AP removals from a distance (3 or more cells from the Xelor) are replaced by application of indirect damage on the target."], "b:Xelor:Assimilation": ["", "{WP} -6 max WP\n\nWhen the Xelor kills a fighter (including allies and summons):\n{Icon Arrow} {Caster} Regenerates 2 WP", "Lowers the Xelor's WP gauge, but gives them greater WP regeneration capacity."], "b:Rogue:Barbed Fire": ["{AP} 4", "{Element Fire} Damage: 4-121 {Area Cross}\n\nCast on {Icon Bomb}\n{Icon Arrow} Attracts by 2 cells {Size: 3}\n{Icon Arrow} {Enemy} {Element Fire} Damage: 4-121 {Size: 3}", "The Rogue inflicts Fire damage in an area of effect. It they directly target a bomb, the area Of effect is increased, and the targets around the bomb are attracted adjacent to it.", "Fire"], "b:Rogue:Sticky Bomb": ["{AP} 2\n{WP} 1", "{Target} Sticky Bomb (Lvl 4-111)\nIf the target dies or 3 turns go by:\n{Icon Arrow} {Element Fire} Damage: 4-111\n\nCast on {Icon Bomb}:\n{Icon Arrow} Stabilized\n{Icon Arrow} The {Icon Bomb} explodes if it takes damage\n\nCannot place {Icon Bomb}", "Places a sticky bomb on the target. When the target dies or three turns go by, an explosion is triggered around the target. It the target is a bomb, it is stabilized (can no longer be moved) and explodes if it suffers damage.", "Fire"], "b:Rogue:Execution": ["{AP} 3", "{Enemy} Execution (Lvl 1) :\n{Elemental Resistance} -50 Elemental Resistance\nIf the Rogue {Caster} kills the target during their turn:\n{Icon Arrow} {Caster} {AP} 2 AP\n\n{Element Fire} Damage: 5-98", "Removes elemental resistances from the target before inflicting Fire damage on it. If the Rogue kills the target during their turn, they regain Powder and AP.", "Fire"], "b:Rogue:Crosswise": ["{AP} 2", "{Element Fire} Damage: 2-65\nAttracts by 5 cells the {Icon Bomb} {Area Cross}", "This shot can only be cast on the diagonal, but has very long range. It's ideal for those hard-to-reach places and can turn blind spots into dead targets.\nBombs aligned with the target are pulled toward the point of impact.", "Fire"], "b:Rogue:Perforation": ["{AP} 5\n{WP} 1", "If the target has Armor:\n{Icon Arrow} {Element Fire} Damage: 3-98 (on Armor)\n{Enemy} {Element Fire} Damage: 6-197\n{Icon Arrow} Escapist: Damage is always 'ranged\n{Icon Arrow} Sneaky: Damage is always melee\n\nThe effect is spread behind each target hit {Area Vline}", "Inflicts major damage in an area of effect. Additional damage is inflicted on the targets' Armor.", "Fire"], "b:Rogue:Machine Gun": ["{AP} 2", "{Enemy} {Element Earth} Damage: 3-98\n{Caster} Moves away 2 cells\n\nCast on {Icon Bomb}:\n{Icon Arrow} Teleports the {Icon Bomb} 2 cells farther\n{Icon Arrow} Switches places if the cell is occupied", "While keeping their distance, the Rogue can mow down anyone foolish enough to get in their crosshairs. If the spell is cast on a bomb, it is teleported 2 cells farther. If the cell is occupied, the bomb switches places with the target.", "Earth"], "b:Rogue:Blunderbuss": ["{AP} 3", "{Element Earth} Damage: 3-91\nPushes back 2 cells\n\n{Caster} Escapist:\n{Icon Arrow} Effects are applied in a {Size: 2}", "Inflicts damage and pushes the target. If the spell is cast in Runaway mode, the effects are applied in a cone.", "Earth"], "b:Rogue:Encumbering Shot": ["{AP} 4", "{Element Earth} Damage: 4-131\n{MP} -3 MP\n\nCast on {Icon Bomb}:\n{Icon Arrow} Effects are applied in a {Size: 3}", "This spell removes MP from the Rogue's target. If the spell is cast on a bomb, the effects are applied in a straight line.", "Earth"], "b:Rogue:Boomerang Dagger": ["{AP} 3", "{Caster} Sneaky:\n{Icon Arrow} {Element Earth} Damage: 3-91\n{Icon Arrow} Applies an additional level of Dagger Return\n\n{Caster} Escapist:\n{Icon Arrow} {Element Earth} Damage: 3-91 in a {Area Boomerang} boomerang area of effect\n{Icon Arrow} Applies 1 level of Dagger Return {Area Boomerang}\n{Icon Arrow} Does not trigger Dagger Return", "In Sneaky mode, the Rogue inflicts damage on their target and applies an additional level of Dagger Return. In Runaway mode, the Rogue inflicts damage in a boomerang area of effect and applies a level of Dagger Return on targets hit instead of triggering them.", "Earth"], "b:Rogue:Pulsar": ["{AP} 2\n{WP} 1", "On the Rogue {Caster}:\n{Icon Arrow} Pulsar (+1 Lvl.)\n\nOn another target:\n{Icon Arrow} {Element Earth} Damage: 3-91\nPer level of Pulsar:\n{Icon Arrow} {Element Earth} Damage: 3-91 extra", "The Rogue can charge their Pulsar to deal devastating damage.", "Earth"], "b:Rogue:Slap Shot": ["{AP} 2", "{Element Air} Damage: 2-55\n{Caster} {MP} 1 MP (1 turn)\n\nCast on {Icon Bomb}:\n{Icon Arrow} The {Icon Bomb} gains 1 level", "The Rogue inflicts Air damage and gains 1 MP. If the spell is cast on a bomb, the bomb loses a level, and the Rogue regains 1 Powder.", "Air"], "b:Rogue:Cheating": ["{AP} 3", "{Element Air} Damage: 3-83 and steals 100%\n\nCast on {Icon Bomb}:\n{Icon Arrow} {Caster} Switches places with it", "The Rogue steals health from the target. If the spell is cast on a bomb, the Rogue switches places with it.", "Air"], "b:Rogue:Longsword": ["{AP} 4", "{Element Air} Damage: 5-164\nSneaky Blade (Lvl 2-82) :\nOn the next mode change:\n{Icon Arrow} {Element Air} Damage: 2-82", "In addition to inflicting Air damage, the Rogue applies an effect on the target: When the Rogue next changes modes, the target suffers additional damage.", "Air"], "b:Rogue:Carbine": ["{AP} 4", "{Enemy} {Element Air} Damage: 4-102\n\n2 rebounds in {Size: 1-3}:\n{Icon Arrow} 1st: {Enemy} {Element Air} Damage: 5-127\n{Icon Arrow} 2nd: {Enemy} {Element Air} Damage: 6-153\n\nIf a bomb was used for a rebound:\n{Icon Arrow} 10% extra damage", "This shot rebounds from one enemy to another, inflicting more and more damage. The Rogue's bombs are included in the rebounds, but do not take damage from them.", "Air"], "b:Rogue:Obliteration": ["{AP} 4\n{WP} 1", "{Element Air} Damage: 4-111\n\nPer level of {Icon Bomb} exploded since last use:\n{Icon Arrow} 4% extra damage (max 200)", "Inflicts Air damage on the target. Damage is increased after causing bombs to explode. This bonus is based on the total level of bombs that have exploded since the spell was last used.", "Air"], "b:Rogue:Boot": ["{AP} 1\n{WP} 1", "Moves a bomb onto the targeted cell\n{Icon Arrow} is the closest bomb\n{Icon Arrow} must be on the same line as the Rogue and the targeted cell\n\nOn the Rogue {Caster} or a {Icon Bomb}:\n{Icon Arrow} Pushes back one cell {Area Cross}", "The Rogue grabs the closest bomb, in the same line or diagonally, and moves it to the targeted cell. If the spell is cast on a bomb or the caster, nearby targets are pushed back 1 cell.", "Neutral"], "b:Rogue:Smoke Bombs": ["{WP} 1", "{Ally} Smoke Bombs (1 turn)\nReduces ranged damage suffered by 20%\nDoes not block lines of sight\nImmune to damage from allied {Icon Bomb}\n\n{Enemy} Smoke Bombs (1 turn)\nReduces ranged damage inflicted by 20%\nDoes not block lines of sight", "Smoke Bombs reduces an ally's ranged damage received, or reduces an enemy's ranged damage inflicted. In addition, the target no longer blocks line of sight. If the target is an ally, they become immune to damage from the Rogue's bombs.", "Neutral"], "b:Rogue:Claw": ["{MP} 1\n{WP} 1", "Escapist: {Caster} Comes right up to the target\n\nSneaky: {Caster} Pulls target into close combat, then goes behind the target", "In Runaway mode, the Rogue uses their claw to get close to a fighter. In Sneaky mode, the Rogue attracts the target, then moves behind them.", "Neutral"], "b:Rogue:Evanescence": ["{AP} 2\n{WP} 1", "Teleports to the other side of the bomb, at equal distance\n\n{Caster} Escapist or Sneaky\nOn the next spell in the {Caster} Rogue's other mode:\n{Icon Arrow} {Element Light} Damage: 3-91", "The Rogue uses a bomb as a pivot to teleport to the other side.", "Neutral"], "b:Rogue:Magnet": ["{WP} 2", "Attracts by 3 cells all aligned fighters {Area Cross}\n\nThis spell must target a bomb", "This spell must target one of the Rogue's bombs. It pulls all aligned fighters 2 cells closer, with no distance limit.", "Neutral"], "b:Rogue:Fusillade": ["{AP} 3", "Makes all {Icon Bomb} explode\n\nFor each {Icon Bomb} destroyed, for 2 turns:\n{Icon Arrow} 10% damage inflicted on direct damage\n{Icon Arrow} 1 MP\n\n{Caster} {AP} 1 AP", "The Rogue enters Fusillade mode for 2 turns, making all their bombs explode and gaining a boost to their direct damage inflicted and their MP.", "Neutral"], "b:Rogue:Powder Trail": ["", "When summoning a bomb:\n{Icon Arrow} {Caster} {Armor} Armor: 5% of max HP\n{Icon Arrow} {Caster} no longer gains {MP} MP", "The Rogue gains Armor instead of 1 MP when placing a bomb."], "b:Rogue:Boomarogue": ["", "The Boombot:\n{Icon Arrow} Gains 2 extra AP and 2 extra MP\n{Icon Arrow} Can target other fighters\n{Icon Arrow} Dies at end of turn", "Lets the Rogue strengthen that valuable tool, the Boombot. In addition to gaining AP and MP, it can target fighters other than the Rogue's own bombs, but it dies at the end of its turn."], "b:Rogue:Explobomb": ["", "{Icon Bomb} explode when destroyed", "Bombs explode when they die. Talk about going out with a bang!"], "b:Rogue:Pyrotechnist": ["", "{Icon Bomb} gain 2 levels when summoned\n\n{Icon Bomb} no longer evolve\n\n1 {Icon Bomb} max per element per turn", "Bombs evolve faster, but the Rogue can only place one of each element per turn."], "b:Rogue:Fugitive": ["", "At start of turn:\n{Icon Arrow} Switches places with the nearest {Icon Bomb} (4 cells max)\n{Icon Arrow} {Caster} {Element Physical} Healing: 10% of HP max of the caster {Fixed: The value is not influenced by the caster's damage.}", "At the start of their turn, the Rogue switches places with their closest bomb, up to 4 cells away, then stabilizes it."], "b:Rogue:Blade Master": ["", "Dagger Return damage is doubled\n\nThe Rogue has Powder Powder less", "Dagger Return damage is doubled, but the Rogue has less Powder to summon bombs."], "b:Rogue:Elemental Bombs": ["", "On an explosion:\n{Icon Arrow} {Element Fire} Incurable (+1 per level of the bomb)\n{Icon Arrow} {Element Earth} -2 MP \n{Icon Arrow} {Element Air} -1 Range (1 turn, max 3)\n\nBombs' max level is 6", "The Rogue's bombs have additional effects. However, the bombs' maximum level is reduced."], "b:Rogue:Reinforced Tunic": ["", "Immune to damage from allied {Icon Bomb}\nAt end of turn, per adjacent {Icon Bomb}:\n{Icon Arrow} {Caster} 30 Elemental Resistance (1 turn)\n{Icon Arrow} {Icon Bomb} -30 Elemental Resistance (1 turn)", "At the end of their turn, the Rogue uses bombs adjacent to them as a shield by absorbing their resistance."], "b:Rogue:Bomber Fan": ["", "When a {Icon Bomb} explodes:\n{Icon Arrow} {Caster} 1 AP (1 turn)\n\nAll {Icon Bomb} have 1 HP", "The Rogue gains 1 AP when a bomb explodes, but their bombs only have a single health point."], "b:Rogue:Surprise Shot": ["", "On switching modes:\n{Icon Arrow} {Caster} Surprise Shot (Lvl. 3-91)\n{Icon Arrow} Once per turn\n\nRuse has 0 Range", "The Rogue will inflict additional damage on their next elemental spell atter changing modes. In exchange, Ruse can no longer be used to switch places with another fighter."], "b:Rogue:Great Escape": ["", "When using Ruse on themself:\n{Icon Arrow} Switches places with the farthest {Icon Bomb} (6 cells max)\n{Icon Arrow} Triggers the {Icon Bomb}", "If the Rogue uses Ruse to change modes, they switch places with the farthest bomb, within a radius of 6 cells, and then detonate it."], "b:Rogue:Rogue Master": ["", "At start of turn:\n{Icon Arrow} Rogue Master (+1 Lvl.)\n\nRuse has a 2 turn cooldown", "At start of turn, the Rogue accumulates the \"Rogue Master\" state up to a maximum level of 5. Upon switching from Sneaky to Runaway, or from Runaway to Sneaky, the Rogue Will gain additional bonuses depending on the mode. In exchange, the Ruse spell has a 2 turn cooldown."], "b:Rogue:Powder Keg": ["", "The Rogue has 2 Powder more\n\nDagger Return become single-target", "The Rogue's Powder reserves are larger, but Dagger Returns no longer inflict damage in an area of effect."], "b:Rogue:Rusty Blade": ["", "In Escapist mode:\n{Icon Arrow} Elemental spells generate Rusty Blade\n{Icon Arrow} The range of elemental spells is fixed\n\nIn Sneaky mode:\n{Icon Arrow} Elemental spells consume Rusty Blade\n{Icon Arrow} The Rusty Blade apply Tetanus", "The Rogue's elemental spells in Runaway mode have fixed range, but generate Rusty Blades. These Rusty Blades are consumed in Sneaky mode to apply a stackable poison on a target."], "b:Rogue:Minesweeper": ["", "When using Ruse on a {Icon Bomb}:\n{Icon Arrow} The spell doesn't cost any {AP} AP\n{Icon Arrow} The {Icon Bomb} does not level up", "When the Rogue uses the Ruse spell to switch places with one of their bombs, the bomb doesn't level up, but the spell doesn't cost any AP."], "b:Rogue:Powder Wall": ["", "If 2 bombs are aligned:\n{Icon Arrow} A Powder Wall is created\n\nFighters that start their turn on the Powder Wall suffer damage\n\nWhen a Powder Wall is activated, the {Icon Bomb} that form a Powder Wall:\n{Icon Arrow} Lose 1 level\n{Icon Arrow} Explode below level 1", "The Rogue can create Powder Walls by placing bombs in a line spaced less than 5 cells apart. The Powder Wall inflicts damage on all fighters who start their turn inside it."], "b:Rogue:Kaboom": ["", "Dynamite can be cast on a fighter\n\nPer level of Dynamite:\n{Ally}: {Damage Inflicted} 6% damage inflicted (1 turn)\n{Enemy}: 8% damage suffered from explosions (1 turn)\n\nThe Dynamite state is limited to level 5", "The Rogue can cast Dynamite on other fighters. Casting it on an ally grants a damage bonus to the ally. Casting it on an enemy makes the enemy"], "b:Rogue:Jackpot": ["", "Once per turn, if Sneaky:\n{Icon Arrow} Switches places with the first {Icon Bomb} placed\n{Icon Arrow} Switches places again at end of turn", "The Rogue switches places with the first bomb placed in their turn while in Sneaky mode, then switches places with it again at the end of the turn if the bomb is still on the field."], "b:Rogue:Tactician": ["", "When moving a bomb:\n{Icon Arrow} {Caster} Regains 1 AP\n{Icon Arrow} The {Icon Bomb} loses a level\n{Icon Arrow} 6 max per turn", "The Rogue regains AP by moving their bombs, but the bombs lose 1 level after being moved. The Rogue can regain up to 6 AP per turn."], "b:Rogue:Time Bombs": ["", "In Sneaky, the Rogue places a glyph instead of {Icon Bomb}:\n{Icon Arrow} The {Icon Bomb} spawns instead of the glyph at start of next turn if the cell is free\n{Icon Arrow} The {Icon Bomb} gains 2 levels", "Instead of directly placing bombs, the Rogue places glyphs. At the start of the next turn, these glyphs turn into bombs if the cell is still free. The bombs summoned in this way level up directly."], "b:Sadida:Sadida's Tear": ["{AP} 3", "{Enemy} {Element Water} Damage: 3-98\n{Ally} {Element Water} Healing: 6-53\n{Icon Voodoll} {Elemental Resistance} 100 Elemental Resistance (1 turn)\n\nOn Sadida Seed:\n{Icon Arrow} Summons The Inflatable", "This spell can deal damage to an enemy or heal an ally without line of sight. It can also be used to make a doll more resistant. If the spell is cast on a seed, the Sadida summons an Inflatable that can increase allies' damage.", "Water"], "b:Sadida:Vaporize": ["{AP} 2", "{Enemy} {Element Water} Damage: 2-65\n{Icon Voodoll} or Tree Transparent (Lvl 1)\n{Icon Voodoll} At end of turn: Nettled (+1 Lvl.)\n\nOn Sadida Seed:\n{Icon Arrow} Summons The Greedy", "This spell makes a summons transparent (no longer blocks line of sight). If the target is one of the Sadida's Dolls, the Doll gains an additional level of Nettled at the end of its turn. If the spell is cast on a seed, the Sadida summons a Greedy with a permanent damage bonus.", "Water"], "b:Sadida:Mudoll": ["{AP} 3", "{Enemy} {MP} -1 MP\n{Enemy} {Element Water} Damage: 3-83\n{Ally} {Element Water} Healing: 6-50\n\nOn Sadida Seed:\n{Icon Arrow} Summons The Block\n{Icon Arrow} {Icon Voodoll} Muddy (Lvl 1)", "This spell either heals an ally or removes an MP from an enemy while inflicting damage on them. If the spell is cast on a seed, the Sadida summons a Block that removes MP around it at end of turn.", "Water"], "b:Sadida:Rust": ["{AP} 4", "{Enemy} {Element Water} Damage: 4-102\n{Ally} {Element Water} Healing: 8-57 {Area Cross}", "The Sadida heals allies and deals damage to enemies in the area of effect.", "Water"], "b:Sadida:Drain": ["{AP} 5\n{WP} 1", "{Element Water} Damage: 6-182\n{Ally} {Element Water} Healing: 12-100 {Area Squarering}", "The Sadida drains some Health Points from a target and redistributes them to nearby allies.", "Water"], "b:Sadida:Bramble": ["{AP} 3", "{Enemy} {Element Earth} Damage: 3-91\n{Ally} {Armor} 3-1,438 Armor\n\nOn Sadida Seed:\n{Icon Arrow} Summons The Sacrificial Doll\n{Icon Arrow} {Icon Voodoll} Prickly (Lvl 1)", "Inflicts Earth damage on an enemy or gives Armor to an ally. The Armor absorbs damage received. If the spell is cast on a seed, the Sadida summons a Sacrificial Doll that becomes more dangerous whenever the Sadida takes damage from an enemy.", "Earth"], "b:Sadida:Compost": ["{AP} 4", "{Enemy} {Element Earth} Damage: 4-131 and steals 1 MP\n{Ally} {Armor} 3-2,398 Armor\n{Ally} {MP} 1 MP (3 if {Icon Voodoll})\n\nOn Sadida Seed:\n{Icon Arrow} Summons The Inflatable\n{Icon Arrow} {Icon Voodoll} Compost (Lvl 1)", "This spell steals I MP from an enemy and inflicts Earth damage on them, or applies a large amount of Armor to an ally. The Armor absorbs hits received. If the spell is cast on a seed, the Sadida summons an Inflatable that can increase allies' mobility.", "Earth"], "b:Sadida:Wild Grass": ["{AP} 2", "{MP} -234 MP \n{Element Earth} Damage: 2-60\nCast on {Icon Voodoll}:\n{Icon Arrow} Effects become {Area Cross} (1)\n{Icon Arrow} The {Caster}'s summons are not affected\n\nOn Sadida Seed:\n{Icon Arrow} Summons The Sacrificial Doll\n{Icon Arrow} {Icon Voodoll} Roots (Lvl 1)", "This spell reduces a target's movement. If it's cast on a seed, the Sadida summons a Sacrificial Doll that removes MP from enemies when it explodes.", "Earth"], "b:Sadida:Earthquake": ["{AP} 3", "{Enemy} {Element Earth} damage: 2-60 {Area Circle} (3)\nPer level of Nettled:\n{Icon Arrow} {Enemy} Extra {Element Earth} damage: 1-30 {Area Circle} (1)\n\nMust target a {Icon Voodoll} or a Tree", "The Sadida deals damage in an area of effect around one of their summons. This spell can be cast anywhere on the battlefield, but it must target a doll or a tree.", "Earth"], "b:Sadida:Manifold Bramble": ["{AP} 5\n{WP} 1", "{MP} -2 MP {Area Circle}\n{Element Earth} Damage: 6-167", "Inflicts Earth damage and removes MP in a large area of effect.", "Earth"], "b:Sadida:Gust": ["{AP} 2", "{Enemy} {Element Air} Damage: 2-51\n{Ally} {Damage Inflicted} 20% damage inflicted\nPushes back 1 cell {Area Circlering}\n\nOn Sadida Seed:\n{Icon Arrow} Summons The Madoll\n{Icon Arrow} {Icon Voodoll} Windy (Lvl 1)", "This spell repels any other fighters around the target. If the target is an ally, they gain a damage bonus for one turn. It the spell is cast on a seed, the Sadida summons a Madoll that will apply its effects in an area of effect.", "Air"], "b:Sadida:Poisoned Wind": ["{AP} 2\n{WP} 2", "Intoxicated (Lvl 1-30) (2 turns) {Area Circle}\n{Damage Inflicted} -20% damage inflicted\nFor each AP or MP loss by an {Enemy}:\n{Icon Arrow} {Element Air} Damage: 1-30", "The Sadida summons a powerful poisoned wind that affects all targets in an area around the target cell for 2 turns. Targets hit by the poison have their damage reduced and suffer damage for every MP or AP lost.", "Air"], "b:Sadida:Sudden Chill": ["{AP} 4", "Sudden Chill (+50 Lvl.):\n{Icon Arrow} -50 Elemental Resistance\n{Element Air} Damage: 4-111\n\nOn Sadida Seed:\n{Icon Arrow} Summons The Greedy\n{Icon Arrow} {Icon Voodoll} Cooled (Lvl 1)", "This spell cools down the target, reducing its resistances as well as dealing damage to it. If the spell is cast on a seed, the Sadida summons a Greedy that can lower its targets' resistances.", "Air"], "b:Sadida:K'mir": ["{AP} 3", "Attracts by 2 cells\nK'mir (Lvl 1)\n{Enemy} {Element Air} Damage: 3-91\n\nOn Sadida Seed:\n{Icon Arrow} Summons The Block\n{Icon Arrow} {Icon Voodoll} Punchy (Lvl 1)", "K'mir enables the Sadida to exert a pull on a target for one turn. If the spell is cast on a seed, the Sadida summons a Block that can pull targets during its turn.", "Air"], "b:Sadida:Woodland Stench": ["{AP} 3", "{Element Air} Damage: 3-91\n{Enemy} Cursed (+2-76 Lvl.) (2 turns)\n\nOn Sadida Seed:\n{Icon Arrow} Summons The Madoll\n{Icon Arrow} {Icon Voodoll} Nauseating (Lvl 1)", "This spell allows the Sadida to curse an enemy: the enemy will take damage every time the Sadida inflicts poisons. If the spell is cast on a seed, the Sadida summons a Madoll that can poison targets.", "Air"], "b:Sadida:Tree": ["{WP} 1", "Transforms the Sadida into Tree\nHeals: 20% of max HP\nMisses a turn", "The Sadida transforms into a tree for one turn. The Sadida can no longer move, but can heal and resistances are increased.", "Neutral"], "b:Sadida:Dolly Sacrifice": ["{AP} 2", "{Caster} Sacrifices all their {Icon Voodoll}\nPer level of Nettled of sacrificed {Icon Voodoll}:\n{Icon Arrow} {Caster} 1 map AP (1 turn)\n{Icon Arrow} {Caster} Healing: 5% max HP", "The Sadida sacrifices all their dolls. They are healed and gain AP based on the sacrificed dolls' level of Nettled.", "Neutral"], "b:Sadida:Sylvan Awakening": ["{AP} 2\n{WP} 1", "Gives 15% of the Sadida's max HP as Armor\n{Icon Arrow} Awake (1 turn)\n\nOn a KO'd target:\n{Icon Arrow} The target comes back to life (25% of max HP)\n{Icon Arrow} In Recovery (Lvl 1)", "The Sadida transmits the very essence of the forest to a team member, awakening their senses to the beauty of nature. This process is long and dangerous, but it can restore life to an ally who's fallen in combat.", "Neutral"], "b:Sadida:Fertilizer": ["{AP} 1\n{WP} 1", "{Icon Voodoll} Skips turn\n{Icon Voodoll} Nettled (+3 Lvl.) at end of turn\n{Icon Voodoll} Stabilized\n{Ally} 30% extra Heals received from {Icon Voodoll}\n{Enemy} 30% extra Damage received from {Icon Voodoll}", "The Sadida nettles a Doll to quickly make it more powerful. However, the Doll is stabilized and skips a turn. On an enemy, the Sadida's dolls will deal more damage to that enemy for 1 turn. On an ally, the Sadida's dolls will heal that ally more for 1 turn.", "Neutral"], "b:Sadida:Force of Nature": ["{AP} 2\n{WP} 1", "{Caster} Must have Armor\n{Caster} Force of Nature (Lvl 1):\n{MP} 2 MP\n{Range} 2 Range\n{Damage Inflicted} 30% damage inflicted (Transferred to {Icon Voodoll})\n{Heart percent} 30% heals performed (Transferred to {Icon Voodoll})\nCancels Armor gains\n\nState is lost if the {Caster} loses their Armor", "The Sadida can only cast this spell if they have Armor. They gain MP, range, damage inflicted, and healing provided, but can no longer gain Armor. The state is lost if the Sadida loses their starting Armor.", "Neutral"], "b:Sadida:Toxines": ["{AP} 3\n{WP} 1", "{Enemy} Toxines (+4-121 Lvl.) (2 turns)\n{Enemy} {Elemental Resistance} -50 Elemental Resistance (2 turns)\n{Ally} Harmless Toxin (Lvl 8-66) (2 turns)", "The Sadida applies toxins to the target for 2 turns. If the target is an enemy, they lose elemental resistance and take damage at start of turn. If the target is an ally, they gain elemental resistance and are healed at start of turn.", "Neutral"], "b:Sadida:Sadida Prayer": ["", "If a fighter ends their turn near a Sadida Tree:\n{Icon Arrow} {Element Light} Healing: 5", "The Sadida's Trees heal fighters who finish their turn on an adjacent cell."], "b:Sadida:Accelerated Growth": ["", "At end of turn, {Icon Voodoll} gain 1 additional level of Nettled\n\nNettling:\n{Icon Arrow} Consumes all levels of Nettled", "Dolls gain Nettled more quickly. However, they lose all their levels of Nettled if they are transformed into seeds with the Nettling spell."], "b:Sadida:Explodoll": ["", "When a {Icon Voodoll} dies, for each level of Nettled:\n{Icon Arrow} {Enemy} {Element Light} Damage: 1-27 {Area Circle} (2)\n{Icon Arrow} {Ally} {Element Light} Healing: 2-15 {Area Circle} (2)\n\n{Icon Voodoll} have 30% less HP", "The Sadida's Dolls explode when they die, inflicting damage on enemies and healing allies in a 2-cell circle. However, the Dolls have less max HP."], "b:Sadida:Sylvan Gift": ["", "When removing a Sadida Tree:\n{Icon Arrow} Sends remaining HP to surrounding fighters\n\nSadida Tree have 50% less HP", "When the Sadida removes one of their Trees, the Tree's remaining HP are sent to nearby fighters. However, the Trees have less max HP."], "b:Sadida:Bad Seed": ["", "If the fighter wals on a Seed:\n{Icon Arrow} {Enemy} -1 MP per level of Nettled\n{Icon Arrow} the Seed disappears", "Seeds disappear if a fighter walks on them. If the fighter is an enemy, the enemy loses MP based on the seed's level of Nettled."], "b:Sadida:Dollish Devotion": ["", "When using the Seed spell on a {Icon Voodoll}:\n{Icon Arrow} Kills the {Icon Voodoll}\n{Icon Arrow} Does not summon a Sadida Seed\n{Icon Arrow} {Caster} 1 WP per level of Nettled on the {Icon Voodoll}", "The Sadida regains WP by sacrificing their dolls with the Seed spell, but the dolls are no longer transformed into seeds."], "b:Sadida:Lone Sadida": ["", "The {Icon Voodoll} Nettling no longer costs AP\n\nThe {Icon Voodoll} spell Nettling no longer restores WP to {Caster}", "The Nettling spell, which allows Dolls to transform into a seed, no longer costs AP. However, the Sadida no longer regains WP when a Doll uses this spell."], "b:Sadida:Fertile Soil": ["", "At end of turn, {Icon Voodoll} and Sadida Seed gain 1 additional level of Nettled if they are near a Tree\n\nOtherwise, they do not gain Nettled", "Dolls and Seeds gain 1 additional level of Nettled if they are near one of the Sadida's Trees; otherwise, they do not gain any Nettled."], "b:Sadida:Doll Link": ["", "{Icon Voodoll} gain 100 Elemental Resistance\n30% of damage suffered by {Icon Voodoll} is replicated on the {Caster} Sadida", "The Sadida's Dolls gain resistance. However, they pass on some of the damage they suffer to the Sadida."], "b:Sadida:Knowledge of Dolls": ["", "Seed:\n{Icon Arrow} Range is reduced to 1, non-modifiable\n\n{Icon Voodoll} gain 2 Range on their spells", "The Sadida's Seed spell can only be cast on an adjacent cell, but all of their Dolls have more range on their spells."], "b:Sadida:Sylvan Cycle": ["", "When summoning a Sadida Tree\n{Icon Arrow} Nettled Tree (+3 Lvl.)\n\nTrees die at start of next turn", "Trees summoned by the Sadida gain additional Nettled, but die at the end of the Sadida's next turn."], "b:Sadida:Venomous": ["", "For each MP removal applied:\n{Icon Arrow} Cancels the loss of MP\n{Icon Arrow} Toxines (+2 Lvl.)", "The Sadida cancels all MP reductions that they apply, but replaces them with Toxines. Toxines is a poison that inflicts damage at the start of the target's turn and can be maintained every turn."], "b:Sadida:Common Ground": ["", "Around Sadida Tree:\n{Icon Arrow} 50 Elemental Resistance\n\nArea of influence of Sadida Tree becomes a 1-cell cross", "The Sadida's Trees protect adjacent fighters by giving them a resistance bonus. However, their area of influence is reduced."], "b:Sadida:Great Chain of Being": ["", "{Caster} {Force of Will} 20 Force of Will\nFor each MP removal applied:\n{Icon Arrow} {Caster} loses 1 MP (fixed)", "The Sadida gains Force of Will but also loses an MP each time they apply an MP reduction."], "b:Sadida:Sylvan Shoot": ["", "Disables Trees' natural WP regeneration\nThe Seed spell changes how it works\nOn a free cell:\n{Icon Arrow} Instantly summons a Sadida Tree\n\nOn a Sadida Seed:\n{Icon Arrow} Removes the Sadida Seed\n\nAt end of the Sadida's turn, around Trees:\n{Icon Arrow} Sadida Seed are summoned", "The Sadida instantly summons Trees with the Seed spell. At end of turn, the Sadida summons seeds adjacent to their Trees. However, the Trees no longer restore the Sadida's WP. The Sadida can remove the seeds from the battlefield by using the Seed spell."], "b:Sadida:Plant Communication": ["", "At end of turn, the Sadida {Caster} sends their remaining MP to their {Icon Voodoll}\n\nIf the Sadida has no MP left at the end of their turn, the {Icon Voodoll} lose all their MP", "The Sadida sends their remaining MP to their dolls at the end of the Sadida's turn. However, if the Sadida has no MP left at the end of their turn, their dolls lose all their MP."], "b:Sadida:Green Guard": ["", "Sadida Tree:\n{Icon Arrow} Plant Blessing becomes Green Guard\n{Icon Arrow} The bonuses become bonuses to Armor received and Heals received\n{Icon Arrow} The base bonus increases from 20% to 40%", "The Sadida's Trees give bonuses on Armor Received and Heals Received to nearby fighters to help keep them better protected."], "b:Sadida:Voodoll Blessing": ["", "The Voodoll:\n{Icon Arrow} Can no longer be linked to an {Enemy}\n{Icon Arrow} Gains 3 max MP\n{Icon Arrow} Gains 2 Range on its Totemic Ritual spell.", "The Voodoll can no longer be linked to an enemy, but it gains mobility and range to support the Sadida's other dolls."], "b:Sadida:Infected Soil": ["", "Sadida Tree apply poison:\n{Icon Arrow} {Enemy} Toxines (+3 Lvl. per level of Nettled)\n\nEach Sadida Tree can only be summoned adjacent to a fighter {Target}", "The Sadida's Trees apply Toxines to enemies in their area of influence. The Sadida can only summon their Trees adjacent to a fighter."], "b:Sadida:Wild Whispers": ["", "Can summon 2 The Voodoll\n\nThe Voodoll is stabilized", "The Sadida can summon 2 Voodolls, but they are stabilized."]});